  </acknowledgments*>

  <subsection|<with|color|black|Preliminaries and
  notation>><label|sec:notations>

  In this section we shall introduce the main notations we are going to use
  throughout the paper.

  \;

  We let <math|\<bbb-R\><rsub|0>\<assign\>\<bbb-R\>>,
  <math|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<assign\>\<varepsilon\>\<bbb-Z\>>,
  <math|<with|color|black|\<bbb-T\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>\<assign\><around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<bbb-Z\>|)>/<around*|(|M\<bbb-Z\>|)>>>
  and define the corresponding spacetime domains

  <\with|color|black>
    <\equation*>
      \<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<assign\>\<bbb-R\>\<times\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>,<space|2em>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>\<assign\>\<bbb-R\>\<times\>\<bbb-T\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><rsup|d>,<space|2em>d=3,<space|1em>\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,<space|1em>M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>.
    </equation*>

    The assumption that <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>
    ensures that <math|M\<bbb-Z\>\<subset\>\<varepsilon\>\<bbb-Z\>> for every
    <math|M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>. These domains are continuous in the time
    direction and discrete in the <math|d> spatial dimensions. For a
    measurable function <math|f:\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>>,
    we write

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>>\<assign\><around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    Given a nonnegative weight <math|w\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>|)>>
    we denote by <math|C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,w|)>> the
    space of continuous functions <math|f:\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>>
    such that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|w|)>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|z\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|\||w<around*|(|z|)>f<around*|(|z|)>|\|>\<less\>\<infty\>.
    </equation*>

    We always identify functions <math|f:\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>>
    with their spatially periodic extensions
    <math|f:\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>>. In
    particular, we write <math|C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>,w|)>>
    for the subspace of <math|C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,w|)>>
    consisting of functions that are periodic in space with period <math|M>.
    We denote by <math|\<cal-S\><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>
    the space of smooth rapidly decreasing functions over
    <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>. The Fourier transform of
    <math|f\<in\>\<cal-S\><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>> is
    defined as
  </with>

  <\equation*>
    <wide|f|^><around*|(|\<omega\>,k|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>e<rsup|-i<around*|(|\<omega\>*t+
    k\<cdot\>x|)>>*f<around*|(|t,x|)>*\<mathd\>t
    \<mathd\>x,<space|2em><around*|(|\<omega\>,k|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|\<ast\>>\<assign\>\<bbb-R\>\<times\><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>|)><rsup|\<ast\>>,
  </equation*>

  where

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>|)><rsup|\<ast\>>\<assign\><around*|(|-\<pi\>/\<varepsilon\>,\<pi\>/\<varepsilon\>|]><rsup|d>
  </equation*>

  is the dual of the group <math|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>>. The
  integral over <math|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>> is understood
  with respect the counting measure (still written by <math|\<mathd\>x>) with
  normalisation\ 

  <\equation*>
    <big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>><space|0.2spc>f<around*|(|x|)>*\<mathd\>x\<assign\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|d><big|sum><rsub|x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>f<around*|(|x|)>,
  </equation*>

  which ensures weak convergence to the Lebesgue measure as
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<rightarrow\>0>. As usual, the Fourier transform
  extends to <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>
  by duality. The inverse Fourier transform is given by

  <\equation*>
    f<around*|(|t,x|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
    <wide|f|^><around*|(|\<omega\>,k|)>*e<rsup|i<around*|(|\<omega\>t+
    k\<cdot\>x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>\<omega\>*\<mathd\>k|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>,<space|2em><around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>.
  </equation*>

  For <math|\<varepsilon\>\<geqslant\>0>, we define the Laplacian
  <math|\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> as the Fourier multiplier on
  <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>
  <math|>with symbol

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>|)><rsup|\<ast\>>\<ni\>k\<mapsto\>-q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|2><around*|(|k|)>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>,
  </equation*>

  \ where

  <\equation>
    q<rsub|0><around*|(|k|)>=<around*|\||k|\|>,<space|2em>q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k|)>\<assign\><around*|[|<big|sum><rsub|i=1><rsup|d><around*|(|<frac|1|\<varepsilon\>>*sin<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>*
    k<rsub|i>|)>|)><rsup|2>|]><rsup|1/2>,<space|2em>\<varepsilon\>\<gtr\>0.<label|eq:discrete-symbol>
  </equation>

  Note that for <math|\<varepsilon\>\<gtr\>0>, the operator
  <math|\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> coincides with the standard
  nearest-neighbour discrete Laplacian.

  <paragraph*|The fractional Laplacian.>For <math|s\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>
  the fractional Laplacian <math|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>>
  is defined as the Fourier multiplier with symbol
  <math|<around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>|)><rsup|\<ast\>>\<ni\>k\<mapsto\>q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|2s><around*|(|k|)>>.
  In particular it is self-adjoint and positive in
  <math|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>> and
  for <math|s\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> it has the (discrete, when
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<gtr\>0>) heat\Ukernel
  representation<nbsp><cite|kwasnickiTenEquivalentDefinitions2017>

  <\equation>
    <around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>f=C<rsub|s>*<big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>><around*|(|f-e<rsup|\<theta\>\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>f|)>*\<theta\><rsup|-1-s>\<mathd\>\<theta\>,<label|eq:fractional-laplacian-heat-kernel>
  </equation>

  with the constant <math|C<rsub|s>=<around*|\||\<Gamma\><around*|(|-s|)>|\|><rsup|-1>>.
  In the continuum, the fractional Laplacian has, for
  <math|s\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>, the integral
  representation<nbsp><cite|kwasnickiTenEquivalentDefinitions2017>:

  <\equation>
    <around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|0>|)><rsup|s>
    f<around*|(|x|)>=C<rsub|d,s>*<text|PV><big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>><frac|f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|y|)>|<around*|\||x-y|\|><rsup|d+2s>>\<mathd\>y,<space|2em>x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>,<label|eq:integral-repr-frac-lapl-cont>
  </equation>

  where <math|C<rsub|d,s>> is an universal constant. In the discrete setting
  a similar formula holds<nbsp><cite|ciaurriFractionalDiscreteLaplacian2015>:

  <\equation>
    <around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s> f<around*|(|x|)>=
    \<varepsilon\><rsup|d>*<big|sum><rsub|y\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d><mid|\|>y\<neq\>x>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x-y|)>*<around*|(|f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|y|)>|)>,<space|2em>x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>,<label|eq:integral-rep-frac-lap-discrete>
  </equation>

  where the kernel <math|H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s>:\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>>
  is positive and such that <math|H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|0|)>=0>,
  <math|H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x|)>=H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|-x|)>>
  and

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\||H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x|)>|\|>\<leqslant\>C<rsub|d,s><rprime|'>*<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|-d-2s>,<space|2em>x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>,
  </equation*>

  uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<gtr\>0> for some constant
  <math|C<rsub|d,s><rprime|'>\<gtr\>0>. <with|color|black|Note that in our
  notation<nbsp><eqref|eq:integral-rep-frac-lap-discrete> can be equivalently
  written as>

  <\equation*>
    <with|color|black|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>
    f<around*|(|x|)>= <big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x-y|)>*<around*|(|f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|y|)>|)>
    \<mathd\>y.>
  </equation*>

  For <math|\<varepsilon\>\<gtr\>0>, we can encode the
  representation<nbsp><eqref|eq:integral-rep-frac-lap-discrete> of the
  fractional Laplacian, via a positive measure
  <math|\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s>> on
  <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
  for which

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\<langle\>|f,<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>g|\<rangle\>>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>f<around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|g<around*|(|z|)>-g<around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|)>
    \<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>.
  </equation*>

  We also define the kernel <math|\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>
  arising from the disintegration of <math|\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s>>
  with respect to the measure <math|\<mathd\>z> on
  <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>. Specifically, we have

  <\equation>
    \<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>=\<delta\><around*|(|t-u|)>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x-y|)>
    \<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>,<space|2em>\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>=\<delta\><around*|(|t-u|)>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x-y|)>
    \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>,<label|eq:int-kernel>
  </equation>

  where <math|z=<around*|(|t,x|)>> and <math|z<rprime|'>=<around*|(|u,y|)>.>
  The kernel <math|\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s>> is
  symmetric, that is,

  <\equation*>
    \<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
    \<mathd\>z=\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,\<mathd\>z|)>
    \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>.
  </equation*>

  <with|color|black|>With this notation in place, the following Leibniz-type
  formula with remainder holds:

  <\equation>
    I<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|f,g|)>\<assign\><around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s><around*|(|f
    g|)>-f*<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>
    g-g*<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>f=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|(|f<around*|(|\<bullet\>|)>-f<around*|(|z|)>|)>*<around*|(|g<around*|(|\<bullet\>|)>-g<around*|(|z|)>|)>*\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|<rsup|>s><around*|(|\<bullet\>,\<mathd\>z|)>.<label|def-I>
  </equation>

  Let us also introduce the fractional difference operator

  <\equation>
    <with|color|black|\<frak-D\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|f|)><around*|(|z|)>>\<assign\>I<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|f,f|)><rsup|1/2><around*|(|z|)>=<around*|[|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|[|f<around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-f<around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>|]><rsup|1/2>,<label|eq:D>
  </equation>

  which behaves like a derivative of order <math|s>. In particular using
  that, for all <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0>, one has the estimates

  <\equation*>
    <big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>><around*|[|f<around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-f<around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<delta\><rsup|2-2s>,<space|1em><big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)><rsup|c>><around*|[|f<around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-f<around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<delta\><rsup|-2s>,
  </equation*>

  <\with|color|black>
    where

    <\equation*>
      B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>\<assign\><around*|<left|{|2>|z<rprime|'>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><mid|\|>
      <around*|\||z-z<rprime|'>|\|><rsub|s>\<leqslant\>\<delta\>|<right|}|2>>
    </equation*>

    denotes the ball of radius <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0>. The discrete
    gradient is defined as

    <\equation*>
      \<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f=<around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|1+>,\<partial\><rsup|1->,\<ldots\>,\<partial\><rsup|d+>,\<partial\><rsup|d->|)>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|\<partial\><rsup|i\<pm\>>> stands for the discrete
    forward/backward derivative on the lattice
    <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> and
    <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f|\<\|\|\>>> is the
    supremum norm. Choosing <math|\<delta\>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>>/<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f|\<\|\|\>>>
    yields
  </with>

  <\equation>
    <with|color|black|\<frak-D\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|f|)><around*|(|z|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f|\<\|\|\>>\<delta\><rsup|1-s>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>>\<delta\><rsup|-s>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f|\<\|\|\>><rsup|s>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1-s>.<label|eq:D-est>
  </equation>

  <\remark>
    Although the kernel representation of the fractional Laplacian fails in
    the continuum case <math|\<varepsilon\>=0> (due to the presence of the
    principal value), the above considerations and the results presented
    below extend to the continuum with only minor modifications in the
    proofs, or simply by taking the <math|\<varepsilon\>\<rightarrow\>0>
    limit in the relevant inequalities. We emphasise, however, that the main
    results of the paper do not rely on these continuum extensions. In
    particular, the limit <math|\<varepsilon\>\<rightarrow\>0> in
    Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:main> is obtained via tightness, using the a
    priori estimates established uniformly for
    <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>.
  </remark>

  <\remark>
    A basic observation is that the fractional Laplacian (whether in the
    continuum or on the lattice) satisfies an inequality under the action of
    convex functions. Let <math|s\<in\><around*|(|0,1|]>,>
    <math|\<Phi\>:\<bbb-R\>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>> be a convex function and
    <math|\<Phi\><rprime|'>> one of its sub-differentials, then, for any
    <math|\<varepsilon\>\<geqslant\>0> and
    <math|u\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>\<Phi\><around*|(|u|)>\<leqslant\>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|u|)>*<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>u.
    </equation*>

    Indeed, let <math|\<Phi\>:\<bbb-R\>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>> be a convex
    function, then

    <\equation*>
      \<Phi\><around*|(|a|)>-\<Phi\><around*|(|b|)>\<leqslant\>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|a|)>*<around*|(|a-b|)>,<space|2em>a,b\<in\>\<bbb-R\>,
    </equation*>

    so if <math|u:\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>> is
    a continuous and bounded function, we have

    <\equation*>
      \<Phi\><around*|(|u|)>-e<rsup|\<theta\>\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><around*|(|u|)>\<leqslant\>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|u|)>*<around*|(|u-e<rsup|\<theta\>\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>u|)>,
    </equation*>

    since <math|e<rsup|\<theta\>\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>> has a
    positive definite probability kernel. The claimed inequality follows now
    from<nbsp><eqref|eq:fractional-laplacian-heat-kernel>
    <with|color|black|in the case <math|s\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>. The case
    <math|s=1> is elementary. For <math|s\<gtr\>1> the result is not true.>
    It is clear that the same proof works for <math|\<varepsilon\>=0>
    <with|color|black|with some additional regularity assumption>. We will
    incorporate this idea in the proof of the key
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:est-apriori-laplacian>, below.
  </remark>

  The operator <math|G=G<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>>=\<cal-L\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
  is defined as

  <\equation>
    <around*|(|\<cal-L\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>f|)><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|-\<infty\>><rsup|t>e<rsup|-<around*|(|m<rsup|2>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>|)>*<around*|(|t-u|)>>*f<around*|(|u,\<bullet\>|)>\<mathd\>u,<space|2em>t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>,<label|eq:ell-minus-one>
  </equation>

  and will be applied to continuous function on
  <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> with at most a limited polynomial
  growth in spacetime. Indeed, on account of Lemma<nbsp>5.4
  of<nbsp><cite|Grigoryan-heat-kernel-metric-meas-sp> together with the
  argument of Sec.<nbsp>1 of<nbsp><cite|Grigoryan-Telcs-Sub-Gaussian-estimates>,
  the kernel <math|G<rsup|><around*|(|t,x|)>> of <math|G> satisfies

  <\equation>
    G<around*|(|t,x|)>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<with|font|Bbb|\<bbb-1\>><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
    e<rsup|-m<rsup|2>t>*min<around*|{|t<rsup|-<frac|d|2s>>,<frac|t|<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|d+2s>>|}>\<lesssim\><frac|<with|color|black|<with|font|Bbb|\<bbb-1\>><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
    t*e<rsup|- c \ m<rsup|2>t>|<around*|(|<around*|\||t|\|><rsup|1/2s>+<around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|d+2s>><label|eq:est-kernel-G>,
  </equation>

  uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<geqslant\>0>. Here
  <math|<with|color|black|<with|font|Bbb|\<bbb-1\>><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>=0>
  if <math|t\<less\>0> and <math|1> if <math|t\<geqslant\>0>. If <math|s=1>,
  then the above estimate is not optimal and the following bound

  <\equation>
    G<around*|(|t,x|)>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<with|font|Bbb|\<bbb-1\>><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
    t<rsup|-d/2> e<rsup|-m<rsup|2>t-c <around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>/t><label|eq:est-kernel-G-s-1>
  </equation>

  holds true uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<geqslant\>0>.

  <\with|color|black>
    <paragraph*|Parameters.>During the subsequent analysis, we shall
    introduce several parameters

    <\equation>
      \<alpha\>,\<beta\>,\<gamma\>,\<delta\>,\<theta\>,\<vartheta\>,\<varrho\>,\<nu\>,\<kappa\>,<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>,\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>,<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>,<wide|k|\<bar\>>,a,\<flat\>.<label|eq:parameters>
    </equation>

    Although their precise values are not specified at this stage, all these
    parameters are to be regarded as fixed once and for all. Their choice
    depends solely on the power <math|s\<in\><around*|(|3/4,1|)>> of the
    fractional Laplacian. Since the specific constraints determining these
    values will emerge later in the analysis, we postpone their detailed
    specification to Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:bounds-on-parameters>
    and<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing> below.<with|font-series|bold|>
  </with>

  <paragraph*|Space-time weights.>

  <\definition>
    <label|def:distance>We define the fractional parabolic distance by

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||z|\|><rsub|s>\<assign\><around*|\||z<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>+<around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsup|><rsup|>,<space|2em>z=<around*|(|z<rsub|0>,<wide|z|\<bar\>>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>=\<bbb-R\>\<times\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|3>,<label|eq:dist-parabolic>
    </equation>

    where <math|<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|>> denotes the usual Euclidean
    distance on <math|\<bbb-R\>> and <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|3>>. For
    <math|\<varkappa\>\<gtr\>0> and <math|z=<around*|(|z<rsub|0>,<wide|z|\<bar\>>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>>
    we denote by

    <\equation*>
      \<varkappa\>.z\<assign\><around*|(|\<varkappa\><rsup|2s>z<rsub|0>,\<varkappa\><wide|z|\<bar\>>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>
    </equation*>

    the fractional parabolic rescaling, satisfying

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a>.z|\|><rsub|s>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\||z|\|><rsub|s>.
    </equation*>
  </definition>

  <\definition>
    <label|def:weights>We introduce the following Japanese brackets:

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<langle\>|z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||z<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/s>+<around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/2><space|2em><text|and><space|2em><around*|\<langle\>|<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\<rangle\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/2>,<space|2em>z=<around*|(|z<rsub|0>,<wide|z|\<bar\>>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>,<label|eq:Japaneese>
    </equation>

    where, as in the previous definition, <math|<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|>>
    denotes the usual Euclidean distance on <math|\<bbb-R\>> and
    <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|3>>.

    <\enumerate-alpha>
      <item>Let <math|a\<gtr\>1> and <math|\<nu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1/3|)>>.

      <item>Let <math|<around*|(|\<chi\><rsub|i
      >:\<Lambda\><rsub|0>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>|)><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1>>
      be a dyadic partition of unity on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>> with
      <math|\<chi\><rsub|i>> supported on an annulus of radius
      <math|\<sim\>2<rsup|a*i>> for <math|i\<geqslant\>0>,
      \ <math|\<chi\><rsub|-1>> supported in a ball of radius
      <math|\<approx\>1> and <math|<big|sum><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1>\<chi\><rsub|i>=1>.

      <item>Define <math|<around*|(|\<mu\><rsub|i>|)><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1>\<subseteq\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>
      by <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>>=2<rsup|-i-2>>,
      <math|i\<geqslant\>-1>.

      <item>Let <math|\<zeta\>:\<Lambda\><rsub|0>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>> be
      a weight defined by

      <\equation*>
        \<zeta\><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\><around*|\<langle\>|z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|-1>,<application-space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>.
      </equation*>

      For <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>, we also introduce the
      associated rescaled weights

      <\equation*>
        \<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\><around*|\<langle\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a>.z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|-1>,<space|2em>\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<nu\>>=<around*|\<langle\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a>.z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|-\<nu\>>,<application-space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>.
      </equation*>
    </enumerate-alpha>
  </definition>

  <\remark>
    Concerning the parameters <math|\<nu\>> and <math|a> introduced above, we
    impose the relation

    <\equation*>
      a\<nu\>=\<gamma\>,<label|eq:a-nu-gamma>
    </equation*>

    where the parameter <math|<with|color|black|\<gamma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,2s|)>>>
    will be fixed in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing>. In
    particular, throughout our analysis we shall be concerned with very small
    values of <math|\<nu\>\<gtr\>0> and with <math|a\<gtr\>1>.
  </remark>

  <\remark>
    <label|rem:reg-weight>The form of the Japaneese
    bracket<nbsp><eqref|eq:Japaneese> is motivated by the requirement that
    the weight function <math|\<zeta\>> (and its powers) be <math|C<rsup|1>>
    in the time variable and <math|C<rsup|2>> in the spatial variables. This
    regularity is essential in the a priori estimates established below (see
    Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:apriori>). Indeed, one readily verifies that

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|t>\<zeta\><around*|(|t,x|)>=-<frac|<around*|\||t|\|><rsup|<around*|(|1-s|)>/s>\<partial\><rsub|t><around*|\||t|\|>|2s*<around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsup|1/s>+<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|3/2>>,<space|2em><around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>,
    </equation*>

    which is continuous for <math|s\<less\>1>. An analogous argument applies
    to all spatial derivatives.
  </remark>

  <\remark>
    <label|rem:weight-properties>Our weights satisfy the following
    properties.\ 

    <\enumerate-alpha>
      <item>We have\ 

      <\equation*>
        \<zeta\><rsub|><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>\<lesssim\>\<zeta\><rsub|><rsup|-1><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>,
      </equation*>

      uniformly over <math|><math|z,z<rsub|1>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>>.
      Consequently,

      <\eqnarray*>
        <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>\<leqslant\>\<zeta\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>,>>|<row|<cell|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z|)>\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>\<lesssim\>\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|0><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>,>>>>
      </eqnarray*>

      uniformly over <math|><math|z,z<rsub|1>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>> and
      <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>.

      <item>We have

      <\equation*>
        \<chi\><rsub|i>\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|-1>\<lesssim\><around*|(|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>|)><rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/2>\<lesssim\>1,
      </equation*>

      uniformly in <math|i\<geqslant\>-1> and
      <math|\<mu\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>>.
    </enumerate-alpha>
  </remark>

  <paragraph*|Scale decomposition.>Let us introduce a scale decomposition of
  spacetime functions parametrised by <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>
  and where we let

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1-\<sigma\>|)>
  </equation*>

  for convenience. The value <math|\<sigma\>=1> corresponds to allowing
  fluctuations at all scales while <math|\<sigma\>\<less\>1> only at spatial
  scales <math|\<gtrsim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>> or
  equivalently at Fourier scales <math|\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>>.

  <\definition>
    <label|def:function-j>Consider a smooth and compactly supported function
    <math|j:\<bbb-R\>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>> such that

    <\equation*>
      j<around*|(|\<eta\>|)>=<around*|{|<tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|1<application-space|2em>if<application-space|2em><around*|\||\<eta\>|\|>\<leqslant\>1,>>|<row|<cell|0<application-space|2em>if<application-space|2em><around*|\||\<eta\>|\|>\<geqslant\>2.>>>>>|\<nobracket\>>
    </equation*>

    For <math|\<ell\>=0,1,2,\<ldots\>> denote

    <\equation*>
      j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>\<assign\>j<around*|(|2<rsup|-\<ell\>>*\<sigma\><rsup|-1>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>*\<eta\>|)>,<space|2em>\<eta\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>,
    </equation*>

    and let <math|j<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>j<rsub|\<sigma\>,0>> and
    <math|<wide|j|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>j<rsub|\<sigma\>,1>>.
  </definition>

  <\remark>
    Note that <math|j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\><rprime|'>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>=j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>>
    for <math|0\<leqslant\>\<ell\>\<less\>\<ell\><rprime|'>>.
  </remark>

  <\definition>
    The family <math|<around*|(|J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>=<around*|(|J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>>
    of Fourier multipliers acting on distributions is defined as

    <\equation>
      <label|eq:cutoff>J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>f<around*|(|t,x|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
      j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|<around*|\||\<omega\>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>
      j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k|)>|)>*<wide|f|^><around*|(|\<omega\>,k|)>*e<rsup|i<around*|(|\<omega\>t+
      k\<cdot\>x|)>>*<frac|\<mathd\>\<omega\>*\<mathd\>k|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>,<space|2em><around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,<space|1em>f\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>,
    </equation>

    where <math|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|2><around*|(|k|)>> is the symbol
    of the Laplacian introduced in<nbsp><eqref|eq:discrete-symbol>. In
    addition, we define <math|<around*|(|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>,\<ell\>=1,2,\<ldots\>>>
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:cutoff> with the function <math|j<rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    replaced by <math|j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>>. Moreover, we let
    <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>\<assign\><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,1><rsup|>>
    and <math|<wide|J|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>>.
  </definition>

  Note that <math|J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>f\<rightarrow\>f> as
  <math|\<sigma\>\<nearrow\>1> in <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>.
  We let <math|q<rsub|0><around*|(|k|)>\<assign\><around*|\||k|\|>>, so that
  <math|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k|)>\<rightarrow\>q<rsub|0><around*|(|k|)>>
  pointwise for <math|k\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>> as
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<rightarrow\>0>. We observe that, on account of the
  above definitions, for any <math|\<ell\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>and
  <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>, it holds that

  <\equation>
    <wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>>,<application-space|2em><application-space|2em><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>+1><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>=<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>.<label|eq:cutoff-symbol-properties>
  </equation>

  Furthermore, since <math|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>>,
  <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>> as well as
  <math|\<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> are Fourier multipliers, they all
  commute. The operators <math|<around*|(|J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
  are used to define the scale decomposition

  <\equation*>
    \<sigma\>\<mapsto\>G<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>G
  </equation*>

  of the Green function <math|G>. The operators
  <math|<around*|(|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>> play
  an auxiliary role and will be used frequently in the estimates.

  <\remark>
    <label|rmk:js>We shall use the fact that if
    <math|\<sigma\>\<less\>\<mu\><rsub|i>>, where <math|\<mu\><rsub|i>> is as
    in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights>, then
    <math|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>>>. This
    is a consequence of the definitions of <math|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>> and
    <math|\<mu\><rsub|i>>, and of the fact that, for
    <math|><math|\<sigma\>\<less\>\<mu\><rsub|i>>,\ 

    <\equation*>
      2*\<sigma\>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>\<leqslant\>2*\<mu\><rsub|i>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>=2<around*|(|2<rsup|i+2>-1|)>
      \<less\><around*|(|2<rsup|i+3>-1|)>=\<mu\><rsub|i+1>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>,
    </equation*>

    which implies <math|j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>*j<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>=j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>>
    for all <math|\<eta\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>.
  </remark>

  <paragraph*|Smoothing operators.>To establish a suitable Schauder estimate,
  we will employ smoothing operators <math|<around*|(|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
  that possess only limited regularising effects in time. It is convenient to
  choose these operators as inverses of differential operators.

  <\definition>
    <label|def:regularizing-kernels>For <math|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>
    >let

    <\equation*>
      L<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2>,<space|2em>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-1><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-2>,<space|2em>K<rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>\<assign\>L<rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>.
    </equation*>
  </definition>

  In the tightness argument, we will also employ a Littlewood\UPaley
  decomposition acting solely on the spatial variables.

  <\definition>
    <label|def:space-LP>(Spatial LP blocks) Let
    <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<Delta\>|^><rsub|i>:<with|color|black|<around*|[|0,\<infty\>|)>>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>|)><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1>>
    be a dyadic partition of unity on <math|<with|color|black|<around*|[|0,\<infty\>|)>>>,
    where <math|><math|<wide|\<Delta\>|^><rsub|-1>> is supported in
    <math|<with|color|black|<around*|[|0,1|]>>>,<math|>
    <math|<wide|\<Delta\>|^><rsub|0>> is supported in
    <math|<with|color|black|<around*|[|1/2,3/2|]>>> and
    <math|><math|<wide|\<Delta\>|^><rsub|i><around*|(|\<cdummy\>|)>\<assign\><wide|\<Delta\>|^><rsub|0><around*|(|2<rsup|-i>\<cdummy\>|)>>
    for <math|i\<geqslant\>1>. We define spatial Littlewood-Paley blocks
    <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>|)><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1>>
    \ as the Fourier multipliers on <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>|)>>
    associated with the symbols <math|k\<mapsto\><wide|\<Delta\>|^><rsub|i><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k|)>|)>>.
  </definition>

  <\remark>
    <with|color|black|By extension, we identify the fractional Laplacian
    <math|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>> and the
    spatial Littlewood-Paley blocks <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>|)><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1>>
    with the corresponding operators on <math|C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,\<zeta\>|)>>
    acting trivially on the time variable.>
  </remark>

  <\with|color|black>
    <paragraph*|Convolution operators.>We call <math|T> a convolution
    operator on <math|C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,w|)>> if
    there exists a signed measure <math|m<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>> such that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|T f|)><around*|(|z|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>m<around*|(|\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      f<around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>.
    </equation*>

    By slight abuse of notation, we usually denote the measure
    <math|m<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>> associated to <math|T> by
    <math|T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>>. We call
    <math|T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>> the kernel of the operator <math|T>. We
    denote by <math|<around*|\||T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>|\|>> the variation
    of the measure <math|T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>>. Given a nonnegative
    weight <math|w\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>|)>> we write

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|T|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w|)>>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>w<around*|(|z|)>
      <around*|\||T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>|\|>
    </equation*>

    for the weighted total variation norm of the kernel of <math|T>. If
    <math|T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>> is absolutely continuous with respect to
    the measure <math|\<mathd\>z> on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>,
    we write <math|T<around*|(|z|)>> for its density,
    <with|font-shape|italic|i.e.> <math|T<around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>=T<around*|(|z|)><with|mode|text|
    >\<mathd\>z>. For <math|p\<in\><around*|[|0,\<infty\>|]> >, we denote by
    <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|T|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p><around*|(|w|)>>> the
    weighted <math|L<rsup|p>> norm of the density of the kernel of <math|T>,
    <with|font-shape|italic|i.e.>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|T|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p><around*|(|w|)>>\<assign\><around*|\<\|\|\>|z\<mapsto\>w
      <around*|(|z|)>T<around*|(|z|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<bullet\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>> is
    the usual <math|L<rsup|p>> norm on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
    with respect to the measure <math|\<mathd\>z>. Given a weight <math|w>, a
    convolution operator <math|T> and a function <math|f> we write

    <\equation>
      <around*|(|w T f|)><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\>w<around*|(|z|)>
      <around*|(|T f|)><around*|(|z|)>.<label|eq:notation-w-T>
    </equation>

    \;

    Note that the operators

    <\equation*>
      G,G<rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>,J<rsub|\<sigma\>>,<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>,<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>,<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>
    </equation*>

    introduced above are all convolution operators on
    <math|C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>>|)>>
    for every <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2s|)>>. The kernels of the
    operators <math|G<rsub|\<sigma\>>,J<rsub|\<sigma\>>,<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    have smooth densities. The kernels of <math|G,K<rsub|\<sigma\>>> have
    densities of limited regularity. The kernels of
    <math|K<rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>,<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>,<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>>
    do not posses densities. In particular, the kernels of
    <math|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>,<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>>
    are proportional to the Dirac delta in time.\ 

    The following lemmas collect the fundamental properties of these
    convolution operators, which will be used repeatedly throughout our
    analysis.

    <\definition>
      <label|def:weight-w>For <math|\<omega\>\<in\> \<bbb-R\>> and
      <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|)>>, we write

      <\equation*>
        w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<omega\>><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>,<space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>.
      </equation*>
    </definition>

    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:bounds-K-J>For all <math|\<flat\>\<in\><around*|(|0,2s|)>>,
      we have

      <\enumerate-alpha>
        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,>

        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,>

        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|t><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>>
        and <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>>,

        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|G|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|0><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\>1>
        and <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1>,>
      </enumerate-alpha>

      uniformly over <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>
      and <math|1/2\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>\<leqslant\>\<eta\>\<less\>1>.
    </lemma>

    <\remark>
      <label|rem:decay-rate>The kernels of the operators
      <math|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsub|>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>><rsub|>,J<rsub|\<sigma\>>>
      and <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>> exhibit rapid decay in spacetime.
      In particular, these operators have finite total variation norms
      <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<bullet\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<omega\>>|)>>>
      for all <math|\<omega\>\<geqslant\>0>. In contrast, for fractional
      Laplacians of order <math|s\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>, the kernels of the
      operators <math|G> and <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> decay
      much more slowly. Their total variation norms
      <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<bullet\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<omega\>>|)>>>
      is finite only for <math|\<omega\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2s|)>>. This slow
      decay of <math|G> and <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
      constitutes a major analytical difficulty and is one of the main
      reasons why PDEs involving fractional Laplacians are particularly
      challenging to study.
    </remark>

    <\remark>
      <label|rem:weights-zeta-w>Note that all of the above bounds remain
      valid if one replaces the weights by <math|\<zeta\><rsup|-\<alpha\>>>
      or <math|\<zeta\><rsup|-\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> with any
      <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> and
      <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>, since
      <math|1\<less\>2s\<less\>2> and

      <\equation*>
        \<zeta\><rsup|-\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<leqslant\>\<zeta\><rsup|-\<alpha\>>\<lesssim\>
        w<rsup|1><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>\<leqslant\>w<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|><rsup|>,
      </equation*>

      for all <math|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
    </remark>

    <\proof>
      Item a) is proved in Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:K-kernel>. Items b) and
      c) follow from Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:J-decay>. Item<nbsp>d) follows
      from the estimates for <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
      established in Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:Gdot-decay>.
    </proof>

    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:bound-L-J>We have

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1><rsup|>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>
      </equation*>

      uniformly over <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>
      and <math|1/2\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>\<less\>1>.
    </lemma>

    <\proof>
      First note that

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>J<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<leqslant\><big|sum><rsub|i\<geqslant\>-1><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>J<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>,
      </equation*>

      where we set <math|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|-2><rsup|>=0>. Next,
      observe that <math|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>J<rsub|\<mu\>>=0>,
      unless <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>>\<geqslant\>2<rsup|-10><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>.>
      Consequently, we have

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>J<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<leqslant\><big|sum><rsub|i<mid|\|><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>>\<geqslant\>2<rsup|-10><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|J<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|i<mid|\|><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>>\<geqslant\>2<rsup|-10><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>,
      </equation*>

      where the second estimate follows from
      Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>
      and<nbsp><reference|lem:LP-block>.
    </proof>

    The following lemma combines the estimates from the preceding lemmas with
    Young's convolution inequality. The resulting bounds will be used
    frequently in the subsequent analysis, often without explicit reference.

    <\lemma>
      For all <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>> we have

      <\enumerate-alpha>
        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>*f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>*f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>,>

        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>f|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>f|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>f|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>f|\<\|\|\>>,>

        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>\<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>>,
        <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>\<partial\><rsub|t><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>>
        and <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>>,

        <item><math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>G
        f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>f|\<\|\|\>>>
        and <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>f<rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>f|\<\|\|\>>,>
      </enumerate-alpha>

      uniformly over <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>,
      <math|0\<leqslant\>\<mu\>\<leqslant\>1>,
      <math|1/2\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>\<leqslant\>\<eta\>\<less\>1> and
      <math|f\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>,
      where <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<bullet\>|\<\|\|\>>> denotes the
      <math|L<rsup|\<infty\>>> norm over <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>,
      and we use the notation introduced in<nbsp><eqref|eq:notation-w-T>.
    </lemma>

    <\proof>
      The stated bounds are consequences of the previous lemmas, together
      with Young's inequality for convolution, the identities

      <\equation*>
        K<rsub|\<sigma\>>=K<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>>
        K<rsub|\<eta\>><rsub|>,<space|2em>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>,<space|2em><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>=L<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>
      </equation*>

      and Remarks<nbsp><reference|rem:weight-properties> a)
      and<nbsp><reference|rem:weights-zeta-w>. For example, to prove the
      first bound, we note that

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>f|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z|)>
        <around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsub|\<eta\>>f|)><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>
        <around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>
        <around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsub|\<eta\>>f|)><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>
        \<zeta\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>
        <around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|K<rsub|\<eta\>>f|)>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1><rsup|>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>*f|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>>
      </equation*>

      The proof of the remaining bounds proceeds analogously.
    </proof>
  </with>

  <section|Stochastic quantisation><label|sec:sq>

  In this section we lay out the main steps in the proof of
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:main>, starting from the effective equation at
  (fractional, parabolic) spacetime scale
  <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<assign\>1-\<sigma\>>,
  <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>, obtained through a scale
  decomposition and the introduction of the approximate effective force.
  Since our analysis primarily concerns scales close to <math|1>, we shall
  restrict all scale parameters, such as <math|\<sigma\>>, to the interval
  <math|<around*|[|1/2,1|]>>.

  <subsection|Scale decomposition><label|sec:scale-decomposition>

  Let <math|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>> be a stationary
  solution to the finite system of SDEs<nbsp><eqref|eq:dynamcs-eps-M> and
  define the scale-dependent field\ 

  <\equation*>
    \<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>
  </equation*>

  localised at (fractional, parabolic) spacetime scales
  <math|\<gtrsim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>>. Then we
  have

  <\equation*>
    \<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsup|>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|)>,<space|2em>\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>,
  </equation*>

  where

  <\equation>
    F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>\<assign\>-\<lambda\>*\<phi\><rsup|3><rsup|>-r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>*\<phi\>+\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>.<label|eq:force>
  </equation>

  <with|color|black|We call <math|F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>> the
  force. Let <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|>\<assign\><big|cap><rsub|\<alpha\>\<gtr\>0>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>,\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>>|)>>
  be the space of continuous periodic in space functions on
  <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> and exhibiting subpolynomial growth
  in time at infinity. Denote by <math|<wide|\<cal-E\>|^>\<subset\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>>
  the image of <math|\<cal-E\>> under <math|\<partial\><rsub|t>>, interpreted
  as the time derivative operator on <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>>.
  Note that the white noise <math|\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>
  on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>> belongs a.s. to
  <math|<wide|\<cal-E\>|^>> and the stochastic convolution <math|G
  \ \<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>> belongs a.s. to
  <math|\<cal-E\>>.> Consider a family of functionals, referred to as the
  <em|effective force>,

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsup|>:\<cal-E\>\<rightarrow\><with|color|black|<wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>,
  </equation*>

  which is differentiable in <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> and
  satisfies the final condition

  <\equation>
    F<rsup|><rsub|1><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>=F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>.<label|eq:final-cond-f>
  </equation>

  Using the identity <math|\<phi\><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>=\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>,
  we obtain

  <\equation*>
    F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|)>=F<rsup|><rsub|1><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|1>|)>=F<rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>+R<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>,<label|eq:force-F-R>
  </equation*>

  for all <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>, where

  <\equation*>
    R<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+\<mathD\>F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>.
  </equation*>

  Here <math|\<mathD\>F<around*|(|\<psi\>|)>\<psi\><rprime|'>> denotes the
  Fréchet derivative of a functional <math|F<rsub|>> in the direction of
  <math|\<psi\><rprime|'>\<in\>\<cal-E\><rsup|>> at the point
  <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-E\>>. Moreover, we have

  <\equation*>
    \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|)>|)>=<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+R<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|)>,
  </equation*>

  where <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>\<assign\>\<cal-L\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
  and <math|<wide|J|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>>.
  Consequently, we deduce that for any choice of the effective force

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>=<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>><with|font-series|bold|>,
  </equation*>

  satisfying the conditions specified above, the pair

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\>>,R<rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>=<around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>,R<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>
  </equation*>

  <math|>satisfies the system of equations

  <\equation>
    <choice|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>=J<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|F<rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>+R<rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|R<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>=<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>H<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|\<mathD\>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>*<around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>*R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>,>>>>><text|><label|eq:rg-spde>
  </equation>

  where

  <\equation*>
    H<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>+\<mathD\>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>*<around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>*F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>|)>.<label|eq:def-H>
  </equation*>

  Our main goal will be to show that this system allows for good a priori
  estimates for a suitably chosen effective force
  <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>>.\ 

  <\remark>
    <with|color|black|Except for Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:tightness>
    and<nbsp><reference|sec:integrability>, we shall almost always suppress
    the explicit dependence on <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>
    and <math|M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>.> To avoid repetition, we will not
    restate this each time, but <with|font-series|bold|all estimates should
    be understood as uniform in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>
    and <math|M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>>, unless explicitly stated otherwise.
    In particular, we shall write <math|\<Lambda\>> for
    <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> and <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>> for
    <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>>. Likewise, we write
    <math|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>> for the discrete fractional
    Laplacian.>
  </remark>

  <\with|color|black>
    <subsection|Overview of the strategy>

    The goal of this section is to provide a blueprint that guides the reader
    through the technical aspects of the proofs and highlights the underlying
    heuristics. We will not present rigorous arguments here. Our intention is
    instead to convey intuition and the global structure of the analysis.
    Readers who find the informal reasoning confusing can safely skip this
    section without loss of logical continuity.

    Our approach to obtaining a priori global spacetime estimates for
    solutions to the system<nbsp><eqref|eq:rg-spde> relies on several new
    conceptual and technical ideas:

    <\enumerate-alpha>
      <item>the introduction of a remainder term <math|R<rsub|\<sigma\>>>,
      which circumvents the need to explicitly solve the flow equation for
      <math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>> (unlike in the original approach
      of<nbsp><cite|duchFlowEquationApproach2021|duchRenormalizationSingularElliptic2022>);

      <item>the use of new weighted norms that control the solution across
      the entire space, inspired by the spatial decomposition introduced
      in<nbsp><cite|gubinelliGlobalSolutionsElliptic2019>);

      <item>a stopping argument for the effective force, allowing us to close
      nonlinear estimates;

      <item>a collection of technical innovations addressing the difficulties
      arising from the limited spacetime decay of the fractional heat kernel.
    </enumerate-alpha>

    In what follows, we focus primarily on the new ideas required to handle
    the large-field problem. For a pedagogical overview of the flow equation
    approach, we refer the reader to the lecture
    notes<nbsp><cite|duch-notes>.

    To keep the exposition clear, let us ignore the remainder
    <math|R<rsub|\<sigma\>>> and model the original equation by

    <\equation>
      \<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>-\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>\<approx\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>-\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>,<label|eq:model-coerc>
    </equation>

    where <math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>> is a
    polynomial in the field <math|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>>. To measure the
    spacetime growth of fields, we use the weight

    <\equation*>
      <space|2em>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z|)>\<approx\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\||z|\|><rsub|s><rsup|>|)><rsup|-1>,<space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|<around*|\||z|\|><rsub|s>> is the fractional parabolic
    distance on <math|\<Lambda\>> and <math|a\<gtr\>1> is an exponent chosen
    to balance the scale behavior at large distances. Its precise value will
    later be crucial to closing our nonlinear estimates.

    Pathwise bounds on the random effective force
    <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>> are obtained from
    a flow-equation analysis of its probabilistic cumulants. The outcome is
    that <math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
    behaves as a random nonlocal polynomial in <math|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    and its coefficients are localized in regions of size
    <math|\<approx\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>> and
    scale roughly as

    <equation*|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|k-3|)>\<beta\>+\<delta\>\<ell\>>,>

    where <math|k\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>> is the monomial degree,
    <math|\<beta\>\<gtr\>\<gamma\>> encodes the field scaling,
    <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0> measures the distance to criticality, and
    <math|\<ell\>> is the perturbative order. \ Due to a Kolmogorov-type
    argument needed to extract the almost sure behaviour of the force
    <math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>> from its moments, we loose also a bit in the
    spacetime growth, which will be modelled by a weight
    <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|\<ell\>+1|)>>>,
    where <math|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<gtr\>0> is an arbitrarily small
    exponent. Overall we have, schematically,

    <\equation>
      F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<approx\>\<xi\>+<wide|r|\<bar\>>
      \<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>-\<lambda\>
      \<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>+<big|sum><rsub|\<ell\>=1><rsup|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>><big|sum><rsub|k=0><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|\<ell\>+1|)>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|k-3|)>\<beta\>+\<delta\>\<ell\>>
      \<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|k>,<label|eq:model-post>
    </equation>

    where the sums over <math|k> and <math|\<ell\>> are finite. The cutoffs
    <math|<wide|k|\<bar\>>> and <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>> are chosen so
    that the equation for the remainder <math|R<rsub|\<sigma\>>> can be
    solved, a technical aspect we omit in this heuristic discussion.

    \ To estimate the size of the solution to<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-coerc>, we
    introduce a constant <math|C<rsub|\<Phi\>>=<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>>
    (cf. Def.<nbsp><reference|def:triple-norms>) such that

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z|)>|\|>=<around*|\||<around*|(|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\>|)><around*|(|z|)>|\|>\<leqslant\>C<rsub|\<Phi\>>
      \<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z|)>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>,<space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\>,<label|eq:trivial-est>
    </equation>

    valid for all <math|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>, where
    <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>> such that
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>>\<ll\>1>
    is a random scale to be chosen later.

    For moderate distances <math|<around*|\||z|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>>,
    the spatial weight <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z|)>>
    is of order one and we are describing the distributional nature of the
    solution, growing like <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>>
    as <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<searrow\>0> for
    some <math|\<gamma\>\<gtr\>0>. For large distances
    <math|<around*|\||z|\|>\<gg\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>>,
    the spatial growth can be improved as follows. Let
    <math|<wide|\<mu\>|^>\<ll\>\<sigma\>> be such that
    <math|<around*|\||z|\|>\<approx\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|^>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>>.
    Observing that <math|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|^>>>
    due to the properties of the smoothing operators, we obtain

    <\equation>
      <tabular*|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-halign|l>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<approx\><around*|\||<around*|(|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|^>>|)>*<around*|(|z|)>|\|>\<approx\><around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|^>><around*|(|z|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<Phi\>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|^>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\||z|\|>|)><rsup|1/3>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|^>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<approx\>C<rsub|\<Phi\>>
      <around*|\||z|\|><rsup|\<gamma\>/a>*\<approx\>C<rsub|\<Phi\>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\||z|\|>|)><rsup|\<gamma\>/a>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>.>>>>><label|eq:model-better>
    </equation>

    This improved spatial growth replaces
    <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>> with
    <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>/a>>, and by taking
    <math|a> large we can make the effective growth arbitrarily mild, an
    essential feature for closing nonlinear bounds.

    Since higher-order monomials (<math|k\<gtr\>3>)
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-post> are accompanied by small coefficients
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|k-3|)>\<beta\>+\<delta\>\<ell\>>\<ll\>1>,
    a coercive bound for<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-coerc> yields, schematically,

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|><rsup|3>\<approx\><around*|\||F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><big|sum><rsub|k,\<ell\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|k-3|)>\<beta\>+\<delta\>\<ell\>><around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|><rsup|k>.<label|eq:model-size-force>
    </equation>

    We estimateded the spacetime growth by taking the worst possible weight
    <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>>,
    where <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>> denotes the largest perturbative
    order that needs to be considered. Substituting<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-better>
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-size-force>, and ignoring the mild nonlocality of
    the effective force, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|><rsup|3>\<approx\><around*|\||F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><around*|[|<big|sum><rsub|k,\<ell\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|k-3|)>\<beta\>-3k
      \<gamma\>+\<delta\>\<ell\>> \<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-k\<gamma\>/a>C<rsub|\<Phi\>><rsup|k>|]>.
    </equation*>

    The terms with <math|\<ell\>=0>, that is the first two terms on the
    right-hand side of<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-post>, are explicit and yield
    improved estimates, so that in total we arrive at

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|><rsup|3>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<beta\>+\<delta\>>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>-<wide|k|\<bar\>>
      \<gamma\>/a>*<around*|(|1+C<rsub|\<Phi\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>,<label|eq:rough-estimate>
    </equation>

    where <math|<wide|k|\<bar\>>> is the maximal degree of the monomials.
    Here we used the fact that <math|\<beta\>\<gtr\>\<gamma\>>, which allows
    the field amplitude to be compensated by the kernel size. The constant
    <math|C<rsub|\<Phi\>>> can then be estimated as

    <\equation*>
      C<rsub|\<Phi\>>\<approx\>sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      \<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3> <around*|\||\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>+\<delta\>/3>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|1-<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>-<wide|k|\<bar\>>
      \<gamma\>/a|)>/3>*<around*|(|1+C<rsub|\<Phi\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>/3>.
    </equation*>

    Choosing <math|\<gamma\>\<leqslant\>\<beta\>> such that
    <math|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>+\<delta\>/3\<geqslant\>\<vartheta\>\<gtr\>0> and
    then taking <math|a> large enough such that

    <\equation*>
      1-<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>-<wide|k|\<bar\>>
      \<gamma\>/a\<geqslant\>0,
    </equation*>

    we obtain the bound

    <\equation*>
      C<rsub|\<Phi\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>**<around*|(|1+C<rsub|\<Phi\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>/3>.
    </equation*>

    It follows that, for sufficiently small
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>>\<ll\>1>,
    the nonlinear estimate closes and yields
    <math|C<rsub|\<Phi\>>\<approx\>1>.

    Let us now address the treatment of the nonlocality of the effective
    force kernels. The main technical challenges in this work stem from the
    limited decay of the slice propagator
    <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> associated with the fractional
    parabolic operator <math|\<cal-L\>>. Roughly speaking, we only have
    algebraic decay of the form \ (see Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:Gdot-decay>):

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsup|>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d-1>
      \ <around*|(|1+<around*|\||z|\|><rsub|s>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d-2s+\<epsilon\>>,<space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\>,<label|eq:limited-decay>
    </equation>

    where <math|\<epsilon\>\<gtr\>0> is arbitrarily small. This behaviour
    contrasts sharply with the stretched-exponential decay of the standard
    heat kernel, and also with the fractional Laplacian case appearing in the
    usual (\Pstatic\Q) renormalisation group analysis of the fractional
    <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4>> model<nbsp><cite|brydgesCriticalF42003>. The
    difference arises from the limited smoothness of the symbol of the
    fractional heat operator <math|\<cal-L\>>.

    The main consequence of<nbsp><eqref|eq:limited-decay> is that the
    effective force kernels, obtained by solving a flow equation driven by
    <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>, inherit a similar algebraic
    decay. The monomials which appear in <math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
    take the schematic form

    <\equation*>
      F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|z|)>\<approx\><big|sum><rsub|k,\<ell\>><big|int>F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z;z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)><big|prod><rsub|j=1><rsup|k>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z<rsub|j>|)>
      \<mathd\>z<rsub|j>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    are random kernels. Ignoring their distributional nature and thinking of
    them as bona-fide functions, their spatial nonlocality and spatial growth
    can be modelled as (cf. Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>
    and<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels>)

    <\equation*>
      F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>\<approx\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-<around*|(|\<ell\>+1|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><around*|(|z|)>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>St<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)><rsup|>|)><rsup|-<around*|(|\<flat\>-\<ell\>
      \<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|St<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>> measures the
    diameter of the set <math|<around*|{|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|}>>.
    The initial decay exponent <math|\<flat\>\<approx\>2s> follows
    from<nbsp><eqref|eq:limited-decay>, while the additional loss
    <math|\<ell\> \<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>> reflects the growth at
    spacetime infinity of the kernel in its output variable, induced by the
    similar growth of the noise. It is now clear that, to proceed as
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:rough-estimate>, we must be able to compensate for the
    spatial growth of the fields <math|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>> by exploiting
    the limited decay of the kernels away from the diagonal.

    The remainder of this section makes this argument rigorous and
    establishes further properties of the solution.
    Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:apriori> \ develops the coercive estimate
    required in <nbsp><eqref|eq:model-size-force>, while
    Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:flow> contains the detailed analysis of the
    random force coefficients and the derivation of the precise form of
    estimate<nbsp><eqref|eq:model-post>.
  </with>

  <subsection|<with|color|black|Main estimate>>

  In this section we introduce a family of weighted norms that will be used
  to measure the size of fields over spacetime uniformly across scales. These
  norms depend on an exponent <math|\<gamma\>\<gtr\>0>, to be fixed in
  Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing>, and a terminal scale
  <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>, which will later be
  tuned according to the noise amplitude.

  <\definition>
    <label|def:triple-norms>For <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>
    and <math|f\<in\>C<around*|(|<around*|[|1/2,1|)>,<with|color|black|C><around*|(|\<Lambda\>,<with|color|black|\<zeta\>>|)>|)>>,
    we set

    <\equation>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>=<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|\<sigma\>>*J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\>|\<\|\|\>>,<label|eq:sol-norm>
    </equation>

    <\equation>
      <around|\<interleave\>|f|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>=<around|\<interleave\>|f|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*f<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.<label|eq:sharp-norm>
    </equation>
  </definition>

  The above \Ptriple norms\Q exhibit a specific behaviour with respect to the
  weight. In particular, the following lemma shows that changing the weight
  yields equivalent norms.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:triple-phi>For <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|3\<nu\>,1|]>>
    the following bounds

    <\equation>
      <around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\><mid|\|>\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|]>\<lesssim\><around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\><mid|\|>\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|]>,<label|eq:equiv-norms>
    </equation>

    \;

    <\equation>
      <around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\><mid|\|>\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|]>\<lesssim\><around|\<interleave\>|\<sigma\>\<mapsto\>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\><mid|\|>\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|]>,<label|eq:equiv-norms-L>
    </equation>

    hold uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>
    and <math|\<phi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>,
    where <math|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>><math|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\>>
    for <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Let us prove the first inequality in<nbsp><eqref|eq:equiv-norms>. We
    start by observing that, on account of the support properties of
    <math|<around*|{|\<chi\><rsub|i>|}><rsub|i>>, we have the following
    decomposition\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>sup<rsub|i><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3><around*|(|\<chi\><rsub|i>+\<chi\><rsub|i-1>+\<chi\><rsub|i+1>|)>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|i><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Let us consider separately the cases <math|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>>
    and <math|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<geqslant\>\<sigma\>>. In the first case, thanks
    to <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>
    \<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>><rsup|-1/3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>1>, we have

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>
      \<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>><rsup|-1/3>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<leqslant\>\<sigma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>.
    </equation*>

    Let us turn to the case <math|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<gtr\>\<sigma\>>. Note that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>
      \<zeta\><rsub|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>><rsup|-1/3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\<llbracket\>|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>|)><rsup|-\<alpha\>/3>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<alpha\>/3>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<alpha\>a/3>.
    </equation*>

    Moreover, on account of Remarks<nbsp><reference|rmk:js>,<nbsp><reference|rem:weight-properties>
    <with|color|black|and Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>><rsup|1/3>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Combining the above estimates, we deduce that

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<gtr\>\<sigma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<gtr\>\<sigma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>\<chi\><rsub|i>
      \<zeta\><rsub|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>><rsup|-1/3>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>>\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<alpha\>/3><around*|[|sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<gtr\>\<sigma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<alpha\>a/3><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>|]>*<around*|[|sup<rsub|i<mid|\|>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<gtr\>\<sigma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|<with|color|black|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>>
      \<phi\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i+1>>|\<\|\|\>>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<alpha\>a/3><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<alpha\>/3>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    where we used that <math|\<alpha\>a/3\<geqslant\>\<nu\>a=\<gamma\>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>.><math|> This proves the first
    inequality in<nbsp><eqref|eq:equiv-norms>. The second inequality
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:equiv-norms> is a direct consequence of the fact that
    <math|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<leqslant\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<alpha\>/3>>.
    The inequalities<nbsp><eqref|eq:equiv-norms-L> are proved similarly.
  </proof>

  The two norms <math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>,<around|\<interleave\>|f|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>>
  fix the analytical setting for the global analysis of the
  SPDE<nbsp><eqref|eq:rg-spde>. In Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:apriori>, we will
  prove a suitable coercive estimates for fractional parabolic equation with
  cubic nonlinearity, which allows us to control the large values of the
  fields. Below we state a direct consequence of this estimate.

  <\theorem>
    <label|thm:apriori>(Coercive estimate) For
    <math|\<phi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> define

    <\equation*>
      f<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>+\<lambda\>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>,<space|2em>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\>,<space|2em>\<cal-L\>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|t>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>+m<rsup|2>.
    </equation*>

    Then the following bound

    <\equation*>
      <around|<left|\<interleave\>|1>|\<phi\>|<right|\<interleave\>|1>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<lesssim\>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3>*<around|<left|\<interleave\>|1>|f|<right|\<interleave\>|1>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|1/3>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<phi\>\<in\>><math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>,
    <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\> <around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
    <math|\<lambda\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<infty\>|)>>.
  </theorem>

  <\proof>
    We apply the a priori estimates from Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:partial-coercive-estimates>
    to <math|u=\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>> and
    <math|\<rho\>=\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>>. The constants <math|A>
    and <math|B> appearing in the theorem can be bounded as follows:

    <\equation*>
      A=<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>
      \<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      a>,
    </equation*>

    and

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|B>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>u|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><rsup|>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>>|)>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><rsup|>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>u|)>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>Q<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+Q<rsub|\<sigma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Here we define

    <\equation*>
      Q<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>\<assign\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      a>.
    </equation*>

    <with|color|black|The bound <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
    a>> is proved in Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:fractional-bound>.> To
    estimate <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>
    we used<nbsp><eqref|eq:D-est>, while the bound on
    <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>
    follows from Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:D-zeta>. Moreover, using the
    bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:D-est>, we obtain

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1-s>.<label|eq:D-proof-est>
    </equation>

    We note that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|)>
      \<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*<around*|(|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Hence, using the fact that <math|<around*|\||\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>>
    and <math|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    as well as <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>>,
    we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*<around*|(|\<nabla\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,1>|)>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Together with<nbsp><eqref|eq:D-proof-est>, this proves that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-s>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>.
    Therefore,

    <\equation*>
      B\<lesssim\><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      a>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|s
      a><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-s>|)><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|s
      a-s> <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    By Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:partial-coercive-estimates> and Young's
    inequality, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>C
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a
      s>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      f<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+C<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a
      s-s><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|)><rsup|1/3><rsub|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>C
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a
      s>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      f<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/3><rsub|>+C
      \<lambda\><rsup|-1/3><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|a
      s-s|)>/3><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/3>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>C
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a
      s>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      f<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/3><rsub|>+C<rprime|'>\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|a
      s-s|)>/2>+<frac|1|2><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    As a result, we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|a
      s-s|)>/2> +\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*f<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/3><rsub|>.
    </equation*>

    This allows us to deduce that

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>=sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>+<around*|(|a
      s-s|)>/2>\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2> +\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3>
      sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      f<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|)><rsup|1/3><rsub|>.
    </equation*>

    Hence, provided <math|\<gamma\>+<around*|(|a
    s-s|)>/2\<geqslant\>\<gamma\>\<geqslant\>0>, which follows from
    <math|a\<gtr\>1>, we conclude our claim.
  </proof>

  The coercivity estimate derived above provides the key ingredient for
  deriving a priori bounds for solutions to system<nbsp><eqref|eq:rg-spde>,
  as stated in the following theorem.

  <\theorem>
    <\with|color|black>
      <label|thm:apriori-system>Let <math|\<phi\>=\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>
      be a solution of the stochastic quantisation
      equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:dynamcs-eps-M> and

      <\equation*>
        <around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>=F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsup|>:\<cal-E\>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>
      </equation*>

      be a family of functionals differentiable in
      <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> and satisfying the final
      condition<nbsp><eqref|eq:final-cond-f>. For
      <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>> define

      <\equation*>
        \<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\>,<space|2em>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>F<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>-F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>.
      </equation*>
    </with>

    Suppose that there exist constants <math|S\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>,C<rsub|F>\<geqslant\>1>
    and <math|\<vartheta\>,<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<gtr\>0> such that

    <\equation>
      <wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|\<nu\>,1|)>,<space|2em>\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>\<gamma\>\<wedge\><around*|(|2s-\<gamma\>|)>,<space|2em><around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>
      <wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<leqslant\>\<vartheta\>/4,<label|eq:thm-constraints>
    </equation>

    and <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>> satisfies the
    following estimates

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<cwith|3|3|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|[|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>-<around*|(|-\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>|)>|]>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around*|<left|[|3>|C<rsub|F>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|S>+<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|2>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<psi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|<right|]|3>>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>H<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|C<rsub|F>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|S>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|C<rsub|F>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>><around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|S>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<wide|\<psi\>|^>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|C<rsub|F>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|S>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|\<psi\>|^>|\<\|\|\>>,>>>>><label|eq:est-F>
    </equation>

    for all <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>
    and <math|\<psi\>,<wide|\<psi\>|^>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>,
    where we denote <math|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\>>
    and <math|<around*|(|\<cal-L\>\<psi\>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>\<cal-L\>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>>,
    and the functional <math|H> is defined by<nbsp><eqref|eq:def-H>.\ 

    Then there exists a universal constant <math|<wide|C|^>\<gtr\>0> such
    that for all <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>
    satisfying

    <\equation>
      <with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>\<leqslant\><wide|C|^>*<around*|(|<around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1>+1|)>C<rsub|F>|)><rsup|-2>,><label|eq:bound-mubar>
    </equation>

    we have

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>1,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>.
    </equation*>
  </theorem>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\remark>
      By the elementary argument presented in
      Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:scale-decomposition>, our assumptions on
      <math|\<phi\>> and <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>>>
      imply that <math|<around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\>>,R<rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>>>
      is a solution of<nbsp><eqref|eq:rg-spde>.
    </remark>
  </with>

  <\proof>
    Define

    <\equation>
      \<Phi\>=\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<assign\>1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><rsup|-1>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>+\<theta\><rsub|R><rsup|-1>*<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>,<label|eq:def-Phi>
    </equation>

    for constants <math|\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>>,\<theta\><rsub|R>\<gtr\>0>
    to be fixed later. Our goal is to bound each term on the right-hand side
    by an increasing function of <math|\<Phi\>> itself and then apply a
    continuity argument to establish the uniform bounds claimed. For now, we
    omit the index <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>, as
    the estimates hold uniformly in this parameter.

    Let <math|C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>>=C<rsub|F><around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>>.
    We first prove a bound for <math|<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>>.
    To this end, we use Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:weighted-gronwall> below,
    which shows that we can control <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>
    in terms of <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>.
    Note that

    <\equation*>
      <wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>=<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><around*|(|\<cal-L\>\<phi\>-F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|)>,
    </equation*>

    which follows from<nbsp><eqref|eq:dynamcs-eps-M>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:force-F-R>. Since <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|\<nu\>,1|)>>
    and <math|\<vartheta\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<gamma\>|]>>, by
    Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:bound-L-J>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:triple-phi>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><around*|(|\<cal-L\><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-L\><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<phi\><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|\<vartheta\>\<in\><around*|(|0,2s-\<gamma\>|]>>, by
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J> and the
    estimates<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>,we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    Altogether, this yields

    <\equation>
      sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>.<label|eq:J-R-bound>
    </equation>

    Using<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F> and Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J> we
    also have

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><big|int><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1>H<rsub|\<eta\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<mathd\>\<eta\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>
      <big|int><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>
      K<rsub|\<eta\>>H<rsub|\<eta\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>.
    </equation*>

    By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:weighted-gronwall>, it then follows that

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>
      K<rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>exp<around*|(|C
      C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>|)>,
    </equation*>

    possibly after adjusting the constant <math|C>. Hence,
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:sharp-norm>,

    <\equation>
      <around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>exp<around*|(|C
      C<rsub|F><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2><around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>|)>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>exp<around*|(|C
      C<rsub|F><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>\<Phi\><rsup|S>|)>.<label|eq:bound-R-sharp>
    </equation>

    The control of <math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>>
    is obtained from<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>\ 

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|<around*|(|J<rsub|\<bullet\>>F<rsub|\<bullet\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|)>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>+<around|\<interleave\>|J<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F><around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>><around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|2>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    using in particular Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J> to bound the
    contribution from <math|R>. From this it follows that

    <\equation>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>\<lesssim\><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)>\<Phi\><rsup|S><label|eq:bound-force>
    </equation>

    and

    <\equation>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>\<leqslant\><around|\<interleave\>|\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>+<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>\<lesssim\><around*|(|\<lambda\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>*+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)>\<Phi\><rsup|S>,<label|eq:bound-Lphi-sharp>
    </equation>

    by triangular inequality and\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>=\<lambda\>*sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\>*<around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3>*\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|]><rsup|3>=\<lambda\>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|3>.
    </equation*>

    Next, the a<nbsp>priori estimates of Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-force> give

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<with|color|black|\<gamma\>>>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#><rsup|1/3>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<with|color|black|\<gamma\>>>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|<with|color|black|><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>*+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)><rsup|1/3>\<Phi\><rsup|S/3>*.>>>>><label|eq:bound-phi-triple>
    </equation>

    Gathering<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-R-sharp>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-Lphi-sharp>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-phi-triple>, we obtain

    <\equation>
      \<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>1+C
      <around*|<left|[|4>|\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>+\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)><rsup|1/3>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|S/3>+\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>
      \<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|S>+\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>exp<around*|(|C
      \<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|S>|)>|<right|]|4>>,<label|eq:bound-Phi>
    </equation>

    where

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>/2>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1><around*|(|<with|color|black|><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>*+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|\<lambda\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>*+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)>+\<theta\><rsub|R><rsup|-1><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>+C<rsub|F><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Choose

    <\equation>
      \<theta\><rsub|R>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>\<lambda\>,<space|2em>\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>\<lambda\>.<label|eq:choice-theta-LR>
    </equation>

    <with|color|black|Then <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<mapsto\>\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>>
    is a decreasing function> and

    <\equation*>
      \<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<leqslant\><with|color|black|><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2><around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<gamma\>-\<vartheta\>|)>/2>+<around*|(|2\<lambda\><rsup|-1>+1|)>C<rsub|F>*+5*+\<lambda\><rsup|-1><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>-<with|color|black|\<vartheta\>/2>>|)>\<leqslant\><with|color|black|10
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2><around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1>+1|)>C<rsub|F>>.
    </equation*>

    Fix <math|\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>\<gtr\>0> small enough such that

    <\equation>
      C <around*|[|\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>+\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/3>4<rsup|S/3>+\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>
      4<rsup|S>+\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>*exp<around*|(|C \<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>
      4<rsup|S>|)>|]>\<leqslant\>1,<label|eq:bound-tau>
    </equation>

    and define <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>=<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>><around*|(|\<lambda\>,C<rsub|F>|)>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>
    as the (unique) solution to\ 

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|10 <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|\<ast\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>
      <around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1>+1|)>C<rsub|F>=\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>.>
    </equation*>

    Then for all <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>>
    we have <math|\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<leqslant\>\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>>
    and as a consequence of<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-Phi>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-tau>,

    <\equation*>
      \<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>4\<Rightarrow\>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>2.
    </equation*>

    Define the set

    <\equation*>
      A\<assign\><around*|{|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>
      <mid|\|> \<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>4|}>\<subseteq\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>.
    </equation*>

    Note that <math|A\<neq\>\<varnothing\>> since for
    <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<nearrow\>1> we have
    <math|\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<searrow\>1>.
    <with|color|black|As the map <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<mapsto\>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
    is continuous, the set <math|A> is closed in
    <math|<around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>>. Hence, to
    prove that <math|A=<around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>>,
    it is enough to show that <math|A> is open in
    <math|<around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>>. If
    <math|\<mu\>\<in\>A>, then <math|\<Phi\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<leqslant\>2> and
    by continuity, there exists a neighbourhood of <math|\<mu\>> within
    <math|<around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>> on which the
    function <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<mapsto\>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
    takes values not exceeding <math|4>.> We conclude that
    <math|A=<around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>,1|)>> and
    therefore that <math|\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>>\<leqslant\>2>.
    Using<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-theta-LR> this implies that for
    <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>=<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>1,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>,
    </equation*>

    with

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>=<around*|<left|(|1>|\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|-1>10
      <around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1>+1|)>C<rsub|F>|<right|)|1>><rsup|2/\<vartheta\>>\<lesssim\><around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1>+1|)>C<rsub|F>|<right|)|1>><rsup|2/\<vartheta\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|C<rsub|F>> and <math|\<lambda\>\<gtr\>0>.
  </proof>

  To apply the previous theorem to the analysis of<nbsp><eqref|eq:rg-spde>,
  we need to construct suitable approximate solution to the flow equation

  <\equation>
    \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>+\<mathD\>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=0<label|eq:flow-eq-sec2>
  </equation>

  for the effective force

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>=<around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>,
  </equation*>

  subject to the final condition<nbsp><eqref|eq:final-cond-f>.
  Sec.-<reference|sec:flow> will be devoted to the construction of such an
  effective force <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>>, as
  formulated in the following theorem.

  <\theorem>
    <label|thm:effective-force>There exists a choice of the deterministic
    parameters

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)><rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|]>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>
    </equation*>

    and a family of random, scale-dependent functionals

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>=F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsup|>:\<cal-E\>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>
    </equation*>

    such that:

    <\enumerate-alpha>
      <item>The map <math|\<sigma\>\<mapsto\>><math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>> is
      differentiable for <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>.

      <item>The final condition<nbsp><eqref|eq:final-cond-f> holds.

      <item>The estimates<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F> are satisfied with
      <math|C<rsub|F>=1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>
      and <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>> introduced in
      Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels>.

      <item>For all <math|N\<geqslant\>1>, it holds that

      <\equation>
        sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>
        \<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|N>|<right|]|3>>\<less\>\<infty\>.<label|eq:stochastic-estimates-kernels>
      </equation>
    </enumerate-alpha>
  </theorem>

  We complete this section with the proof of the following auxiliary lemma,
  used in Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori-system>.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:weighted-gronwall>Suppose that there exist constants
    <math|S\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>,C<rsub|F>\<geqslant\>1> and
    <math|\<vartheta\>,<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<gtr\>0> such that

    <\equation*>
      <wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|\<nu\>,1|)>,<space|2em><around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>
      <wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<leqslant\>\<vartheta\>/4
    </equation*>

    and <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>> satisfies the
    following estimate

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<wide|\<psi\>|^>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|C<rsub|F>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|S>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|\<psi\>|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>,>>>>><label|eq:est-DF>
    </equation>

    for all <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>
    and <math|\<psi\>,<wide|\<psi\>|^>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>,
    where we denote <math|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\>>.
    <with|color|black|Fixed a function <math|<around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>\<ni\>\<mu\>\<mapsto\>\<cal-H\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>
    and consider the linear equation>

    <\equation>
      R<rsub|\<mu\>>=\<cal-H\><rsub|\<mu\>>+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>,<space|2em>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>.<label|eq:lin-R>
    </equation>

    Then there exists a universal constant <math|C\<gtr\>0> such that

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>
      K<rsub|\<mu\>>R<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\> exp<around*|(|C
      C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>|)>
      <around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>
      K<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-H\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|]>,<space|2em>\<mu\>\<geqslant\>\<eta\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,<label|eq:gronwall>
    </equation>

    where <math|C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>>=C<rsub|F>**<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Start by observing that, by interpolation, for any
    <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>> and
    <math|\<beta\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>, we have by Young's inequality

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<beta\><around*|(|1-\<alpha\>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|\<alpha\>+<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>><around*|(|1-\<alpha\>|)>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<beta\><around*|(|1-\<alpha\>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1-\<alpha\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<beta\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Choose <math|\<alpha\>=<around*|(|1-2<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>>.
    Then <math|\<alpha\>+<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>><around*|(|1-\<alpha\>|)>=1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>
    and <math|1-\<alpha\>=<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>>.
    Consequently,

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<beta\><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<beta\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.<label|eq:interp>
    </equation>

    Then, by<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-DF>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    and by<nbsp><eqref|eq:interp> with <math|\<beta\>=2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>>,
    and Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>, we have

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>><around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|)>.<label|eq:grad-interp>
    </equation>

    At this point, to deduce the desired estimate, we apply Gronwall's
    inequality to

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>>R<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>>\<cal-H\><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>+C
      C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1-2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>>
      <around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>|)>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>,
    </equation*>

    which follows from<nbsp><eqref|eq:lin-R> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:grad-interp>,
    and use the inequality <math|\<vartheta\>-2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/<around*|(|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<geqslant\>\<vartheta\>/2>.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Tightness><label|sec:tightness>

  In this section, we apply Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori-system>,
  together with the effective force constructed in
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force>, to prove tightness of the
  sequence of measures <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<nu\>|^><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><rsub|>>.
  This constitutes the first step in the proof of our main result,
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:main>. In order to pass to the limit
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<rightarrow\>0> and <math|M\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>> we
  embed all the random spatially periodic fields
  <math|\<phi\>=\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>> in the same
  space by extending them from <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> to
  <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>>. Let

  <\equation>
    \<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>><around*|(|t,x|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
    <wide|\<theta\>|^><around*|(|\<varepsilon\>*<around*|\||k|\|>|)>*<wide|\<phi\>|^><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|\<omega\>,k|)>*e<rsup|i<around*|(|\<omega\>t+
    k\<cdot\>x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>\<omega\>*\<mathd\>k|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>,<space|2em><around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>,<label|eq:embedding>
  </equation>

  where <math|<wide|\<theta\>|^>:\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>>
  that <math|<wide|\<theta\>|^><around*|(|0|)>=1> and
  <math|<wide|\<theta\>|^><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>=0> for
  <math|<around*|\||\<eta\>|\|>\<gtr\>1>. The random fields
  <math|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>>> all live now in the
  continuum domain <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>> for any
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>>. To extract
  information about the EQFT, we must evaluate the marginal at a fixed time
  of the SPDE solution. This is not possible when controlling only spacetime
  distributional norms such as<nbsp><math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>.
  The necessary temporal regularity can, however, be recovered by means of a
  Schauder estimate adapted to our weighted norms. Indeed, by
  Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:schauder-full> and using
  <math|\<rho\>\<leqslant\>\<rho\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>, we obtain

  <\equation*>
    sup<rsub|i>*2<rsup|-*i\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|i>*2<rsup|-*i\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|<right|]|3>>.
  </equation*>

  By Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori-system> there exists
  <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> such that
  <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>>
  is of order <math|C<rsub|F>=1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>
  and

  <\equation*>
    <around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>1,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>.
  </equation*>

  Recalling that <math|\<cal-L\>\<phi\>=F<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>+R<rsub|\<mu\>>>,
  we deduce from the above bounds that

  <\equation>
    <around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|>\<leqslant\><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>F<rsub|\<bullet\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|F>
    <around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>|)><rsup|S>+\<lambda\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|F>.<label|eq:est-Lphi>
  </equation>

  Combining this with the previous Schauder estimate yields

  <\equation>
    sup<rsub|i>*2<rsup|-*i\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>=sup<rsub|i>*2<rsup|-*i\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>C<rsub|F>\<lesssim\><rsub|>C<rsub|F><rsup|2\<gamma\>/\<vartheta\>+1>.<label|eq:schauder-est>
  </equation>

  To derive a meaningful estimate, we need to control a suitable weighted
  Besov norm of <math|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>>> in terms
  of the left-hand side of the bound above. Indeed, we have

  <\eqnarray*>
    <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)><around*|(|\<theta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<ast\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|\<theta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>/<wide|\<rho\>|\<bar\>><rsup|>|)><around*|(|x-\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|1><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>|)>>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>,>>>>
  </eqnarray*>

  where <math|<wide|\<rho\>|\<bar\>><around*|(|x|)>\<assign\>\<rho\><around*|(|0,x|)>>
  and <with|color|black|<math|\<ast\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> denotes the
  convolution on the lattice <math|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>>>.
  Here we used the fact that

  <\equation*>
    \<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>><around*|(|t,x|)>=<around*|(|\<theta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<ast\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|)><around*|(|x|)>,<space|2em>\<theta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|x|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>><wide|\<theta\>|^><around*|(|\<varepsilon\>*<around*|\||k|\|>|)>e<rsup|i
    k\<cdot\>x><frac|*\<mathd\>k|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d>>.
  </equation*>

  As a result, we have

  <\equation*>
    sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>><around*|(|t|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<cal-C\><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>,\<rho\><around*|(|t|)>|)>>=sup<rsub|i>*2<rsup|-*i\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>|)>>\<lesssim\><rsub|>C<rsub|F><rsup|2\<gamma\>/\<vartheta\>+1>\<lesssim\>1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|4\<gamma\>/\<vartheta\>+2>,
  </equation*>

  <with|color|black|where <math|\<cal-C\><rsup|\<alpha\>><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>,w|)>>
  stands for the usual Hölder\UBesov norm with the weight <math|w> and the
  regularity index <math|\<alpha\>>>. Combining the above estimate with
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force>, we arrive at

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>><big|int><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<varphi\><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<cal-C\><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>,<wide|\<rho\>|\<bar\>>|)>><rsup|N><wide|\<nu\>|^><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>
    \<bbb-E\><around*|[|sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<phi\><rsup|<around*|[|\<varepsilon\>,M|]>><around*|(|t|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<cal-C\><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>,\<rho\><around*|(|t|)>|)>><rsup|N>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\><rsub|>>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>
    \<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|3>|1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|4\<gamma\>N/\<vartheta\>+2N>|<right|]|3>>\<less\>\<infty\>,<label|eq:tightness>>>>>>
  </equation>

  for all <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>. The
  bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:tightness> implies the tightness of the family
  <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<nu\>|^><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)><rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>>
  in <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>|)>>. This proves
  the first part of Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:main>.

  <subsection|Integrability><label|sec:integrability>

  In order to complete the proof of Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:main> it
  remains to establish the integrability property of the measures
  <math|<wide|\<nu\>|~><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>> uniformly in
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> and
  <math|M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> and obtain the
  bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:int-bound> for any limit points. We look to estimate
  quantities of the form

  <\equation*>
    Z<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>>\<assign\><big|int>exp<around*|<left|[|3>|\<theta\>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>|<right|]|3>>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>,
  </equation*>

  where <math|\<theta\>\<gtr\>0> is a small parameter,

  <\equation>
    Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|-A/2><label|eq:Q-A>
  </equation>

  is a regularising kernel and

  <\equation>
    h<around*|(|x|)>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|-B><label|eq:h-B>
  </equation>

  is a polynomially decaying weight in the spatial variables. The constants
  <math|A> and <math|B> are chosen big enough according to
  Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bound-o> below.

  The main tool for this purpose is the Hairer\USteele argument
  <cite|hairerPhiMeasureHas2022>, which provides optimal estimates with
  respect to the growth of the function. We introduce a new
  <with|font-shape|italic|tilted> probability measure

  <\equation>
    \<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>\<assign\><frac|exp<around*|<left|[|3>|\<theta\>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>|<right|]|3>>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>|Z<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>>>.<label|eq:exp-tilt>
  </equation>

  <with|color|black|To prove that this measure is well defined we take
  advantage of the presence of the coercive term
  <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|4><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>>
  in the action functional<nbsp><eqref|eq:action> defining the original
  measure <math|\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>> and use the inequality>

  <\equation*>
    <with|color|black|\<theta\> <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>\<leqslant\><frac|\<lambda\>|4>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|4><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>,>
  </equation*>

  <with|color|black|for all <math|\<varepsilon\>> and <math|M> as soon as
  <math|\<theta\>\<gtr\>0> is small enough and <math|A,B> are big enough.>
  Observe that Jensen's inequality gives

  <\equation*>
    1=<big|int>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>=Z<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><big|int>exp<around*|<left|[|3>|-\<theta\>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>|<right|]|3>>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>\<geqslant\>Z<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>>*exp<around*|[|-\<theta\><big|int><around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>|]>.
  </equation*>

  Hence,

  <\equation>
    log<big|int>exp<around*|<left|[|3>|\<theta\>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>|<right|]|3>>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>=log
    Z<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>>\<leqslant\>\<theta\><big|int><around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>.<label|eq:hs-tilt>
  </equation>

  The problem of controlling the size of <math|Z<rsub|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>|)>>>
  is, by virtue of<nbsp><eqref|eq:hs-tilt>, reduced to estimating certain
  polynomial moments of <math|\<varphi\>> under the tilted measure
  <math|\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>>.
  Through stochastic quantisation, this measure can be identified with the
  marginal law of a stationary solution to the SPDE

  <\equation>
    \<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|>+\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|><rsup|3><rsup|>-r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>
    \<phi\><rsup|>=O<around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|>|)>+\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>,<label|eq:tilted-spde>
  </equation>

  where the additional perturbation <math|O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>> is given by

  <\equation*>
    O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)><with|color|black|<around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>>=-\<theta\><frac|\<delta\>|\<delta\>\<phi\>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|h
    Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><with|color|black|<around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>=-2\<theta\>
    <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|h Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><with|color|black|<around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>
    <around*|(|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><with|color|black|<around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>>.
  </equation*>

  <\with|color|black>
    We use the notation

    <\equation*>
      Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>=<with|color|black|>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|h<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)>,<space|2em><around*|(|h<rsup|i>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><with|color|black|><around*|(|t,x|)>=<around*|(|h<rsup|><around*|(|x|)>|)><rsup|i>
      <around*|(|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><with|color|black|><around*|(|t,x|)>,<space|1em>i\<in\><around*|{|1,2|}>.
    </equation*>

    We exploited above the fact that the operator
    <math|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> is self-adjoint and bounded. Note that
    using the fact that <math|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>> has a fast-decaying
    continuous kernel, one shows that <math|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>> is
    continuous and has a mild polynomial growth. Hence, <math|h
    Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>> is in
    <math|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>>.
  </with>

  Estimates for this new equation uniform in
  <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>> and
  <math|M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> can be obtained by modifying our previous
  arguments. As before we rewrite<nbsp><eqref|eq:tilted-spde> as a system of
  equations

  <\equation>
    <choice|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>=J<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|F<rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>+R<rsup|O><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|R<rsup|O><rsub|\<mu\>>=<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>H<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>+O<around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|>|)>+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>\<mathD\>F<rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>*<around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>*R<rsup|O><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>>>><label|eq:rem-O>
  </equation>

  for

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>,R<rsup|O><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>,R<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>,O><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>>.
  </equation*>

  Applying estimate<nbsp><eqref|eq:gronwall> with <math|\<eta\>=\<mu\>> to
  the equation for <math|R<rsub|\<bullet\>><rsup|O>>, we obtain

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>*K<rsub|\<mu\>>R<rsup|O><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>
    exp<around*|(|C C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>|)><around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>>
    <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>
    K<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-H\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
    sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|O>|\<\|\|\>>|]>,
  </equation*>

  with

  <\equation*>
    \<cal-H\><rsub|\<mu\>>=O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>H<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>.
  </equation*>

  The term with <math|H<rsub|\<sigma\>>> can be estimated as previously
  from<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>, while to estimate <math|O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>>
  we use the uniform boundedness of <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>>
  and Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bound-o> below. We obtain that

  <\equation*>
    sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>
    K<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-H\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>C<rsub|F>
    <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>
    <around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>+\<theta\>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>><rsup|3>,
  </equation*>

  uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>.> We also
  observe that

  <\equation*>
    sup<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>R<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|O>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>
    C<rsub|F><around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>,
  </equation*>

  uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>, by an argument
  analogous to the one leading to<nbsp><eqref|eq:J-R-bound>. Therefore,
  combining the above estimates, we obtain

  <\equation*>
    <around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsup|O><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>\<lesssim\>exp<around*|(|C
    C<rsub|\<cal-Q\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>|)>
    <around*|<left|[|5>|C<rsub|F> <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>
    <around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|S>+\<theta\>*<around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>><rsup|3>|<right|]|5>>.
  </equation*>

  We need a good bound for <math|<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>>
  in terms of <math|\<Phi\>=\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>> defined
  by<nbsp><eqref|eq:def-Phi> with <math|R> replaced by <math|R<rsup|O>>.
  Observe that by<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>, we have

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>F<around*|(|\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsup|O><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<lambda\>\<Phi\><rsup|3>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsup|O><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<lambda\>\<Phi\><rsup|3>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S>+\<theta\><rsub|R>*\<Phi\>.>>>>><label|eq:K-L-phi-O>
  </equation>

  As a result, for <math|\<theta\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>, we obtain

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsup|O><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|exp<around*|(|C
    C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>|)><around*|<left|[|5>|C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><around*|(|1+\<lambda\>|)><rsup|3>\<Phi\><rsup|9>+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S>|)><rsup|3>+\<theta\>
    \<theta\><rsub|R><rsup|3>*\<Phi\><rsup|3>|<right|]|5>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|exp<around*|(|C
    C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>|)><around*|<left|[|5>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>+\<theta\><around*|(|1+\<lambda\>|)><rsup|3>+\<theta\>
    \<theta\><rsub|R><rsup|3>*|<right|]|5>>\<Phi\><rsup|9>,>>>>><label|eq:bound-ro>
  </equation>

  with possibly different constants <math|C>.
  Gathering<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-ro>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-Lphi-sharp>
  and<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-phi-triple> we arrive at

  <\equation>
    \<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>1+C
    <around*|<left|[|4>|\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>+\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)><rsup|1/3>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|S/3>+\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>
    \<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|S>+\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|9>*exp<around*|(|C
    \<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|S>|)>|<right|]|4>>,<label|eq:bound-Phi-O>
  </equation>

  where

  <\equation*>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>/2>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>*+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)>+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|\<lambda\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>*+\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>+\<theta\><rsub|R>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+\<theta\><rsub|R><rsup|-1><around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>+\<theta\><around*|(|1+\<lambda\>|)><rsup|3>+\<theta\>*\<theta\><rsub|R><rsup|3>|<right|]|3>>+C<rsub|F><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2>.>>>>>
  </equation*>

  Let

  <\equation>
    \<theta\><rsub|R>=\<lambda\>\<theta\><rsup|1/2>,<space|2em>\<theta\><rsub|\<cal-L\>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>\<lambda\>.<label|eq:choice-theta-LR-O>
  </equation>

  <with|color|black|Then <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<mapsto\>\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>>
  is a decreasing function> and, for <math|\<theta\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>>,
  we have

  <\equation*>
    \<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<leqslant\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2><around*|[|<around*|(|3+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>|)>+<around*|(|1+2\<lambda\><rsup|-1>|)>C<rsub|F>*+\<lambda\><rsup|-1>\<theta\><rsup|-1/2>|]>+\<theta\><rsup|1/2><around*|[|2+\<lambda\><rsup|-1><around*|(|1+\<lambda\>|)><rsup|3>+\<lambda\><rsup|2>|]>.
  </equation*>

  Fix <math|\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>\<gtr\>0> so that

  <\equation*>
    C <around*|<left|[|4>|\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>+\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/3>4<rsup|S/3>+\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>
    4<rsup|S>+\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>4<rsup|9>*exp<around*|(|C
    \<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>4<rsup|S>|)>|<right|]|4>>\<leqslant\>1.\ 
  </equation*>

  Let <math|\<theta\><rsub|\<ast\>>=\<theta\><rsub|\<ast\>><around*|(|\<lambda\>|)>>
  be such that

  <\equation*>
    \<theta\><rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/2><around*|[|2+\<lambda\><rsup|-1><around*|(|1+\<lambda\>|)><rsup|3>+\<lambda\><rsup|2>|]>=\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>/2,
  </equation*>

  and define <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>=<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>><around*|(|\<lambda\>,\<theta\><rsub|\<ast\>>,C<rsub|F>|)>>
  by

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>/2><around*|[|<around*|(|3+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>|)>+<around*|(|1+2\<lambda\><rsup|-1>|)>C<rsub|F>*+\<lambda\><rsup|-1>\<theta\><rsup|-1/2>|]>=\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>/2.
  </equation*>

  Then, for <math|\<theta\>\<leqslant\>\<theta\><rsub|\<ast\>>> and
  <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>>,
  we have <math|\<tau\><around*|(|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>|)>\<leqslant\>\<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>>>,
  and the continuity argument from Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori-system>
  can be applied to obtain the desired estimates. We conclude that
  <math|\<Phi\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>>\<leqslant\>2>.
  By<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-theta-LR-O> this implies that for
  <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>=<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<ast\>>>, we have

  <\equation*>
    <around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>1,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<vartheta\>/2>,<space|2em><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>R<rsup|O><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\>\<theta\><rsup|1/2>,
  </equation*>

  with

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>=<around*|<left|[|4>|2
    \<tau\><rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|-1><around*|<left|(|2>|<around*|(|3+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>|)>+<around*|(|1+2\<lambda\><rsup|-1>|)>C<rsub|F>*+\<lambda\><rsup|-1>\<theta\><rsup|-1/2>|<right|)|2>>|<right|]|4>><rsup|2/\<vartheta\>>\<lesssim\><around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|(|1+\<lambda\><rsup|-1>|)>C<rsub|F>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1>\<theta\><rsup|-1/2>|<right|]|3>><rsup|2/\<vartheta\>>,
  </equation*>

  uniformly in <math|C<rsub|F>=1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>,
  <math|\<theta\>\<leqslant\>\<theta\><rsub|\<ast\>><around*|(|\<lambda\>|)>>
  and <math|\<lambda\>\<gtr\>0>. By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bound-o>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:K-L-phi-O>
  and<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-theta-LR-O>, we also have

  <\equation*>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>
    \<rho\><around*|(|t,0|)><rsup|4> <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><around*|(|t|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-4\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>><rsup|4>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-4\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|\<Phi\>+\<lambda\>\<Phi\><rsup|3>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>>C<rsub|F>\<Phi\><rsup|S>+\<theta\><rsub|R>*\<Phi\>|<right|]|3>><rsup|4>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\><rsub|\<lambda\>>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-4\<gamma\>>C<rsub|F>\<lesssim\><rsub|>1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|16\<gamma\>/\<vartheta\>+2><rsup|>.>>>>>
  </equation*>

  As a consequence of Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force>, we obtain

  <\eqnarray*>
    <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<with|color|black|sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>><big|int><around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4N>\<nu\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M,\<theta\>><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>
    \<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|t|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4N>|<right|]|3>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<varepsilon\>\<in\>2<rsup|-\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>,M\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>
    \<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|3>|1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|16\<gamma\>N/\<vartheta\>+2N>|<right|]|3>>\<less\>\<infty\>,>>>>
  </eqnarray*>

  for all <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> and <math|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>. From
  this and<nbsp><eqref|eq:hs-tilt>, we deduce easily that any accumulation
  point <math|\<nu\>> of the sequence <math|<around*|(|<wide|\<nu\>|^><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>>
  satisfies<nbsp><eqref|eq:int-bound> provided <math|\<theta\>\<gtr\>0> is
  small enough. This proves the exponential integrability, required for the
  Osterwalder\USchrader reconstruction, completing the proof of
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:main>.

  <\remark>
    The choice of the norm to verify the exponential integrability is quite
    arbitrary. Since we need to determine an SPDE for it, we want a
    differentiable norm. In general, we could replace the <math|L<rsup|2>>
    norm by any <math|L<rsup|2n>> norm, as long as <math|n> is finite and
    similarly use a different weight <math|h> in space and smoothing operator
    <math|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>, as long as they remain compatible with our
    Schauder estimate.
  </remark>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:bound-o>Suppose that the parameters <math|A> and <math|B>
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:Q-A> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:h-B> satisfy
    <math|A\<gtr\>\<gamma\>> and <math|B\<geqslant\>d+1>. Then it holds that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>*\<theta\>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|4>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|4>><rsup|3>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>> \<rho\><rsub|0><around*|(|t,0|)><rsup|4>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><around*|(|t|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-4\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>><rsup|4>.
    </equation*>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Let us first observe that

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<theta\>*
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*<around*|(|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>
      <around*|(|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h*<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<theta\>*
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\><around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>*\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)><with|font-series|bold|>
      <around*|(|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>
      <around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>> \<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1>
      \<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|> Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h*<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<theta\>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|1>|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>
      <around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      \<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>
      |<right|\<\|\|\>|1>> <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>
      \ \ <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h*<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    By Remark<nbsp><eqref|rem:weight-properties> (a) we have

    <\equation*>
      \<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>\<lesssim\>\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,0|)>\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|0,x|)>.
    </equation*>

    Hence, using the fact that <math|h<around*|(|x|)>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|-B>>
    with <math|B\<geqslant\>d+1>, we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>\<lesssim\>\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-2><around*|(|t,0|)>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|0,\<bullet\>|)><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>\<lesssim\>\<rho\><rsup|-2><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,0|)>.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|\<rho\><rsup|-2><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,0|)>\<leqslant\>\<rho\><rsup|-2><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>>
    for any <math|x\<in\>\<Lambda\>> and <math|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<nu\>>>
    with <math|\<nu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1/3|)>> we obtain\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|1>|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|2>
      <around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      \<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>
      |<right|\<\|\|\>|1>>\<lesssim\><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|1>|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>
      \<rho\><rsup|-2><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,0|)>
      <around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      \<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>
      |<right|\<\|\|\>|1>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<rho\><rsup|-3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>1.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|A\<gtr\>\<gamma\>> by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:schauder-full>,
    we have

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h*<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<with|color|black|<around*|\<\|\|\>|Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>h*<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|h*<rsup|2>Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|i>2<rsup|-i
      A> <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>*\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>*<around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-2\<gamma\>><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    uniformly over <math|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>.
    Combining the above estimates we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>>O<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>*\<theta\>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>>*<around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>><rsup|3>.
    </equation*>

    Using Remark<nbsp><eqref|rem:weight-properties> a) and
    <math|B\<geqslant\>d+1> we get

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>> \<rho\><rsub|0><around*|(|t,0|)><rsup|4>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|0><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|0><around*|(|0,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>\<lesssim\>1.
    </equation*>

    Since

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|0>*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|i>2<rsup|-i
      A><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\>*<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>*\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>*<around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-2\<gamma\>><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>>,
    </equation*>

    we obtain

    \;

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>
      \<rho\><rsub|0><around*|(|t,0|)><rsup|4>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><around*|(|t|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>
      \<rho\><rsub|0><around*|(|t,0|)><rsup|4>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|h*\<rho\><rsup|-1><rsub|0><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)>><rsup|4>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|0>*Q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|4>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-4\<gamma\>>*<around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>><rsup|4>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <subsection|The vector model><label|sec:vector>

  In this final subsection, we discuss the modifications required to extend
  our results to the vector-valued model, where the field
  <math|\<phi\>=\<phi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>> takes values in
  the Euclidean space <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>> for some <math|n\<gtr\>1>. We
  denote by <math|<around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|a>|)><rsub|a\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>>>
  the components of the field <math|\<phi\>> in the canonical basis. The
  dynamics reads

  <\equation>
    \<cal-L\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<phi\><rsup|a>+\<lambda\>*<around*|\||\<phi\><rsup|>|\|><rsup|2>*\<phi\><rsup|a><rsup|>-r<rsub|>*\<phi\><rsup|a>=\<xi\><rsup|a>,<space|2em>a=1,\<ldots\>,n,<label|eq:dynamics-eps-vector>
  </equation>

  on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>>, where

  <\equation*>
    <around*|\||\<phi\>|\|><rsup|2><rsub|>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|a><around*|(|\<phi\><rsup|a>|)><rsup|2>.
  </equation*>

  Here

  <\equation*>
    \<xi\>=<around*|(|\<xi\><rsup|a>|)><rsub|a\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>>=<around*|(|\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>,a>|)><rsub|a\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>>
  </equation*>

  is a vector-valued, spacetime white noise on
  <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>> such that

  <\equation>
    \<bbb-E\><around*|[|\<xi\><rsup|a><around*|(|t,x|)>*\<xi\><rsup|b><around*|(|s,y|)>|]>=\<delta\><around*|(|t-s|)>*\<delta\><rsub|a,b>*\<bbb-1\><rsub|x=y>,<space|2em><around*|(|t,x|)>,<around*|(|s,y|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>,<space|1em>a,b=1,\<ldots\>,n.<label|eq:cov-noise-vector>
  </equation>

  <with|color|black|As before, we identify <math|\<phi\>> and <math|\<xi\>>
  with spatially periodic functions on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>.>\ 

  Our proof of the main result in the scalar-valued case extends
  straightforwardly to the vector-valued case. The main subtlety lies in
  obtaining the analogue of Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori> in this
  setting, which, however, follows directly from
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:partial-coercive-estimates> below. Beyond this
  adjustment, the subsequent analysis carries over with minimal changes, as
  it does not depend on the scalar nature of the equation until the
  classification of the relevant cumulants in
  Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:classification-of-relevant>. At that stage, one
  must exploit the <math|O<around*|(|n|)>>-symmetry of the
  noise<nbsp><eqref|eq:cov-noise-vector> to deduce that the cumulants are
  likewise symmetric. Consequently, the only contribution to the mass
  renormalisation is diagonal in the vector indices, and can therefore be
  absorbed into a redefinition of the renormalisation constant
  <math|r=r<rsub|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>.

  <section|A<nbsp>priori estimates><label|sec:apriori>

  This section is devoted to establishing weighted estimates for classical
  solutions of a fractional parabolic equation with a cubic coercive term. To
  the best of our knowledge, this result is new, although the proof closely
  follows the argument developed in the case of the standard Laplacian (see,
  for instance,<nbsp><cite|gubinelliGlobalSolutionsElliptic2019>).
  Furthermore, we present the estimates directly in a vector-valued setting,
  as no additional difficulties arise in this more general formulation.

  <\theorem>
    <label|thm:partial-coercive-estimates>Let <math|\<lambda\>\<gtr\>0>,
    <math|<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>\<less\>2s> and
    <math|u\<in\>C<rsub|t><rsup|1>C<rsub|x><rsup|2><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>|)>>
    be such that <math|<around*|\||\<zeta\><rsup|<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>>u|\|>>
    is a bounded function, where the weight <math|\<zeta\>> was introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights>. Then <math|u> belongs to the domain of
    the operator <math|\<partial\><rsub|t>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>>.
    Define <math|f\<in\>C<rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>|)>>
    by

    <\equation>
      f<rsup|a>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|t>u<rsup|a>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>u<rsup|a>+m<rsup|2>*u<rsup|a>+\<lambda\>*<around*|\||u|\|><rsup|2>*u<rsup|a>,<space|2em>a\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>,<label|eq:cubic-fractional>
    </equation>

    where <math|><math|<around*|\||u|\|><rsup|2><rsub|>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|a><around*|(|u<rsup|a>|)><rsup|2>>.\ 

    For any positive weight <math|\<rho\>\<in\>C<rsub|t><rsup|1>C<rsub|x><rsup|2><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|<with|color|black|0>>|)>>
    such that <math|>for some <math|<wide|\<nu\>|~>\<in\><around*|(|<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>,2s|)>>
    the functions <math|\<zeta\><rsup|-<wide|\<nu\>|~>>\<rho\>>,
    <math|\<zeta\><rsup|<wide|\<nu\>|~>>\<rho\><rsup|-1>> are bounded we have

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\>u|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>2\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>
      A<rsup|1/2>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3> <around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|<right|)|1>><rsup|1/3>,<label|eq:coercive-bound>
    </equation>

    where

    <\equation*>
      A\<assign\> <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<rho\><rsup|2>|\<\|\|\>>+
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      B\<assign\> <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\>u|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|><around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<rho\>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|2>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\><rsup|-1>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>|<right|)|1>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>u|)>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>
  </theorem>

  <\proof>
    We assume that <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+A+B\<less\>\<infty\>>
    as otherwise there is nothing to prove. For
    <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> and <math|L\<gtr\>0>, we define a convex
    function <math|\<Phi\>=\<Phi\><rsub|L,N>\<in\>C<around*|(|\<bbb-R\>|)>>
    by

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|\<Phi\><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>\<assign\><around*|(|\<eta\>-L|)><rsup|N><rsub|+>,<space|2em>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<eta\>|)>\<assign\>N*<around*|(|\<eta\>-L|)><rsup|N-1><rsub|+>,><space|2em>\<eta\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|\<Phi\><rprime|'>> denotes the derivative of <math|\<Phi\>>
    and <math|<around*|(|\<eta\>|)><rsub|+>\<assign\>\<bbb-1\><rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>0>\<eta\>>.
    We fix the parameter <math|N\<gtr\>1> such that
    <math|2N<around*|(|<wide|\<nu\>|~>-<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<gtr\>d+2s>.
    The parameter <math|L> will be fixed later. Let
    <math|<wide|u|^>\<assign\>\<rho\>u>. After
    testing<nbsp><eqref|eq:cubic-fractional> with
    <math|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)><wide|u|^><rsup|a>\<rho\><rsup|3>>
    and summing over <math|a\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>>, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      0=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsub|>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<around*|[|\<rho\><rsup|3>*<wide|u|^>\<cdot\>\<partial\><rsub|t>u+\<rho\><rsup|3>*<wide|u|^>*\<cdot\><around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>u+m<rsup|2>*\<rho\><rsup|2>*<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>+\<lambda\>*<around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|2>-\<rho\><rsup|3>*f\<cdot\><wide|u|^>|]>.
    </equation*>

    Observe that

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*\<rho\><rsup|3>*<wide|u|^>\<cdot\>\<partial\><rsub|t>u>|<cell|=>|<cell|<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<around*|[|\<rho\><rsup|2>\<partial\><rsub|t><around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>-<around*|(|\<rho\>*\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>*<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|[|\<rho\><rsup|2>\<partial\><rsub|t>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-<around*|(|\<rho\>*\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|-<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|[|\<partial\><rsub|t><around*|(|\<rho\><rsup|2>|)>*\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>+<around*|(|\<rho\>*\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|-<with|color|black|><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rsup|><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-<frac|1|2><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><around*|(|\<partial\><rsub|t>\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>*<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:est-apriori-laplacian> below,

    <\equation*>
      <big|sum><rsub|a><around*|\<langle\>|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a>,\<rho\><rsup|3>*<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>u<rsup|a>|\<rangle\>>\<geqslant\>-<frac|1|2><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>
      \<rho\><rsup|2>|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-<with|color|black|<wide|
      B|\<bar\>> <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>>
      <big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.
    </equation*>

    We also have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<langle\>|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>,m<rsup|2>
      \<rho\><rsup|2> <around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>+\<lambda\>*<around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|2>|\<rangle\>>>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<langle\>|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>,\<lambda\>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|2>|\<rangle\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|\<lambda\>
      N <around*|\<langle\>|<around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>-L|)><rsup|N-1><rsub|+>,<around*|(|<around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>-L|)><rsub|+>+L|)>
      L|\<rangle\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|\<lambda\>
      \ L<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rsup|><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>+\<lambda\>
      L<rsup|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>>>>>>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      -<around*|\<langle\>|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>,\<rho\><rsup|3>*f\<cdot\><wide|u|^>|\<rangle\>>\<geqslant\>-<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.
    </equation*>

    We conclude that

    <\equation*>
      0\<geqslant\><around*|[|\<lambda\>L-A|]><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>+<around*|<left|[|2>|\<lambda\>*L<rsup|2>-<around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|)>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>|<right|]|2>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Taking

    <\equation*>
      L\<gtr\>L<rsub|\<ast\>>\<assign\>max<around*|(|\<lambda\><rsup|-1>A,\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2><around*|[|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|]><rsup|1/2>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/2>|)>,
    </equation*>

    we deduce that

    <\equation*>
      <big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rsub|><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>=0,
    </equation*>

    which implies that <math|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>\<leqslant\>L>
    a.e. on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>. Thus,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<leqslant\>inf<rsub|L\<gtr\>L<rsub|\<ast\>>>
      L=L<rsub|\<ast\>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><rsup|-1>A+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2><around*|[|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|]><rsup|1/2><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/2>.
    </equation*>

    This implies that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>
      A<rsup|1/2>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/4>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/4>*<around*|[|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|]><rsup|1/4>.
    </equation*>

    By Young's inequality, we have

    <\equation*>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-1/4>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|1/4>*<around*|[|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|]><rsup|1/4>\<leqslant\><frac|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>|4>+<frac|3|4>*\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3>*<around*|[|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|]><rsup|1/3>,
    </equation*>

    and hence

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>2\<lambda\><rsup|-1/2>A<rsup|1/2>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1/3>*<around*|[|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|3>f|\<\|\|\>>+B|]><rsup|1/3>,
    </equation*>

    as claimed.
  </proof>

  The following lemma completes the proof.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:est-apriori-laplacian>Suppose that
    <math|u\<in\>C<rsub|t><rsup|1>C<rsub|x><rsup|2><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>,\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>|)>>
    is such that <math|<around*|\||\<zeta\><rsup|<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>>u|\|>>
    is a bounded function for some <math|<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>\<less\>2s> and
    <math|\<rho\>\<in\>C<rsub|t><rsup|1>C<rsub|x><rsup|2><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>>
    is a positive weight such that <math|>for some
    <math|<wide|\<nu\>|~>\<in\><around*|(|<wide|\<nu\>|\<bar\>>,2s|)>> the
    functions <math|\<zeta\><rsup|-<wide|\<nu\>|~>>\<rho\>>,
    <math|\<zeta\><rsup|<wide|\<nu\>|~>>\<rho\><rsup|-1>> are bounded. Let
    <math|\<Phi\>=\<Phi\><rsub|L,N>\<in\>C<around*|(|\<bbb-R\>|)>> with
    <math|N\<gtr\>1> fixed as in the proof of the above lemma and arbitrary
    <math|L\<gtr\>0>. Then we have

    <\equation*>
      <big|sum><rsub|a><around*|\<langle\>|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a>,\<rho\><rsup|3>*<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>u<rsup|a>|\<rangle\>>\<geqslant\>-<frac|1|2><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>
      \<rho\><rsup|2>|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-<with|color|black|<wide|B|\<bar\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>><rsup|><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.
    </equation*>

    where <math|<wide|u|^>\<assign\>\<rho\>u> and

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<wide|B|\<bar\>>\<assign\>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|><around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<rho\>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|2>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\><rsup|-1>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>>|<right|)|1>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|<wide|u|^>|)>|\<\|\|\>>.>
    </equation*>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Leaving the sum over <math|a> implicit we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<bbb-X\>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|<around*|\<langle\>|\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a>,\<rho\><rsup|3><around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>u<rsup|a>|\<rangle\>>>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|3><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|u<rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>-u<rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|)>>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>-<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|)>>|<cell|<around*|(|\<backassign\><around*|(|\<bbb-I\>|)>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>*u<rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>>|<cell|<around*|(|\<backassign\><around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>|)>|)>>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Let <math|V<rsub|\<tau\>>\<assign\>\<tau\>*<wide|u|^><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>+<around*|(|1-\<tau\>|)>*<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>>.
    Since <math|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>\<mapsto\>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||V<rsub|\<tau\>>|\|><rsup|2>|)>>
    is a convex function (as a composition of a convex function with an
    affine one),

    <\equation*>
      \<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||V<rsub|1>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||V<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|2>|)>\<geqslant\><around*|\<nobracket\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<tau\>>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||V<rsub|\<tau\>>|\|><rsup|2>|)>|\|><rsub|\<tau\>=0>,
    </equation*>

    that is,

    <\equation*>
      \<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>\<geqslant\>2*\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<big|sum><rsub|a><wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Using the above inequality we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<bbb-I\>>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|[|\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>-\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>**<around*|[|\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>-\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|-<frac|1|2><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>
      \<rho\><rsup|2>|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where the equality in the second line follows by an integration by parts
    of the fractional Laplacian, which is a symmetric operator in
    <math|L<rsup|2>>. Let us now consider
    <math|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>|)>> and split it as follows

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>*\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>**<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z|)>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>*\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>*\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z|)>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<mathd\>z*\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)>*\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z|)>*<around*|(|\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|)>
      <around*|(|<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-<wide|u|^><rsup|a><around*|(|z|)>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>|)>+<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|2>|)>+<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|3>|)>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    For <math|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>|)>> we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|-<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\>*<around*|(|-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|s>\<rho\>|\<\|\|\>>*<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Next,

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|2>|)>>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|-<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>*<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^><around*|(|z|)>|\|><rsup|2>|)>*\<rho\><rsup|2><around*|(|z|)><around*|(|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|\||\<rho\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><around*|(|z|)>|\|>*<around*|\||\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<rho\><rsup|-1><around*|(|z|)>|\|>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|-<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>**<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|2>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\><rsup|-1>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Finally, using the Cauchy\USchwarz inequality, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|3>|)>>|<cell|\<geqslant\>>|<cell|-<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|u|^>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsup|>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|\<rho\>|)>\<frak-D\><rsub|s><around*|(|<wide|u|^>|)>|\<\|\|\>>*<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<Phi\><rprime|'><around*|(|<around*|\||<wide|u|^>|\|><rsup|2>|)>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Since <math|<around*|(|\<bbb-X\>|)>\<geqslant\><around*|(|\<bbb-I\>|)>+<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>|)>+<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|2>|)>+<around*|(|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|3>|)>>,
    our claim is proved.
  </proof>

  <section|Analysis of the flow equation><label|sec:flow>

  In this section, we prove Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force>,
  which asserts the existence of an approximate solution to the flow
  equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-eq-sec2> for the effective force
  <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>>>, with
  well-controlled bounds encoded by<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>. These bounds are
  achievable only because we can \Ptune\Q the boundary
  condition<nbsp><eqref|eq:final-cond-f> using the <math|\<varepsilon\>>- and
  <math|M>-dependent renormalisation term <math|r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>>.

  Conceptually, we are dealing with a random bilinear equation whose solution
  is analysed via the evolution equation for its cumulants. The flow equation
  for cumulants has a similar structure to the flow equation for the
  effective force and propagates comparable bounds backwards from the final
  condition at <math|\<sigma\>=1>, except in a low-dimensional (so-called
  relevant) subspace, where the bounds must be propagated forwards from small
  to large <math|\<sigma\>>. This procedure requires tuning an appropriate
  final condition so that the solution lies on a trajectory with controlled
  bounds. To simplify this tuning, we decompose the flow equation to reduce
  the relevant subspace to one dimension.

  Once bounds for the cumulants are established, a Kolmogorov-type argument
  allows us to deduce pathwise bounds on the effective force. The section
  concludes with a technical \Ppost-processing\Q step, which extracts the
  coercive term essential for the global a priori estimates and verifies the
  conditions<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>.

  <subsection|Random flow equation><label|sec:random-flow>

  To study approximate solutions <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>>
  of the flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-eq-sec2> we need to set up the
  appropriate spaces. Recall that

  <\equation*>
    \<cal-E\><rsup|>\<assign\><big|cap><rsub|\<alpha\>\<gtr\>0>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>,\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>>|)>,<space|2em><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|t>\<cal-E\>.
  </equation*>

  As we shall argue, the flow equation can be approximatively solved in the
  space <math|\<cal-P\><around*|(|\<cal-E\>|)>> of polynomial functionals on
  <math|\<cal-E\>> with values in <math|<wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>. We say that a
  functional <math|F> belongs to <math|\<cal-P\><around*|(|\<cal-E\>|)>> if
  for some <math|<wide|k|\<bar\>>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> there exist kernels
  <math|<around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>>|)><rsub|k\<in\><around*|{|0,\<ldots\>,<wide|k|\<bar\>>|}>>>
  of operators <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>
  <math|>such that

  <\equation*>
    F<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>=<big|sum><rsub|k=0><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>F<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>=<big|sum><rsub|k=0><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|k>>F<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|\<bullet\>;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>
    \<phi\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>\<cdots\>\<phi\><around*|(|z<rsub|k>|)>\<in\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>,
  </equation*>

  for all <math|\<phi\>\<in\>\<cal-E\>>. In order to construct a suitable
  approximate solution of<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-eq-sec2> we introduce a formal
  parameter <math|\<hbar\>> and make the ansatz

  <\equation*>
    <lsup|\<hbar\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>>=<big|sum><rsub|\<ell\>\<geqslant\>0>\<hbar\><rsup|\<ell\>>
    F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>>.
  </equation*>

  Moreover, we assume that the finial condition is of the form

  <\equation*>
    <with|color|black|<lsup|\<hbar\>>F<around*|(|\<phi\>|)>=-\<lambda\>*\<phi\><rsup|3><rsup|>-<lsup|\<hbar\>>r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>*\<phi\>+\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>,<space|2em><lsup|\<hbar\>>r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>=<wide|r|\<bar\>>+<big|sum><rsub|\<ell\>\<geqslant\>0>\<hbar\><rsup|\<ell\>>
    r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M><rsup|>.>
  </equation*>

  We are led to look for solutions of the
  <with|font-shape|italic|perturbative flow equation>

  <\equation>
    \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><lsup|\<hbar\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>>+\<hbar\>\<mathD\><lsup|\<hbar\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><lsup|\<hbar\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=0,<space|2em><lsup|\<hbar\>>F<rsub|1>=<lsup|\<hbar\>>F,<label|eq:pert-flow>
  </equation>

  in the space of <math|\<cal-P\><around*|(|\<cal-E\>|)><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<hbar\>|\<rrbracket\>>>
  of formal power series in <math|\<hbar\>> with coefficients in
  <math|\<cal-P\><around*|(|\<cal-E\>|)>>. This setup has the advantage that
  now the flow equation has a unique global solution which can be determined
  by induction on the degree <math|\<hbar\>>. An approximate solution
  to<nbsp><eqref|lem:estimates-DF> is obtained by fixing an integer
  <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>0> and letting

  <\equation*>
    F<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|\<ell\>=0><rsup|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>>.
  </equation*>

  The choice of value for <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>> will be discussed in
  Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing> below. We observe that, thanks
  to<nbsp><eqref|eq:pert-flow>, this truncation implies the existence of a
  maximal polynomial order <math|<wide|k|\<bar\>>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> in
  the fields for the kernels. We decompose the force as

  <\equation*>
    F<rsub|\<mu\> ><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>=<big|sum><rsup|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<ell\>=0>F<rsub|\<mu\>
    ><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>=
    <big|sum><rsup|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<ell\>=0><big|sum><rsub|k=0><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>F<rsub|\<mu\>
    ><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>,
  </equation*>

  where <math|\<ell\>> measures the perturbative order in <math|\<hbar\>>
  while <math|k> the polynomial degree in <math|\<phi\>>.

  Let us now introduce a condensed notation to manipulate these kernels. Let

  <\equation*>
    \<frak-A\>\<assign\><around*|{|<around*|(|\<ell\>,k|)><mid|\|>0\<leqslant\>\<ell\>\<leqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>,0\<leqslant\>k\<leqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>|}>.
  </equation*>

  For <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>> with
  <math|\<frak-a\>=<around*|(|\<ell\>,k|)>> we let
  <math|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<assign\>k> ,
  <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<assign\>\<ell\>> and write

  <\equation>
    <around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<assign\>-\<alpha\>+\<delta\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<beta\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>,<label|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>
  </equation>

  for suitable positive parameters <math|\<alpha\>,\<delta\>> and
  <math|\<beta\>> whose value will be fixed later. We say that a kernel
  <math|>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\equation*>
      F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>\<assign\>F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>
    </equation*>

    is <with|font-shape|italic|relevant> if
    <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>,
    <with|font-shape|italic|marginal> if <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>=0>
    and <with|font-shape|italic|irrelevant> if
    <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>. We refer to <math|z> as the
    <with|font-shape|italic|output> variable, and to
    <math|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>> as the
    <with|font-shape|italic|input> variables of the kernel
    <math|F<rsup|<with|font|Euler|a>><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>>.
    To simplify the notation, we usually ignore the fact that the kernel
    <math|F<rsup|<with|font|Euler|a>><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>>
    is generally not well-defined pointwise in the output variable <math|z>.
  </with>

  <subsection|Norms for kernels>

  To introduce suitable norms for the effective force kernels

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>,
  </equation*>

  we first need some notations and preliminary definitions for weights and
  smoothing operators.

  <\definition>
    We denote by <math|St<around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>|)>> the
    Steiner diameter of the set <math|<around*|{|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>|}>>
    with respect to the parabolic distance introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:distance>, <with|color|black|<with|font-shape|italic|<with|font-shape|italic|i.e.>>
    the minimum over lengths of trees with nodes at the points
    <math|<around*|{|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>|}>> and possibly other
    points <math|<around*|{|z<rsub|1><rprime|'>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m><rprime|'>|}>>>.
  </definition>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\remark>
      <label|rem:steiner>Our fractional parabolic
      distance<nbsp><eqref|eq:dist-parabolic> satisfies the triangle
      inequality

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||z<rsub|1>+z<rsub|2>|\|><rsub|s>\<leqslant\><around*|\||z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>+<around*|\||z<rsub|2>|\|><rsub|s>,<space|2em>z<rsub|1>,z<rsub|2>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>.
      </equation*>

      Moreover, for <math|n\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>,m\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>n-1|}>>
      and <math|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>>, the
      Steiner diameter satisfies

      <\equation*>
        St<around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>|)>\<leqslant\>St<around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>,z|)>+St<around*|(|z,z<rsub|m+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>|)>,
      </equation*>

      which, noting that <math|St<around*|(|z<rsub|1>,z<rsub|2>|)>=<around*|\||z<rsub|1>-z<rsub|2>|\|><rsub|s>>,
      can be seen as a generalisation of the triangle inequality for the
      fractional parabolic distance.
    </remark>
  </with>

  <\definition>
    <label|def:weights-kernels>Let <math|\<flat\>\<in\><around*|(|1,2s|)>> be
    a constant close to <math|2s> and <math|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<flat\>/<around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>|)>>
    be a small constant, to be fixed later.

    <\enumerate-alpha>
      <item>For <math|m\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+ >> and
      <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>, the weight
      <math|w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\> >\<in\>
      C<rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>>|)>> is
      defined by

      <\equation*>
        w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>
        ><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>St<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>,<space|2em>z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>.
      </equation*>

      <with|color|black|We write <math|><math|w<rsup|<around*|(|1|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >=1\<in\>C<rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|>|)>>.>

      <item>For <math|m\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>, the weight
      <math|v<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>><rsub|\<mu\> >\<in\>
      C<rsup|\<infty\>><rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>>|)>>
      is defined by\ 

      <\equation*>
        v<rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><rsub|\<mu\>
        ><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)>\<assign\>v<rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>.z,<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>.z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>.z<rsub|m>|)>,
      </equation*>

      where <math|v<rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><rsub| >\<in\>
      C<rsup|\<infty\>><rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>>,<around*|[|0,1|]>|)>>
      is a fixed function such that

      <\equation*>
        v<rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)>=<around*|{|<tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|1>|<cell|if>|<cell|St<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)>\<leqslant\>1,>>|<row|<cell|0>|<cell|if>|<cell|St<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)>\<geqslant\>2.>>>>>|\<nobracket\>>
      </equation*>

      <with|color|black|We write <math|><math|v<rsup|<around*|(|1|)>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >=1\<in\>C<rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|>|)>>.>

      <item>The weight <math|\<frak-o\>\<in\>
      C<rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|>|)>> is defined by

      <\equation*>
        \<frak-o\><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\>\<zeta\><around*|(|z|)><rsup|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>=<around*|\<langle\>|z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>,<application-space|2em>z\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>.
      </equation*>

      <item>For <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>>, we write

      <\equation*>
        w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<space|2em><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>,\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<space|2em>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>v<rsup|<around*|(|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<space|2em>\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<assign\>\<frak-o\><rsup|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsup|>.<rsup|>
      </equation*>

      <item>For <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>,> the weight
      <math|h<rsub|\<mu\> >\<in\> C<rsup|><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsup|2><rsub|0>|)>>
      is defined by

      <\equation*>
        h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rprime|'>|)>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>|)><rsup|-1>.
      </equation*>
    </enumerate-alpha>
  </definition>

  <\with|color|black>
    Recall that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<langle\>|z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||z<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/s>+<around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/2>.
    </equation*>

    The weights <math|w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> and
    \ <math|<wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsub|>> will control the
    approximate localisation of the effective force kernels
    <math|F<rsup|<with|font|Euler|a>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>>
    <math|>near the diagonal <math|<around*|{|z=z<rsub|1>=\<cdots\>=z<rsub|k>|}>>.
    The weights <math|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>> will instead be used to
    control the growth at spacetime infinity of the kernels in the output
    variable <math|z>, reflecting the corresponding growth inherited from the
    white noise. These three families of weights are constructed to be
    compatible with the estimates for the bilinear terms appearing in the
    flow equation, as detailed in the lemma below. The additional weights
    <math|v<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><rsub|>> and
    <math|h<rsub|\<mu\>>> will be used only in intermediate estimates and
    play an auxiliary role. Some of their useful properties are summarised in
    Appendix<nbsp><reference|sec:weight-properties>. Finally, observe that

    <\equation*>
      w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><around*|(|z,z<rprime|'>|)>=w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rprime|'>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> is the weight introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weight-w>. The exponent
    <math|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>
    in the definition of the weight <math|<wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>
    is designed in such a way that the bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-o> below
    holds true.
  </with>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:weight-factorization>For all
      <math|\<frak-a\>,\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>> be such
      that<math|<rsub|>> <math|k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>+k<around*|(|\<frak-c\>|)>=k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+1>
      and <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-c\>|)>=\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1>,
      the bounds

      <\equation>
        w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>\<lesssim\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsup|><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>-1>,<wide|z|^>|)>
        w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|<wide|z|^><rsub|>-<wide|z|~>|)>
        w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>,<label|eq:weight-w>
      </equation>

      <\equation>
        \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>
        <wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>\<lesssim\>\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-b\>><around*|(|z|)><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsup|><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>-1>,<wide|z|^>|)>
        w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|<wide|z|^><rsub|>-<wide|z|~>|)>
        \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~>|)>
        <wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>,<label|eq:weight-w-o>
      </equation>

      hold uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> and
      <math|><math|z,<wide|z|^>,<wide|z|~>,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>>.
      For all <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>> such that
      <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>>,
      the bounds

      <\equation>
        \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>\<lesssim\><around*|(|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>|)><rsup|-1>
        \ \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>\<lesssim\>w<rsup|2-\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>
        \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>,<label|eq:weight-o>
      </equation>

      <\equation>
        w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>\<lesssim\>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z<rsub|1><rprime|'>|)>\<ldots\>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>-z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rprime|'>|)>
        w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>,<label|eq:weight-w-2>
      </equation>

      <\equation>
        \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>
        <wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>\<lesssim\>w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z<rsub|1><rprime|'>|)>\<ldots\>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>-z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rprime|'>|)>
        \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>
        <wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>,<label|eq:weight-w-o-2>
      </equation>

      hold uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> and
      <math|><math|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>,z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|0>>.
    </lemma>

    <\proof>
      To prove the claim we apply iteratively the inequalities from
      Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:steiner> and use the bounds

      <\equation*>
        1+<big|sum><rsub|i\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>>a<rsub|i>\<leqslant\><big|prod><rsub|i\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n|}>><around*|(|1+a<rsub|i>|)>,<space|2em><around*|(|1+a<rsub|i>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>\<leqslant\><around*|(|1+a<rsub|i>|)><rsup|<wide|\<omega\>|\<bar\>>>,
      </equation*>

      valid for all <math|a<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,a<rsub|n>\<geqslant\>0> and
      <math|0\<leqslant\>\<omega\>\<leqslant\><wide|\<omega\>|\<bar\>>>. To
      prove<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-o> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-2>, we use
      furthermore that

      <\equation*>
        <around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\>\<flat\>\<leqslant\>2-\<flat\>,
      </equation*>

      which holds because <math|\<flat\>\<gtr\>1>.
    </proof>
  </with>

  <\definition>
    <label|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>For
    <math|n,m\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>,\<eta\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> we set

    <\equation*>
      K<rsup|n,m><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>1<rsup|\<otimes\>n>\<otimes\><around*|(|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>m>,<application-space|2em>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|n,m>\<assign\>1<rsup|\<otimes\>n>\<otimes\><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>m>,<space|2em>K<rsup|n,m><rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>\<assign\>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|n,m>*K<rsup|n,m><rsub|\<eta\>>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      <wide|K|~><rsup|n,m><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>K<rsup|\<otimes\>n><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<otimes\><around*|(|K<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>m>,<space|2em><wide|L|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|n,m>\<assign\>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<otimes\>n>\<otimes\><around*|(|L<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>m>,<space|2em><wide|K|~><rsup|n,m><rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>\<assign\><wide|L|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|n,m>*<wide|K|~><rsup|n,m><rsub|\<eta\>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>>
    are introduced in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels>. Given
    <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>>, we write

    <\equation*>
      <wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><wide|K|~><rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>=K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>K<rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>.
    </equation*>
  </definition>

  <\definition>
    <label|def:norm-kernels>The norm of a kernel <math|F> associated with an
    operator <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k>\<rightarrow\>\<cal-E\>> is
    defined by

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F|\<\|\|\>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|z\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|k>><around*|\||F<around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>|\|>
      .<label|eq:basic-norm>
    </equation>

    Given weights <math|\<frak-o\>\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0>|)>>
    and <math|w\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|1+k>|)>>, we write

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<around*|(|\<frak-o\>\<cdot\><rsup|>F\<cdot\>w|)><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>\<assign\>\<frak-o\><around*|(|z|)>
      F<around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>
      w<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>.>
    </equation*>

    Let <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>>. The norm of a kernel
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>> of an operator
    <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>
    <math|>at scale <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> is defined by

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>>
    denotes the convolution of <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>>, viewed as an
    element of <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>>,
    with the kernel of <math|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>. We
    further introduce a norm for the family of effective force kernels

    <\equation*>
      F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>\<assign\><around*|(|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>,
    </equation*>

    defined by

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<assign\><around*|[|sup<rsub|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>>
      sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<vee\><around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|d/2+s+2\<kappa\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>,<label|eq:norm-family-F>
    </equation>

    where <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>> is defined
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>.
  </definition>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\remark>
      An inspection of our parameter choices discussed in
      Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:bounds-on-parameters>
      and<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing>, together
      with<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>, shows that
      <math|><math|<around*|[|<around*|(|0,0|)>|]>\<less\>-d/2-s-2\<kappa\>>.
      Consequently, the second term on the right-hand side
      of<nbsp><eqref|eq:norm-family-F> provides a stronger bound on
      <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>
      than the first term. For technical reasons, this stronger control will
      be required in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing> to establish
      the estimates stated in<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>.
    </remark>
  </with>

  <\remark>
    <label|rem:norm0-scale-monotonicity>By Young's inequality,
    <eqref|eq:weight-w-o-2> and Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>, we
    have

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>><wide|K|~><rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>>>><label|eq:norm-mon>
    </equation>

    uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>.
  </remark>

  <\with|color|black>
    Given kernels <math|F<rsub|><rprime|'>> and <math|F<rprime|''>> of
    operators <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<rprime|'>>\<rightarrow\>\<cal-E\>>
    and <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<rprime|''>>\<rightarrow\>\<cal-E\>>
    respectively, we denote by

    <\equation>
      F=\<frak-C\><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|F<rprime|'><rsub|>\<otimes\>
      F<rprime|''>|)><label|eq:frak-B-operator>
    </equation>

    the kernel of the operator <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k>\<rightarrow\>\<cal-E\>>,
    with <math|k=k<rprime|'>+k<rprime|''>-1>, defined by

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|F<around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|k>|)>>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<assign\><frac|1|k!><big|sum><rsub|\<pi\>\<in\><with|font|cal|P><rsub|k>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|2>>>|<cell|F<rprime|'><rsub|><around*|(|z;\<mathd\>z<rsub|\<pi\><around*|(|1|)>>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|\<pi\><around*|(|k<rprime|'>-1|)>>,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>
      <wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>-z<rprime|''>|)>
      F<rprime|''><around*|(|z<rprime|''>;\<mathd\>z<rsub|\<pi\><around*|(|k<rprime|'>|)>>,\<cdots\>,\<mathd\>z<rsub|\<pi\><around*|(|k|)>>|)>
      \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|''>,>>>>><label|eq:def-B-general>
    </equation>

    where <math|<with|font|cal|P><rsub|k>> denotes the set of permutations of
    <math|<around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,k|}>> and the integral is over the variables
    <math|z<rprime|'>> and<nbsp><math|z<rprime|''>>. Note that
    <math|<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
    applies <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> to the output variable of
    the kernel <math|F<rprime|''>> and plugs the result to the last input
    variable of the kernel <math|F<rprime|'>>. \ The above definition extends
    naturally to kernels of operators <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<rprime|'>>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>
    and <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<rprime|''>>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>.\ 

    The flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:pert-flow> for the effective force can
    be rewritten as the following flow equation for the kernels

    <\equation>
      \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>=<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>>B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>|)>,<application-space|2em>F<rsub|1><rsup|\<frak-a\>>=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>,<label|eq:flow-kernels>
    </equation>

    where the operators <math|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>>>
    are implicitly defined by

    <\equation>
      <big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>>B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|\<ell\><rprime|'>=0><rsup|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|>|)>-1><big|sum><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|k<rprime|'>=0><around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>
      \<frak-C\><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<otimes\>
      F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>|)><label|eq:B-form>
    </equation>

    and in particular <math|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>>=0>
    unless\ 

    \;

    <\equation>
      <choice|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|c>|<table|<row|<cell|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|>|)>=<space|0.2spc>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-c\><rsub|>|)>+1,>>|<row|<cell|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=<space|0.2spc>k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>+k<around*|(|\<frak-c\>|)>-1,>>|<row|<cell|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>+<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>+<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>=-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>.>>>>><label|eq:link-between-homogeneities-kernels>
    </equation>
  </with>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimate-B-kernels>For all
    <math|\<frak-a\>,\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>>, the following
    bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>-<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>-1>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>, provided

    <\equation>
      2s-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>\<geqslant\>0.<label|eq:constraint-flow-kernels>
    </equation>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    <\with|color|black>
      By Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels>
      and<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>, together
      with <eqref|eq:B-form>, <eqref|eq:def-B-general> and the identity
      <math|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>=1>, we obtain

      <\eqnarray*>
        <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>,<around*|\||<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>,<around*|\||<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>|)>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>
      </eqnarray*>

      Hence, by <eqref|eq:weight-w-o>, <eqref|eq:B-form>,
      <eqref|eq:def-B-general>, Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels> and
      Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>, we arrive at

      <\eqnarray*>
        <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>,\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-b\>>\<cdot\><around*|\||<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>,\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-c\>>\<cdot\><around*|\||<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>|)>|]>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-b\>>\<cdot\><around*|\||<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-b\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-c\>>\<cdot\><around*|\||<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-c\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>
      </eqnarray*>
    </with>

    Moreover, combining<nbsp><eqref|eq:link-between-homogeneities-kernels>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:constraint-flow-kernels> yields

    <\equation*>
      -<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>+2s-1=-<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>-<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s-1\<geqslant\>-<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>-<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>-1.
    </equation*>

    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Norms for cumulants>

  In order to prove probabilistic bounds for the moments of the norm
  <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>>, we start by
  establishing bounds for the cumulants of the family
  <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>>
  of the effective force kernels. To this end, let us first introduce a
  useful notation. For

  <\equation*>
    \<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>\<assign\><around*|{|<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<frak-a\><rsub|n>|)><mid|\|>\<frak-a\><rsub|k>\<in\>\<frak-A\>,L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|}>,
  </equation*>

  we write\ 

  <\equation*>
    n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<assign\>n,<space|2em>L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<assign\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>|)>+\<cdots\>+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|n>|)>,<space|2em>K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<assign\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>|)>+\<cdots\>+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|n>|)>.
  </equation*>

  <with|color|black|We denote by <math|\<frak-K\><rsub|n><around*|(|X<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,X<rsub|n>|)>>
  the <math|n>-th order joint cumulant of the random variable
  <math|X<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,X<rsub|n>>.> For
  <math|\<b-a\>=<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,\<frak-a\><rsub|n>|)>\<in\>\<b-A\>>
  and <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>, we use the following
  shorthand notation

  <\equation*>
    \<cal-F\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|n>|)>\<assign\>\<frak-K\><rsub|n><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|1>|)>,\<cdots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|n>><around*|(|z<rsub|n>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|n>|)>|)>,
  </equation*>

  where

  <\equation>
    Z<rsub|i>=<around*|(|z<rsub|i,1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|i,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>><rsup|>,<space|2em>i\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>n|}>,<space|1em>n=n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>,<label|eq:notation-Z>
  </equation>

  are the input variables of the <math|i>-th effective force kernel involved
  in the joint cumulant. Since <math|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>>>
  is a kernel of an operator <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^>>,
  it is natural to view <math|\<cal-F\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>> as a
  kernel of an operator

  <\equation>
    \<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>\<rightarrow\><wide|\<cal-E\>|^><rsup|\<otimes\>n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>.<label|eq:operator-cumulant>
  </equation>

  We define the global homogeneity of the kernel
  <math|\<cal-F\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>> as\ 

  <\equation*>
    <around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<assign\>-\<varrho\>+n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)><around*|(|\<theta\>+\<alpha\>|)>+<around*|[|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>|]>+\<cdots\>+<around*|[|\<frak-a\><rsub|n>|]>,
  </equation*>

  for suitable parameters <math|\<varrho\>> and <math|\<theta\>> whose values
  will be fixed in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:bounds-on-parameters>.
  By<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>, we have

  <\equation>
    <around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>*n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+\<delta\>*L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+\<beta\>*K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>.<label|eq:homogenity-cum>
  </equation>

  We say that a cumulant <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>> is
  <with|font-shape|italic|relevant> if <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<less\>0>,
  <with|font-shape|italic|marginal> if <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=0> and
  <with|font-shape|italic|irrelevant> if <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>.

  <\definition>
    For <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> and <math|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>
    we define

    <\equation*>
      w<rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>\<assign\><big|otimes><rsub|i=1><rsup|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>>w<rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>,<application-space|2em>K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><big|otimes><rsub|i=1><rsup|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>>K<rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<space|2em>L<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\><big|otimes><rsub|i=1><rsup|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>>L<rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,<space|2em>K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>,\<sigma\>>\<assign\>L<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|w<rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>> is introduced
    in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>, and
    <math|K<rsup|1,k><rsub|\<mu\>>> and <math|L<rsup|1,k><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    are introduced in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>
  </definition>

  The space of cumulants is endowed with the norm
  <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|>> defined by
  taking <math|L<rsup|\<infty\>>> norm on the first output variable and the
  total variation norm in all other variables, with the output variables
  restricted to the first period in space. The restriction of the integration
  of the output variables to the first period is natural since
  cumulants<math|> are kernels of operators acting between spaces of periodic
  functions, cf.<nbsp><eqref|eq:operator-cumulant>.

  <\definition>
    <label|def:norm-cumulants>Let <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>>,
    <math|n=n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>> and <math|k=K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>. The
    norm of a kernel <math|\<cal-F\><rsub|><rsup|\<b-a\>>> associated with an
    operator <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>k>\<rightarrow\>\<cal-E\><rsup|\<otimes\>n*>>
    is defined by

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsub|><rsup|\<b-a\>>|\<interleave\>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|z<rsub|1>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|n-1><rsub|M>><around*|(|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|k>><around*|\||\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|n>|)>|\|>|)>
      \<mathd\>z<rsub|2>\<cdots\>\<mathd\>z<rsub|n>,<label|eq:basic-norm-cumulant>
    </equation>

    with the notation as in<nbsp><eqref|eq:notation-Z>. Given a weight
    <math|w\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|n+k>|)>>, we write

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<around*|(|F\<cdot\>w|)><around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|n>|)>\<assign\>
      \<cal-F\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|n>,\<mathd\>Z<rsub|n>|)>
      w<around*|(|z<rsub|1>,Z<rsub|1>,\<cdots\>,z<rsub|n>,Z<rsub|n>|)>.>
    </equation*>

    The norm of <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>> <math|>at scale
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> is defined by

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>>,<label|eq:cumulant-norms-mu>
    </equation>

    where <math|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>>
    denotes the convolution of <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>>, viewed as an
    element of <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsup|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>|)>>,
    with the kernel of <math|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>. We
    further introduce a norm for the family of cumulants of effective force
    kernels

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>\<assign\><around*|(|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
    </equation*>

    defined by

    \;

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>>
      <around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]><rsup|1/n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>.<label|eq:norm-family-cumulants>
    </equation>

    \;
  </definition>

  <\remark>
    <label|rem:norm-scale-monotonicity>Analogously to
    Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:norm0-scale-monotonicity>, by
    <math|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>
    K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>>, Young's
    inequality,<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-2> and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>, we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>\<comma\>\<sigma\>>K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>><rsup|K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>.
  </remark>

  In Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:concl-of-cumul-analysis>, we will pass from
  estimates on the norm <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>>
  for the family of cumulants to estimates on the norm
  <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>> for the corresponding
  family of kernels, using a Kolmogorov-type argument.
  Following<nbsp><cite|duchFlowEquationApproach2021|duchRenormalizationSingularElliptic2022>,
  we introduce a flow equation for cumulants, which will allow us to control
  the norm <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>>.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:flow-cumulants>The cumulants satisfy the following flow
    equation:

    <\equation>
      \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=<big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>
      ><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+<big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>,<label|eq:cumulant-flow>
    </equation>

    where the multilinear operators <math|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>>>
    and <math|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>> are defined in
    Appendix<nbsp><reference|sec:A-B-cumulants>. We have
    <with|color|black|<math|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>>=0> unless>

    <\equation>
      <choice|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|c>|<table|<row|<cell|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=n<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>-1,<space|0.2spc><space|0.2spc>>>|<row|<cell|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=L<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>+1,>>|<row|<cell|K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=K<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>-1,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=<around*|[|\<b-b\>|]>-\<theta\>+\<delta\>-\<beta\>,>>>>><label|eq:characterization-a>
    </equation>

    and <with|color|black|<math|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>=0>
    unless>

    <\equation>
      <choice|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|c>|<table|<row|<cell|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=n<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>+n<around*|(|\<b-c\>|)>-1,<space|0.2spc><space|0.2spc>>>|<row|<cell|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=L<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>+L<around*|(|\<b-c\>|)>+1,>>|<row|<cell|K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=K<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>+K<around*|(|\<b-c\>|)>-1,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=<around*|[|\<b-b\>|]>+<around*|[|\<b-c\>|]>+\<varrho\>-\<theta\>+\<delta\>-\<beta\>.>>>>><label|eq:characterization-b>
    </equation>

    Moreover, the operators <math|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>>> and
    <math|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>> satisfy the
    following bounds:

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-1>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,<with|font-series|bold|c>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|c>|]>-1>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    provided the following compatibility conditions hold:

    <\equation>
      \<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>-d\<geqslant\>0,<application-space|2em>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s\<geqslant\>0.<label|eq:compatibility>
    </equation>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    The derivation of the flow equation is a direct consequence of the
    definition of cumulants, see<nbsp><cite|duchFlowEquationApproach2021|duchRenormalizationSingularElliptic2022>.
    The explicit form of the operators is not essential for the subsequent
    discussion and is provided in Appendix<nbsp><reference|sec:A-B-cumulants>,
    where the stated bounds are also proved (see
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-A> and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-B>).
  </proof>

  This general structure of the flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>
  allows us to propagate estimates for the cumulants of the form

  <\equation*>
    sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<less\>\<infty\>.
  </equation*>

  However, depending on the sign of <math|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>,
  we shall handle differently the cumulants: in particular, for
  <math|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>\<gtr\>0>, namely for
  irrelevant cumulants, the flow equation can be solved
  <with|font-shape|italic|backward> starting from the final condition at
  <math|\<sigma\>=1>. On the other hand, this approach does not work for
  cumulants for which <math|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>\<less\>0>
  as in this case the flow equation cannot be integrated close to
  <math|\<sigma\>=1>. As we shall see in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:induction>,
  we will solve the flow equation for this class of cumulants, called
  <em|relevant cumulants>, by integrating it <em|forward>.

  <\remark>
    <label|rem:symmetries>Before proceeding with the analysis of the flow
    equations for cumulants, we record a few remarks about symmetries. First,
    we observe that the SPDE under consideration,
    namely<nbsp><eqref|eq:dynamcs-eps-M>, is invariant under the
    transformation

    <\equation*>
      \<phi\>\<mapsto\>-\<phi\>,<space|2em>\<xi\>\<mapsto\>-\<xi\>,
    </equation*>

    which also preserves the law of the noise
    <math|\<xi\>=\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>. By the
    discussion in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:bounds-on-parameters>, \ this
    invariance implies that <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0>
    for all <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>> and
    <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> such that <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0> and

    <\equation*>
      n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<in\>2\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>+1.
    </equation*>

    <\with|color|black>
      <with|font-series|bold|>To extend this property to higher levels
      <math|><math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0>, we exploit the fact that
      it is preserved by the flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>
      thanks to the compatibility conditions<nbsp><eqref|eq:characterization-a>
      and<nbsp><eqref|eq:characterization-b>. Indeed, fix an arbitrary
      <math|\<ell\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> and assume inductively that

      <\equation*>
        \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0,<space|2em>\<forall\>\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>,\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\><space|1em>such<space|1em>that<space|1em>L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<less\>\<ell\><space|1em>and<space|1em>n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<in\>2\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>+1.
      </equation*>

      Then from the flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow> and the
      conditions<nbsp><eqref|eq:characterization-a>
      and<nbsp><eqref|eq:characterization-b>, it follows that

      <\equation*>
        \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0,<space|2em>\<forall\>\<sigma\>\<in\>*<around*|(|0,1|]>,\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\><space|1em>such<space|1em>that<space|1em>L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=\<ell\><space|1em>and<space|1em>n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<in\>2\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>+1.
      </equation*>

      Since by construction <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>=1>=0>
      for all <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> such that
      <math|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<in\>2\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>+1>,
      we conclude that\ 

      <\equation*>
        \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0,<space|2em>\<forall\>\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>,\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\><space|1em>such<space|1em>that<space|1em>n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<in\>2\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>+1.
      </equation*>
    </with>

    A further symmetry is given by spatial reflection, that is, the
    transformation

    <\equation*>
      <math|\<phi\><around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>\<phi\><around*|(|t,-x|)>,<application-space|2em>>
      \<xi\><around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>\<xi\><around*|(|t,-x|)>,
    </equation*>

    which also leaves the law of <math|\<xi\>> invariant. By an argument
    analogous to the one above, we infer that for any
    <math|<with|font-series|bold|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>>>, the cumulant
    <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> is symmetric under spatial
    reflections.
  </remark>

  <subsection|Bounds on parameters><label|sec:bounds-on-parameters>

  We shall now fix the parameters

  <\equation*>
    \<beta\>,\<theta\>,\<varrho\>,\<alpha\>,\<delta\>,\<flat\>
  </equation*>

  introduced in the analysis of the kernels. We have to choose these
  parameters so that<nbsp><eqref|eq:compatibility> is satisfied. Another
  constraint comes from the requirement that
  <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>>>
  for <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> with <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0>. Note
  that for <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> such that
  <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0>, we have
  <math|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0>
  and <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|1>>.
  Using the equality

  <\equation*>
    F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<varphi\>|)>=F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>><rsub|1><around*|(|\<varphi\>|)>=-\<lambda\>\<varphi\><rsup|><rsup|3>+<wide|r|\<bar\>><rsub|>*\<varphi\><rsup|>+\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>
  </equation*>

  and the fact that the noise <math|\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>
  is Gaussian, one shows that for <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> such that
  <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0> the cumulant
  <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> is nonzero only if:

  <\enumerate-alpha>
    <item>it is the covariance of the noise, that is
    <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=2>, <math|k<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0> and

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rprime|'>|)>=\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><around*|(|z|)>,F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|)>=\<bbb-E\><around*|[|\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|z|)>*\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>|]>=\<delta\><rsup|M><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>,
    </equation*>

    <with|color|black|where <math|\<delta\><rsup|M>> is the periodisation in
    space of the Dirac delta with period <math|M>,> or

    <item>it is the expected value of the (deterministic) kernel
    <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|3|)>><rsub|1>>, that is
    <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=1>, <math|k<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=3> and

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,z<rsub|2>,z<rsub|3>|)>=-\<lambda\>
      \<delta\><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>\<delta\><around*|(|z-z<rsub|2>|)>\<delta\><around*|(|z-z<rsub|3>|)>,
    </equation*>

    or

    <item>it is the expected value of the (deterministic) kernel
    <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><rsub|1>>, that is
    <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=1>, <math|k<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=1> and

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=<wide|r|\<bar\>>
      \<delta\><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>.
    </equation*>
  </enumerate-alpha>

  In the case a) <with|color|black|using the fact that
  <math|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>=1>>, we conclude that\ 

  <\equation>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsub|>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>>\<delta\><rsup|M><around*|(|\<mathd\>z|)>=1.<label|eq:est-cov-noise>
  </equation>

  As a consequence, we have to require that

  <\equation>
    <around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=-\<varrho\>+2\<theta\>\<leqslant\>0.<label|eq:two
    point>
  </equation>

  In the case b) we observe that

  \;

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|z;z<rsub|1>,z<rsub|2>,z<rsub|3>|)>=-\<lambda\>
    <big|prod><rsub|i=1><rsup|3>K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|i>|)>,
  </equation*>

  and thus <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\>1>
  uniformly in <math|\<sigma\>\<gtr\>0> by
  Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>. Consequently, we have to require
  that

  <\equation>
    <around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+3\<beta\>\<leqslant\>0<label|eq:initial-c>.
  </equation>

  In the case c) we have

  \;

  <\equation*>
    <around*|(|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|z;z<rsub|1>|)>=<wide|r
    |\<bar\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>,
  </equation*>

  and thus <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\>1>
  uniformly in <math|\<sigma\>\<gtr\>0>. Consequently, we have to require
  that

  <\equation*>
    <around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+\<beta\>\<leqslant\>0.
  </equation*>

  Note that since <math|\<beta\>\<gtr\>0> the last condition is implied by
  the bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:initial-c>.

  Let us collect in a table the various conditions which influence the choice
  of parameters. Some of them we already encountered, while other will appear
  later on (<with|color|black|the constraints
  <math|<around*|[|K|]>,<around*|[|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|]>> below>). We prefer to
  collect here all our constraints and fix the values of the parameters to
  proceed later in a straightforward way to the discussion of various
  conditions.

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|6|6|3|3|cell-bborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|-1|3|3|cell-lborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-rborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|-1|3|3|cell-rborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|3|3|cell-lborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-rborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|1|3|3|cell-rborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|3|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|1|3|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|1|3|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|1|3|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|3|3|cell-tborder|0ln>|<cwith|2|2|3|3|cell-lborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-rborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|2|2|3|3|cell-rborder|0ln>|<cwith|2|2|1|3|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|1|3|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|1|3|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|1|3|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|[|B|]>>|<cell|<text|Flow
    kernels<nbsp><math|<eqref|eq:constraint-flow-kernels>>>\<space\>>|<cell|2s-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>\<geqslant\>0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-A\>|]>>|<cell|<text|Flow
    cumulants <math|\<cal-A\>><nbsp><eqref|eq:compatibility>>
    >|<cell|\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>-d\<geqslant\>0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>>|<cell|<text|Flow
    cumulants <math|\<cal-B\>><nbsp><eqref|eq:compatibility>>>|<cell|2s-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>\<geqslant\>0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<Xi\>|]>>|<cell|<text|Initial
    condition <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>><nbsp><eqref|eq:two
    point>>>|<cell|-\<varrho\>+2\<theta\>\<leqslant\>0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<Phi\><rsup|3>|]>>|<cell|<text|Initial
    condition <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|3|)>>><nbsp><eqref|eq:initial-c>>>|<cell|-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+3\<beta\>\<leqslant\>0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|K|]>>|<cell|<text|Kolmogorov<nbsp><math|<eqref|eq:wanted-bound>>>\<space\>>|<cell|\<alpha\>-<frac|\<varrho\>|2>+\<theta\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-\<kappa\>\<gtr\>0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|]>>|<cell|<text|Kolmogorov
    <math|<wide|F|\<bar\>>><nbsp><math|\<space\><eqref|eq:constraint-f-bar>>>>|<cell|\<alpha\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>-\<kappa\>\<geqslant\>0>>>>><label|eq:summary-ineq>
  </equation>

  \;

  The parameter <math|\<kappa\>\<gtr\>0> quantifies the loss of regularity in
  the Kolmogorov-type argument used to estimate the pathwise behaviour of the
  random kernels and will be chosen sufficiently small.\ 

  From the constraints <math|<around*|[|\<Phi\><rsup|3>|]>> and
  <math|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>> we have

  <\equation*>
    \<beta\>\<leqslant\>s-\<delta\>/2,
  </equation*>

  while from <math|<around*|[|\<Xi\>|]>>, <math|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>> and
  this last inequality we deduce that

  <\equation*>
    \<theta\>\<leqslant\>\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s\<leqslant\>3s-3\<delta\>/2.
  </equation*>

  Using now <math|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>> again we have

  <\equation*>
    \<varrho\>\<leqslant\>\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s\<leqslant\>6s-3\<delta\>.
  </equation*>

  And <math|<around*|[|\<bbb-A\>|]>> now gives

  <\equation>
    0\<leqslant\>\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>-d\<leqslant\>4s-d-3\<delta\>=3<around*|(|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-\<delta\>|)>,<label|eq:sub-crit>
  </equation>

  where the strict positivity of

  <\equation*>
    \<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>\<assign\><frac|4s-d|3>\<gtr\>0,
  </equation*>

  defines the subcritical regime of this model. We now fix and choose the
  other parameters to saturate most of the inequalities we just found
  giving:<math|><math|>,

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-tborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-bborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-lborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-rborder|0.5ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<table|<row|<cell|\<beta\>=s-\<delta\>/2-\<kappa\>/2,<space|1em>\<theta\>=3\<beta\>,<space|1em>\<varrho\>=2\<theta\>,<space|1em>\<alpha\>=3\<beta\>+\<kappa\>,<space|1em><with|color|black|\<delta\>=\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>/2>.>>>>><label|eq:values-param>
  </equation>

  By substituting these values into the inequalities<nbsp><eqref|eq:summary-ineq>
  above, we check the following.

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|6|6|2|2|cell-bborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|8|2|2|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|8|2|2|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|8|2|2|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|8|2|2|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-lborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-rborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|-1|3|3|cell-lborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-bborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-lborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-rborder|0ln>|<cwith|1|1|3|3|cell-lborder|0ln>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-lsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-rsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-tborder|0ln>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-lborder|0ln>|<cwith|2|2|2|2|cell-rborder|0ln>|<cwith|2|2|3|3|cell-lborder|0ln>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|[|B|]>>|<cell|0\<leqslant\>2s-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>>|<cell|=2s-2\<beta\>-\<kappa\>-\<delta\>>|<cell|=0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-A\>|]>>|<cell|0\<leqslant\>\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>-d>|<cell|=4\<beta\>-\<delta\>-d>|<cell|=<with|color|black|<frac|3|2>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-2\<kappa\>>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>>|<cell|0\<leqslant\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s>|<cell|=-2\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s>|<cell|=\<kappa\>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<Xi\>|]>>|<cell|0\<geqslant\>-\<varrho\>+2\<theta\>>|<cell|=0>|<cell|=0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<Phi\><rsup|3>|]>>|<cell|0\<geqslant\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+3\<beta\>>|<cell|=0>|<cell|=0>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|K|]>>|<cell|0\<less\>\<alpha\>-<frac|\<varrho\>|2>+\<theta\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-\<kappa\>>|<cell|=3\<beta\>-<frac|d+2s|2>>|<cell|<with|color|black|=<frac|3|4>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-<frac|3|2>\<kappa\>>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|]>>|<cell|0\<leqslant\>\<alpha\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>-\<kappa\>>|<cell|=0>|<cell|=0>>>>><label|eq:ver-param>
  </equation>

  We used that

  <\equation>
    <frac|d+2s|2>=<frac|6s-3\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|2>=3\<beta\>-<frac|3|2><around*|(|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-\<delta\>|)>+3\<kappa\>.<label|eq:dplustwos>
  </equation>

  <\with|color|black>
    All the inequalities are satisfied provided

    <\equation>
      \<kappa\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>/2|)>.<label|eq:cond-kappa>
    </equation>

    In addition, in Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:loc-kernels> below we use the
    fact that the parameter of the weight <math|\<frak-o\>> introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels> satisfies

    <\equation>
      \<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\>\<delta\>\<wedge\>\<flat\>/<around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>.<label|eq:cond-kappa-o>
    </equation>
  </with>

  <\with|color|black>
    \;

    Finally, we explain how the value of the parameter <math|\<flat\>>,
    introduced in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>, is fixed. The
    role of this parameter is to compensate for the loss of spatial weight
    arising in the localisation procedure for the relevant cumulants
    discussed below, where the Taylor expansion allows to gain in homogeneity
    and establish that only a local renormalisation is needed. In
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:cumul-est-1> and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:loc-kernels>, we shall need
    <math|\<flat\>\<gtr\>2s-\<delta\>>. On the other hand, as argued in
    Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:decay-rate>, we must also impose
    <math|\<flat\>\<less\>2s>. Thus, <underline|we fix <math|\<flat\>>> such
    that \ 

    <\equation>
      2s-\<delta\>\<less\>\<flat\>\<less\>2s.<label|eq:choice-of-flat>\ 
    </equation>

    \;

    In Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing>, we shall introduce
    additional constraints on the parameters <math|\<kappa\>> and
    <math|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>, and we will fix all remaining
    parameters

    <\equation*>
      \<gamma\>,\<vartheta\>,<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>,<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>,<wide|k|\<bar\>>,a,\<nu\>,\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>,\<kappa\>,
    </equation*>

    which play a role in our analysis. We postpone this discussion because,
    apart from <math|\<kappa\>> and <math|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>, which
    must satisfy conditions<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappa>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappa-o>, these parameters are only relevant for
    the results established in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing>. We
    emphasise once again that all these parameters are to be regarded as
    fixed once and for all, and their choice depends solely on the exponent
    <math|s\<in\><around*|(|3/4,1|)>> of the fractional Laplacian.
  </with>

  <subsection|Classification of cumulants><label|sec:class-rel-cumulants><label|sec:classification-of-relevant>

  Given the bounds on the parameters from the previous section, we can now
  examine the class of cumulants that are relevant or marginal,
  <with|font-shape|italic|i.e.>, those satisfying
  <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<leqslant\>0>. Recalling that

  <\equation*>
    \<varrho\>=2\<theta\>,<space|1em><text|and><space|1em>\<theta\>=\<varrho\>-3\<beta\>,
  </equation*>

  observe that the condition <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<leqslant\>0> can be
  written as

  <\equation*>
    <around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>=\<theta\>*<around*|(|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>-2|)>+\<beta\>*K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+\<delta\>*L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=\<beta\>*<around*|(|3n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>-6+K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>|)>+\<delta\>*L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>0.
  </equation*>

  Then

  <\enumerate-alpha>
    <item>if <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<gtr\>2>, there are no
    relevant/marginal cumulants;

    <item>if <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=2>, the only relevant/marginal
    cumulant is the one with <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0>,
    that is the covariance of the noise: <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>=\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>.

    <item>if <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=1>, the only relevant/marginal
    cumulants are (at most) those with <math|K<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>3>.
  </enumerate-alpha>

  Summarising, the only relevant/marginal cumulants are

  <\equation*>
    \<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>,<space|2em><application-space|2em>\<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|k|)>>|)>=\<bbb-E\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|k|)>>,<space|1em><application-space|2em>k=0,1,2,3.
  </equation*>

  We can further restrict the set of cumulants to be analysed. Indeed, the
  flow equation for the cumulants with <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=0> is
  trivial and there is no evolution, so they coincide with their initial
  values. This applies to <math|\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
  and <math|\<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|0|]><around*|(|3|)>>|)>>.
  Moreover <math|\<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|3|)>>|)>>
  for <math|\<ell\>\<geqslant\>1> is irrelevant. As for the others,
  <with|color|black|by Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:symmetries>>, we know that
  the cumulants <math|\<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|0|)>>|)>>
  and <math|\<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|2|)>>|)>>
  vanish due to symmetry arguments. Thus the only remaining cumulants that we
  have to consider in detail are

  <\equation>
    \<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|1|)>>|)>=\<bbb-E\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|1|)>>,<space|2em>\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,<wide|\<ell\>|^>|}>,<label|eq:relevant-cum>
  </equation>

  where by definition <math|<wide|\<ell\>|^>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> is the
  smallest natural number such that <math|\<delta\>*<around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|^>+1|)>-2\<beta\>\<gtr\>0>.
  <with|color|black|Since the paramter <math|<wide|\<ell\>|^>> appears only
  in this and following section, it is not included in the
  list<nbsp><eqref|eq:parameters>.> Note that there are no marginal cumulants
  <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>> with <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0>.

  <subsection|Inductive procedure><label|sec:induction>

  The aim of this section is to derive bounds for the cumulants
  <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> using an induction on
  <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>, based on the flow
  equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>. More precisely,
  Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:flow-cumulants> shows that the flow equation
  defines a triangular system with respect to <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>.
  For irrelevant cumulants, we have <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>=1>=0>,
  and the desired bounds follow by directly integrating the flow equation
  from <math|\<sigma\>=1>. For relevant cumulants
  <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>, which for
  <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0> coincide with
  <eqref|eq:relevant-cum>, the bound for <math|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>
  is not integrable at <math|\<sigma\>=1>. To overcome this, we decompose
  relevant cumulants into a local relevant part and a<nbsp>nonlocal
  irrelevant part, using the procedure detailed in
  Appendix<nbsp><reference|app:localization>. The irrelevant part can again
  be integrated from <math|\<sigma\>=1> with zero boundary condition. For the
  relevant part, we instead impose the boundary condition at
  <math|\<sigma\>=1/2>, which acts as the renormalisation condition fixing
  the mass counterterm <math|r<rsub|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>. This
  allows the integration of the flow equation from <math|\<sigma\>=1/2>,
  thereby avoiding the non-integrable singularity at <math|\<sigma\>=1>.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:cumul-est-1>For any <math|<wide|r|\<bar\>>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>
    there exist (nonunique) choice of constants
    <math|<around*|(|r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>|)><rsub|\<ell\>=1,\<ldots\>,<wide|\<ell\>|^>>>
    such that the solution\ 

    <\equation*>
      F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>\<assign\><around*|(|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>,
    </equation*>

    of the approximate flow equation with the final condition

    <\equation>
      <with|color|black|<tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|3|2|3|cell-halign|l>|<table|<row|<cell|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>><rsub|1><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>>|<cell|=-\<lambda\>\<phi\><rsup|3>+<wide|r|\<bar\>>*\<phi\>+\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>,>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|1><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>>|<cell|=r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>
      \<phi\>,>|<cell|\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,<wide|\<ell\>|^>|}>,>>|<row|<cell|F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|1><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>>|<cell|=0,>|<cell|\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|<wide|\<ell\>|^>+1,\<ldots\>,<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|}>,>>>>><label|eq:initial-cond-induction-lemma>>
    </equation>

    satisfies

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>=sup<rsub|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>><around*|<left|[|1>|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|<right|]|1>><rsup|1/n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>\<less\>\<infty\>.
    </equation*>
  </lemma>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\remark>
      Note that

      <\equation*>
        F<rsup|><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>=<big|sum><rsub|\<ell\>=1><rsup|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>>F<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|1><around*|(|\<phi\>|)>,<space|2em>r<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>=<big|sum><rsub|\<ell\>=1><rsup|<wide|\<ell\>|^>>r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>,
      </equation*>

      where <math|F=F<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>> is the
      force<nbsp><eqref|eq:force> and <math|r<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>>
      is the mass renormalisation, which appears in the
      expression<nbsp><eqref|eq:action> for the action. The parameter
      <math|<wide|\<ell\>|^>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> was fixed at the end of
      Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:class-rel-cumulants>, whereas the parameter
      <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|^>> will be fixed
      in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:post-processing>.
    </remark>
  </with>

  <\proof>
    For <math|><math|\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|0,\<ldots\>,2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|}>>,
    define

    <\equation*>
      M<rsub|\<ell\>>\<assign\>1+sup<rsub|<stack|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<b-a\><mid|\|>L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>>>>>>><around*|[|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]><rsup|1/n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    We will prove by induction on <math|\<ell\>> that

    <\equation>
      <with|color|black|M<rsub|\<ell\>>\<less\>\<infty\>,<application-space|2em>and><application-space|2em>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0,<space|2em><text|for
      all <math|\<b-a\>> such that <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>>
      and <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<gtr\>2<rsup|\<ell\>+1>>,><label|eq:induction>
    </equation>

    for any <math|\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|0,\<ldots\>,2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|}>>.

    Let us remark that the second part of the above statement implies that
    there are only finitely many nonzero cumulants
    <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> such that
    <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>>. We first note that the
    case <math|\<ell\>=0> was already discussed in Sec.
    <reference|sec:bounds-on-parameters>, where it was proved that
    <math|M<rsub|0>\<less\>\<infty\>>.\ 

    Let us now consider the induction step. <with|color|black|Assume that the
    conditions expressed by<nbsp><eqref|eq:induction> hold true at the order
    <math|\<ell\>-1>, for a fixed <math|\<ell\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>. We
    shall prove that then the same is true at the order<nbsp><math|\<ell\>>.>
    The proof is based on the flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>. We
    first note that, by Lemma <reference|lem:flow-cumulants>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1>*M<rsub|\<ell\>-1><rsup|n<around*|(|b|)>>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1>*M<rsub|\<ell\>-1><rsup|n<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>>*M<rsub|\<ell\>-1><rsup|n<around*|(|\<b-c\>|)>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    for all <math|\<b-a\>\<in\>\<b-A\>> such that
    <math|L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=\<ell\>>. Recall that
    <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=n<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>-1 > and
    <math|><math|L<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>=L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>-1=\<ell\>-1>
    in the first line and <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>=n<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>+n<around*|(|\<b-c\>|)>-1>
    and <math|L<around*|(|\<b-b\>|)>+L<around*|(|\<b-c\>|)>=L<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>-1=\<ell\>-1>
    in the second line above. Hence, using the induction hypothesis we
    conclude that\ 

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-A\><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=0,<space|2em>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=0,
    </equation*>

    if <math|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>\<gtr\>2<rsup|\<ell\>+1>>, and

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1>,<space|2em><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1>.<label|eq:bound-ind>
    </equation>

    In the rest of the proof of the induction step we treat separately two
    cases: <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> is irrelevant,
    <with|font-shape|italic|i.e.> <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>, or
    <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> is relevant, <em|i.e.>,
    <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<less\>0>. Note that, according to the
    analysis in Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:class-rel-cumulants>, there are no
    marginal cumulants at level <math|\<ell\>\<gtr\>0>.

    <\with|color|black>
      If <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>> is irrelevant, <em|i.e.>
      <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>, then we can bound it by
      integrating the flow equation<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>
      <with|font-shape|italic|backward> from the final condition at
      <math|\<sigma\>=1>. We stress that for any irrelevant cumulant this
      final condition is vanishing, namely
      <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|1>=0>. To see this fact, note that
      <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|1>> is a cumulant of kernels
      <math|F<rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>>> of the
      force<nbsp><eqref|eq:initial-cond-induction-lemma>. Since for
      <math|\<ell\>\<gtr\>0> these kernels are

      <\equation*>
        F<rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>
        \<delta\><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>
      </equation*>

      which are deterministic, for <math|L<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<gtr\>0>
      every non-vanishing cumulant <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|1>>
      coincides with the expected value of
      <math|F<rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>>><math|>, which is relevant.
      As a consequence, for <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0> and
      <math|L<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>\<gtr\>0>,
      <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|1>=0>.
      Using<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>,
      Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:norm-scale-monotonicity>
      and<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-ind> we show easily that
    </with>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>-1>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>\<lesssim\>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>>.
    </equation*>

    On the other hand, if <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>> is relevant,
    <em|i.e.> <math|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>\<less\>0>, then on account of the
    discussion of Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:class-rel-cumulants>
    <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>>> is of the form
    <math|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>=\<frak-K\><rsub|1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]><around*|(|1|)>>|)>>
    with <math|\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,<wide|\<ell\>|^>|}>>. The
    treatment of the relevant cumulant proceeds via a localisation procedure,
    which shows that only the local part of the cumulant requires
    renormalisation. However, in our fractional setting, where the kernels
    exhibit only limited polynomial decay, this must be done with care.
    Specifically, we first introduce a preliminary truncation before
    performing a Taylor expansion to localise the fields. Consequently, to
    bound <math|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>>,
    we shall use the following decomposition

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|<around*|(|1-K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1,1>|)><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>
      <around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)> \<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<with|font-series|bold|L><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>-<with|font-series|bold|L><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|-<math-bf|R><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>.>>>>><label|eq:flow-decomposition>
    </equation>

    Here

    <\equation*>
      <wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>,
    </equation*>

    the operators <math|<with|font-series|bold|L>> and
    <math|<with|font-series|bold|R>> are suitable localisation and remainder
    operators defined in Appendix<nbsp><reference|app:localization> and the
    polynomial weight <math|h<rsub|\<mu\>>> was introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>. Recall that, by
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>, in the
    present case <math|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<b-a\>>=K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>>=1\<otimes\>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>>.
    We impose the following renormalisation condition

    <\equation*>
      <wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>=-<with|font-series|bold|L><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=\<delta\><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>
    r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>> the above condition
    fixes uniquely the counter-term <math|r<rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>.>
    Note that the above integral is finite for all
    <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> since on account
    of<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>, the estimates<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-ind>
    and Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:A-B-epsilon-bounds> we have

    <\equation>
      <with|color|black|<around*|\<interleave\>|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>>=><around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1>\<wedge\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>+\<flat\>-1>.<label|eq:expected-epsilon>
    </equation>

    Actually, the above bound implies that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||r<rsub|1><rsup|\<ell\>,\<varepsilon\>>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|1/2><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsup|\<varepsilon\>><rsub|0><around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<\|\|\>>
      \<mathd\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<varepsilon\>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>+\<flat\>-1>\<mathd\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>+<big|int><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|1/2><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1>\<mathd\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>,
    </equation*>

    where we used the fact that

    <\equation>
      <around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>+\<flat\>\<geqslant\>\<flat\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+\<delta\>+\<beta\>=\<flat\>-2\<beta\>+\<delta\>=\<flat\>-2s+2\<delta\>+\<kappa\>\<gtr\>0<label|eq:proof-a-bound>
    </equation>

    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogenity-cum>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:values-param>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-of-flat>. Taking into account the
    renormalisation condition, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|(|1-K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>+<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|\<mu\>><around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Finally, applying Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-1-h>,<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-1-K>,<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-local><nbsp>and<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-remainder>,
    we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>+2s-1>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>+\<flat\>-1>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>+\<flat\>-1>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>+<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|\<mu\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>-1>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<b-a\>|]>+2>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where we used again<nbsp><eqref|eq:proof-a-bound>. This concludes the
    proof of the induction step.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Local estimates for the flow of
  kernels><label|sec:localization-of-random-kernels>

  In this section, we prove an auxiliary result showing that the norms of the
  effective force kernels <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> can be
  controlled in terms of the norms of the localised kernels
  <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\> >\<cdot\>
  v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> restricted to a neighbourhood of the
  diagonal, <with|color|black|where <math|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> is
  the weight introduced in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>>. We use
  the notation

  <\equation*>
    <with|color|black|<around*|\<\|\|\>|X|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>\<assign\><around*|(|\<bbb-E\><around*|\||X|\|><rsup|N>|)><rsup|1/N>.>
  </equation*>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:loc-kernels>For all <math|\<ell\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsub|>,N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>it
    holds,

    <\equation>
      <label|eq:lemma-F-vF>sup<rsub|\<frak-a\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=\<ell\>>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<ell\>>
      1+sup<rsub|\<frak-a\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>,<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>N>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>>,
    </equation>

    and

    <\equation>
      <label|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF>sup<rsub|\<frak-a\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=\<ell\>>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>+1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<ell\>>
      1+sup<rsub|\<frak-a\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>,<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      \ <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>N>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>>
      .
    </equation>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    We shall prove the lemma by induction on
    <math|\<ell\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>>. First, we discuss the case
    <math|\<ell\>=0> for which we have <math|\<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=0>
    and thus <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>>
    for all <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>. Observe that the kernels
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>> are local, that is supported on the
    diagonal, <with|color|black|as can be seen from<nbsp><eqref|eq:force>>.
    Hence, <math|>

    <\equation*>
      F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<space|2em>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=0,
    </equation*>

    <math|>for all <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> since
    <math|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=1> on the diagonal. Moreover, for
    the irrelevant kernels, that is the kernels
    <math|><math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> such that
    <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>, we have
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=0> for all
    <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>> since
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>=0> for <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>>
    such that <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=0> and
    <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>. This proves the
    bounds<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-F-vF> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF> for
    <math|\<ell\>=0>.

    Let <math|\<ell\><rsub|0>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>> and suppose that the
    bounds<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-F-vF> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF> are
    true for all <math|\<ell\>\<leqslant\>\<ell\><rsub|0>>. We shall prove
    the bounds for <math|\<ell\>=\<ell\><rsub|0>+1>. It follows
    from<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-kernels> and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimate-B-kernels> that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>+1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-2\<kappa\>+1><around*|\<\|\|\>|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|<text|>\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, by Hölder's inequality

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>+1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|2N>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|<text|>\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|2N>>.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>\<vee\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-c\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1\<leqslant\>\<ell\><rsub|0>>
    and <math|\<ell\>=\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=\<ell\><rsub|0>+1> the
    above bound together with the induction hypothesis imply the
    bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF>. The dependence on <math|\<ell\>> in
    the bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF> comes from the estimate on the
    (finite) number of terms in the sum over <math|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>>.

    Let <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> be an irrelevant kernel, for
    which <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>. Then
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>=0>, <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
    > \<mathd\>\<eta\>> and

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>> \<mathd\>\<eta\>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>> \<mathd\>\<eta\>
    </equation*>

    where we replaced the norm <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
    >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> with <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
    >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>>> for <math|\<eta\>\<gtr\>\<mu\>>
    using<nbsp><eqref|eq:norm-mon>. Hence, by the Minkowski inequality

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, for the irrelevant kernels the
    bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-F-vF> follows from the
    bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF>.

    Let us now consider relevant kernels <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>>, for which
    <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>. If
    <math|><math|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=0>, then
    <math|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>*F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
    >=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\> >> and the
    bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-F-vF> is trivial. For
    <math|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0> we shall use the following
    decomposition

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1
      >\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|<around*|(|1-<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|]>\<cdot\>
      <around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>.>>>>><label|eq:fluct-decomp-Kolmogorov>
    </equation>

    <with|color|black|Note that <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1
    >\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>=0>, which
    follows from the fact that the kernels <math|F<rsub|1><rsup|\<frak-a\>>>
    are local, that is supported on the diagonal, and
    <math|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=1> on the diagonal.> Then

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>-F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<around*|(|1-<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>+<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|]>\<cdot\>
      <around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>.
    </equation*>

    We observe now that on account of Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-1-v>
    and Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-1-K-coeff>, it holds that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>-F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|(|<frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>>*+<with|color|black|<frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>>>|)>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><with|color|black|<frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, by Minkowski's inequality

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>-F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><with|color|black|<frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>>>*<around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|N>>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>.
    </equation*>

    Note that by <eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>, <eqref|eq:values-param>,
    <eqref|eq:choice-of-flat> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappa-o>,

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>+\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<geqslant\>\<flat\>-\<alpha\>+<around*|(|\<delta\>-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<beta\>=\<flat\>+<around*|(|\<delta\>-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-2\<beta\>-\<kappa\>=<around*|(|\<delta\>-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<delta\>+\<flat\>-2s\<gtr\>0>,
    </equation*>

    for <math|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0> and
    <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0>. Thus, the previous
    estimate and the bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:lemma-dot-F-vF> imply the bound
    <eqref|eq:lemma-F-vF> for the relevant kernels. This concludes the proof.
  </proof>

  <subsection|From cumulants to random kernels><label|sec:concl-of-cumul-analysis>

  The bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:stochastic-estimates-kernels> stated in
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force> is proved by combining the
  cumulant estimates from Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:cumul-est-1> with the
  auxiliary bounds established in Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:loc-kernels>, via
  the following lemma, which shows how estimates on the cumulants translate
  into estimates on the effective force kernels. The remaining part of
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force>, namely, the proof that the
  estimates<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F> hold with
  <math|C<rsub|F>=1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>,
  is presented in Sec. <reference|sec:post-processing>.

  Our analysis relies on the decomposition of the effective force kernels
  into mean and fluctuation parts:

  <\equation*>
    F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsup|>+<wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>,<application-space|2em><application-space|2em><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsup|>\<assign\>\<bbb-E\>
    F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<application-space|2em><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<assign\>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>-\<bbb-E\>
    F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>.
  </equation*>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:kolmogorov><with|color|black|Let
    <math|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>>
    be the solution of the approximate flow equation with initial
    condition<nbsp><eqref|eq:initial-cond-induction-lemma> with
    <math|r<rsub|\<varepsilon\>,M>> as in Lemma <reference|lem:cumul-est-1>.>
    For every <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>, we have

    <\equation>
      \<bbb-E\><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|N>=<around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsup|N><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<less\>\<infty\>,<label|eq:bound-FA>
    </equation>

    where <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>> was defined
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:norm-family-F>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    If the kernel <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> is irrelevant, that
    is <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<gtr\>0>, then
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>=0>, <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
    > \<mathd\>\<eta\>> and

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>> \<mathd\>\<eta\>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>> \<mathd\>\<eta\>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>> \<mathd\>\<eta\>.
    </equation*>

    On the other hand, if the kernel <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>
    is relevant, that is <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>, then
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|1>> and
    <with|font-series|bold|><math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>=0>
    at <math|\<mu\>=1>. Consequently, we have
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=0>
    at <math|\<mu\>=1>. From\ 

    <\equation>
      \<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>\<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><with|color|black|-><around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-1>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<label|eq:F-rho-derivative>
    </equation>

    we deduce that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-1>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)> \<mathd\>\<eta\>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-1>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|)> \<mathd\>\<eta\>.
    </equation*>

    Next, Minkowski inequality gives

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-1><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>,
    </equation*>

    for both relevant and irrelevant kernels. Since
    <math|<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<kappa\>-1>
    \<mathd\>\<eta\>\<less\>\<infty\>>, we arrive at

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>+1-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>+sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Using Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:loc-kernels> and the decomposition
    <math|F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>=<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>+<wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>>
    we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|1+sup<rsub|\<frak-a\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>,<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>*F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>
      N>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|1+sup<rsub|\<frak-a\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<ell\>,<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>\<less\>0>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|(|<around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>*<wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>><rsub|L<rsub|\<bbb-P\>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>N>>+<around*|<left|(|2>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>*<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|)|2>><rsup|2<rsup|\<ell\>>>|)>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Applying Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:v-and-K>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:control-of-avgs> and recalling that
    <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>\<less\>\<infty\>>,
    on account of Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:cumul-est-1>, we conclude that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<less\>\<infty\>.
    </equation*>

    Finally, to establish the slightly stronger bound<equation*|>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|sup<rsub|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|d/2<rsub|>+s+2\<kappa\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<less\>\<infty\>
    </equation*>

    for <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>,
    we proceed as before, replacing <math|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>> by
    <math|><math|-d/2<rsub|>-s-2\<kappa\>> and invoke the second bound stated
    in Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:v-and-K>.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:v-and-K>For all <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>> and<math|>
    <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>, we have

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|4>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|4>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<lesssim\><rsub|N><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>><rsup|1/2>,>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|sup<rsub|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|4>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|d/2+s+\<kappa\>><rsup|><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|4>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>
      \<lesssim\><rsub|N>1.>|<cell|>>>>
    </eqnarray*>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Let <math|k=k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>. By
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:aux-weight>, there exists is a weight
    <math|<wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> with support properties
    analogous to those of <math|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> such that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><rsub|><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Moreover, it holds that

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|z\<in\> \<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|k>>
      <wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>
      <math-up|>\<mathd\>Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<lesssim\>
      <with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      k> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|d
      k>>,<space|2em>Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>=<around*|(|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsup|k>.
    </equation*>

    Thus, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      k> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|d
      k>> <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>,
    </equation*>

    where, here and below, <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<bullet\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>>
    denotes the supremum norm in all the variables. Hence,

    <\equation>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      k> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|d
      k>> <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>><rsup|>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>.<label|eq:nuF-F>
    </equation>

    To analyse the last term, we decompose the operator <math|K<rsub|\<mu\>>>
    as

    <\equation*>
      K<rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|K|\<check\>><rsub|\<mu\>> <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>>,
    </equation*>

    where

    <\equation>
      <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-2>,<application-space|2em><wide|K|\<check\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>,<label|eq:partial-kernel>
    </equation>

    and <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<gtr\>0> is a small constant to be fixed
    later. By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:check-K>,

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|\<check\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<with|color|black|L<rsup|2N/<around*|(|2N-1|)>><around*|(|1/\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><rsup|>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|d+2s|)>/2N>,<label|eq:bound-K-check>
    </equation>

    <with|color|black|>provided <math|4N <wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<gtr\>3>. In what
    follows, we choose <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<in\><around*|(|0,1/<around*|(|2+2<wide|k|\<bar\>>|)>|)>>
    and assume that <math|<with|color|black|N\<gtr\><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>><rsup|-1>\<gtr\>2+2<wide|k|\<bar\>>>>.
    Recall that

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|K|\<check\>><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>>
    </equation*>

    by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels>
    and<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>. Hence, by
    weighted Young's inequality, Fubini's theorem
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-K-check>, it holds that

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>><rsup|2N>|<right|]|3>>\<lesssim\>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|1em>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|d+2s|)><around*|(|1+k|)>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k>>\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|2>|<around*|<left|(|1>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>
      <around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><around*|(|z;Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>|<right|)|1>><rsup|2N>|<right|]|2>>\<mathd\>z
      \<mathd\>Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|1em>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|d+2s|)><around*|(|1+k|)>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k>>\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><around*|(|z;Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>|<right|)|1>><rsup|2N>|<right|]|3>>
      <around*|(|<frac|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>|w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>>|)><rsup|><rsup|2N>\<mathd\>z
      \<mathd\>Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|1em>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|d+2s|)><with|color|black|<around*|(|1+k|)>>>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|1>|<around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsup|2N>|<right|]|1>><rsup|>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where we used that,

    <\equation*>
      <big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k>><around*|(|<frac|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>|w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>>|)><rsup|><rsup|2N>\<mathd\>z
      \<mathd\>Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|1>,
    </equation*>

    for <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> large enough. Thus,

    <\equation>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>><rsup|>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<frac|<around*|(|d+2s|)><with|color|black|<around*|(|1+k|)>>|2N><with|color|black|>>
      \ <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|2>|<around*|<left|(|2>|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|)|2>><rsup|2N>|<right|]|2>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>><rsup|1/2N>.<label|eq:steptwo-Fbound>
    </equation>

    We need to control the <math|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>> norm of the
    centred random variable

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><around*|(|z;Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>
      w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,Z<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>.
    </equation*>

    To this end, we observe that, by induction it is easy to show that
    <math|<wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>> is a polynomial of the
    Gaussian random field <math|\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>>.
    Consequently, by Nelson's hypercontractivity estimate, all higher moments
    can be controlled by the second one. In particular, the <math|2N>-th
    moment can be bounded in terms of the second-order cumulant

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|\<bbb-E\><around*|(|<wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<otimes\><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>=\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>,F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>=\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>>.>
    </equation*>

    Using the notation

    <\equation*>
      w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>>\<assign\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<otimes\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>,<space|2em>K<rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>\<otimes\>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>,
    </equation*>

    <math|>we have

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|2>|<around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|)|1>><rsup|2N>|<right|]|2>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>>>|<row|<cell|<space|1em>\<lesssim\><rsub|N><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|\<bbb-E\><around*|<left|[|1>|<around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsup|2>|<right|]|1>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>><rsup|N>>>|<row|<cell|<space|1em>\<lesssim\><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsup|N><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>.>>>>><label|eq:hypercontractivity>
    </equation>

    Since

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>=<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|>,
    </equation*>

    by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:kolmogorov-aux> below, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|2>|\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k>F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|<right|\<\|\|\>|2>><rsup|><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
      <around*|(|1+2k|)>> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
      <around*|(|1+2k|)>>> <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>.
    </equation*>

    Hence, by<nbsp><eqref|eq:hypercontractivity>,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|3>|\<bbb-E\><around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1,k><wide|F|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsup|2N>|<right|\<\|\|\>|3>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>><rsup|<frac|1|2N>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-s
      <around*|(|1+2k|)>> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
      <around*|(|1+2k|)>/2>> <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1/2>.
    </equation*>

    Overall, using<nbsp><eqref|eq:nuF-F>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:steptwo-Fbound>
    together with the definition<nbsp><eqref|eq:norm-family-cumulants> of
    <math|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>>
    and the fact that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|[|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>|]>=-\<varrho\>+2<around*|(|\<theta\>+\<alpha\>|)>+2<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>,
    </equation*>

    we arrive at

    <\equation>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|4>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|4>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<lesssim\><rsub|N><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>><rsup|1/2>*sup<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<frac|\<varrho\>|2>+\<theta\>+\<alpha\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-<frac|<around*|(|d+2s|)><around*|(|1+k|)>|2N>-\<kappa\>>.<label|eq:exp-bound-2>
    </equation>

    In order to conclude, we need the right-hand side above to be finite,
    that is, we require

    <\equation>
      \<theta\>+\<alpha\>-<frac|\<varrho\>|2>-<frac|d+2s|2>-<frac|<around*|(|d+2s|)><with|color|black|<around*|(|1+<wide|k|\<bar\>>|)>>|2N>-\<kappa\>\<geqslant\>0.<label|eq:wanted-bound>
    </equation>

    Given our choices of parameters<nbsp><eqref|eq:values-param> this bounds
    has the form

    <\equation>
      <with|color|black|<frac|3|4>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>>-<frac|<around*|(|d+2s|)><with|color|black|<around*|(|1+<wide|k|\<bar\>>|)>>|2N>-<frac|3|2>\<kappa\>\<geqslant\>0.<label|eq:smallness-conditions>
    </equation>

    Since <math|\<kappa\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>/2|)>>
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappa>, it suffices to take
    <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> large enough to satisfy this inequality
    and conclude our bound. The bound for smaller values of
    <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> follows then immediately by Jensen's
    inequality.

    The second of the stated bounds, namely the estimate for the noise
    <math|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>=\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|>>,
    is proved by the same argument as for<nbsp><eqref|eq:exp-bound-2>, except
    that we now use the precise estimate

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>,\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=1
    </equation*>

    for the covariance of the noise

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>,\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|>,\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><rsub|>|)>,<space|2em>\<frak-a\>=<around*|(|0,0|)>,
    </equation*>

    which follows from<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-cov-noise>, instead of the weaker
    bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>,\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<leqslant\><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<around*|(|\<frak-a\>\<frak-a\>|)>|]>>.
    </equation*>

    Specifically, in place of<nbsp><eqref|eq:exp-bound-2> we obtain

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|1>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|d/2+s+\<kappa\>><rsup|><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|1>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>=sup<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|<left|\<\|\|\>|1>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|d/2+s+\<kappa\>><rsup|><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\>K<rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>|\<\|\|\>>|<right|\<\|\|\>|1>><rsub|L<rsup|2N><rsub|\<bbb-P\>>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<frac|<around*|(|d+2s|)>|2N>+\<kappa\>>\<lesssim\>1,
    </equation*>

    for <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> large enough, depending on
    <math|\<kappa\>\<gtr\>0>.
  </proof>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:kolmogorov-aux>Let <math|F\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k>|)>>
      be a random field whose law is invariant under spacetime translations
      and such that

      <\equation>
        \<Lambda\>\<ni\>z\<mapsto\>F<around*|(|z,z+z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z+z<rsub|k>|)>\<in\>\<bbb-R\><label|eq:F-periodicity-lem>
      </equation>

      is a.s. periodic in space with period <math|M> for all
      <math|z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>\<in\>\<Lambda\>>. Define

      <\equation*>
        \<cal-F\><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>=\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<around*|(|0<rsub|>,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>,
        F<around*|(|z,z<rsub|k+1>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|)>,<space|2em>z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>\<in\>\<Lambda\>.
      </equation*>

      For all <math|\<omega\>\<geqslant\>0> and
      <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<in\><around*|[|0,1/<around*|(|2k+1|)>|)>>, we
      have

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|<around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F|)>,
        <around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F|)>|)>\<cdot\>
        <around*|(|w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<otimes\>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
        <around*|(|1+2k|)>> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
        <around*|(|1+2k|)>>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rsub|2k>,>>>>>
      </equation*>

      uniformly over <math|F> and <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>,
      where

      <\equation*>
        <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-2>.
      </equation*>
    </lemma>

    <\proof>
      We claim that

      <\equation*>
        \<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|<around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F|)><around*|(|0<rsub|>,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>,
        <around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F|)><around*|(|z<rsub|>,z<rsub|k+1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|)>=<around*|(|\<cal-K\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>>\<ast\><rsub|>\<cal-F\>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>
      </equation*>

      for all <math|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>\<in\>\<Lambda\>>, where
      <math|\<ast\><rsub|>> stands for the convolution on
      <math|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+2k>> and

      <\equation*>
        \<cal-K\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|''>|)>*<wide|K|^><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z+z<rprime|''>|)>*<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>+z<rprime|''>|)>\<ldots\>
        <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|2k>+z<rprime|''>|)><space|0.4spc>\<mathd\>z<rprime|''>.
      </equation*>

      Indeed, we have

      <\eqnarray*>
        <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<around*|(|\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<ast\><rsub|>\<cal-F\>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|2+2k>><wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|''>|)>*<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+z<rprime|''>|)>*<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'><rsub|1>+z<rprime|''>|)>\<ldots\>
        <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>+z<rprime|''>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        \<cal-F\><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|''>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|2+2k>><wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|''>|)>*<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>*<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'><rsub|1>|)>\<ldots\>
        <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        \<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|F<around*|(|0-z<rprime|''><rsub|>,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>,F<around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>,z<rsub|k+1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|)>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|''>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|=\<frak-K\><rsub|2><around*|(|<around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F|)><around*|(|0<rsub|>,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>,<around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>F|)><around*|(|z<rsub|>,z<rsub|k+1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|)>,>>>>
      </eqnarray*>

      where the second equality above follows from the translation invariance
      of the law of <math|F>.

      It remains to show that

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|
        <around*|\||<around*|(|\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<ast\><rsub|>\<cal-F\>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|>,z<rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|1em>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
        <around*|(|1+2k|)>> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
        <around*|(|1+2k|)>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|4em>\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rsub|2k>.>>>>>
      </equation*>

      We have

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||<around*|(|\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<ast\><rsub|>\<cal-F\>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|\|>\<leqslant\><big|sum><rsub|n\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>>|<cell|<around*|\||\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>.>>>>>
      </equation*>

      Thus, by <eqref|eq:weight-w-2> we obtain

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||<around*|(|\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<ast\><rsub|>\<cal-F\>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|>,z<rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|n\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n|)> w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1><rprime|'>|)>\<cdots\>w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|2k><rprime|'>|)>
        <around*|\||\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>
        w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rsub|k+1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>,>>>>>
      </equation*>

      where for <math|z=<around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>> and
      <math|n\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>> we write <math|><math|z+M
      n=<around*|(|t,x+M n|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>>. Using
      Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels> we arrive at

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rsub|k+1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rsub|1>-z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>-z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>>>|<row|<cell|=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>z<rprime|'><rsub|k>,z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n+z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z-z<rprime|'>+M
        n+z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|> \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>.>>>>>
      </equation*>

      Note that by<nbsp><eqref|eq:F-periodicity-lem>, the above expression
      can be rewritten as

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>z<rprime|'><rsub|k>,z<rprime|'>+z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'>+z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>>>|<row|<cell|=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>
        <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>z<rprime|'><rsub|k>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>.>>>>>
      </equation*>

      Consequently,

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||<around*|(|\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<ast\><rsub|>\<cal-F\>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|>,z<rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|2k>|)>>>|<row|<cell|\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|sum><rsub|n\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>>w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n|)> w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1><rprime|'>|)>\<cdots\>w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|2k><rprime|'>|)>
        <around*|\||\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|\<times\>
        <big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|M>\<times\>\<Lambda\><rsup|2k>>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|0,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|k+1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>
        \ <around*|\||\<cal-F\><around*|(|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>
        \<mathd\>z<rprime|'>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|1>\<ldots\>\<mathd\>z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>.>>>>>
      </equation*>

      The statement follows now from the estimate

      <\equation*>
        sup<rsub|z<rprime|'>,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|sum><rsub|n\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>>w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n|)> w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1><rprime|'>|)>\<cdots\>w<rsup|\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|2k><rprime|'>|)>
        <around*|\||\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rprime|'>+M
        n,z<rprime|'><rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rprime|'><rsub|2k>|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
        <around*|(|1+2k|)>> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
        <around*|(|1+2k|)>>,
      </equation*>

      which is a consequence of Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:hat-K>.
    </proof>
  </with>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:control-of-avgs>We have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|*<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>
      >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>><rsup|>|\<interleave\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:aux-weight>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Moreover, by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>,

    <\equation*>
      \<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><wide|w|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<leqslant\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>.
    </equation*>

    Thus, by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogenity-cum> we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>K<rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>><rsup|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<kappa\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-A\>>|\<interleave\>>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<alpha\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>-\<kappa\>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    To conclude we use the inequality

    <\equation>
      \<alpha\>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>-\<kappa\>\<geqslant\>0,<label|eq:constraint-f-bar>
    </equation>

    which coincides with the constraint<nbsp><math|<around*|[|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|]>>
    stated in<nbsp><eqref|eq:summary-ineq>.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Post-processing><label|sec:post-processing>

  To complete the proof of Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:effective-force>, it
  remains to exhibit the bounds<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F> with
  <math|C<rsub|F>=1+<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>,
  based on the analysis of the flow equation carried out so far. This is the
  content of Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:overall-difference-bound>,
  <reference|lem:estimates-DF> and<nbsp><reference|lem:packaging> below.

  Before continuing with the specific computations leading
  to<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F> it will be useful to discuss how to fix the values
  of the parameters

  <\equation*>
    \<gamma\>,\<vartheta\>,<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>><with|color|black|,<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>,<wide|k|\<bar\>>,a,\<nu\>,\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>,\<kappa\>.>
  </equation*>

  The validity of the Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:overall-difference-bound>\U<reference|lem:difference-bound>
  below, which together yield<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F>, depends on a series of
  conditions on these parameters, namely<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-zeta>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:xi-on-zeta>,<nbsp><math|<eqref|eq:DF-bound>,><nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-of-K-and-l>
  and<nbsp><eqref|eq:one-J-bound> as well as the
  constraints<nbsp><eqref|eq:thm-constraints> in
  Theorem<nbsp><reference|thm:apriori-system>. The parameters
  <math|><math|\<kappa\>,\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><rsub|>> are further
  constrained by conditions<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappa>
  and<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappa-o>.

  For the reader's convenience, these conditions are summarised in the
  following table:

  <\equation*>
    <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-halign|c>|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-bsep|0.5em>|<cwith|1|-1|2|2|cell-tsep|0.5em>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-A\>|]>>|<cell|\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>3<around*|(|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>|)>+\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>-\<kappa\>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>>|<cell|\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>2\<gamma\>\<wedge\><around*|(|3\<gamma\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-2\<kappa\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-C\>|]>>|<cell|\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>\<delta\>
    <wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>-\<alpha\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-D\>|]>>|<cell|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>\<nu\>+<around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-E\>|]>>|<cell|\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>\<gamma\>\<wedge\><around*|(|2s-\<gamma\>|)>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-F\>|]>>|<cell|\<vartheta\>\<geqslant\><frac|4<around*|(|s+\<gamma\>|)>
    <wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-G\>|]>>|<cell|<with|color|black|\<kappa\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>/2|)>>>>|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<bbb-H\>|]>>|<cell|<with|color|black|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\>\<delta\>\<wedge\>\<flat\>/<around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>>>>>>
  </equation*>

  In order to satisfy all these constraints, together with the basic bounds
  <math|\<vartheta\>\<gtr\>0> and <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0>, we proceed as
  follows. First, we set

  <\equation>
    <block|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<text|<math|\<gamma\>=\<beta\>-\<vartheta\>>,<space|2em><math|\<vartheta\>=<frac|1|16>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>>.>
    >>>>><label|eq:fix-gamma-zeta>
  </equation>

  Next, we <underline|fix <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<gtr\>0> small
  enough> so that

  \;

  <\equation*>
    <frac|4<around*|(|s+\<beta\>|)> <wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>\<leqslant\><frac|1|16>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>,
  </equation*>

  which allows to satisfy<nbsp><math|<around*|[|\<bbb-F\>|]>>. The
  constraint<nbsp><math|<around*|[|\<bbb-A\>|]>> is satisfied provided

  <\equation>
    a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>+\<kappa\>\<leqslant\><frac|1|4>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>.<label|eq:const-kappa-two>
  </equation>

  Since from<nbsp><eqref|eq:values-param> we have

  \;

  <\equation*>
    3\<gamma\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-2\<kappa\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>=3<around*|(|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>|)>+3\<beta\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-2\<kappa\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>=3<around*|(|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>|)>+<frac|3|4>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-<frac|7|2>\<kappa\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>,
  </equation*>

  the condition<nbsp><math|<around*|[|\<bbb-B\>|]>> is satisfied provided\ 

  <\equation*>
    4\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\><frac|3|4>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-<frac|7|2>\<kappa\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>,
  </equation*>

  and

  <\equation*>
    3\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>2\<beta\>=2s-\<delta\>-\<kappa\>=2s-<frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|2>-\<kappa\>,
  </equation*>

  that is, whenever

  <\equation>
    <frac|7|2>\<kappa\>+a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\><frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|2>,<space|2em>\<kappa\>\<leqslant\>2s-<frac|11|16>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>.<label|eq:const-kappa-three>
  </equation>

  Note that

  <\equation*>
    2s-<frac|11|16>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>\<geqslant\>2s-\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>\<geqslant\>2s-<frac|4s-d|3>=<frac|2s+d|3>\<gtr\>0,
  </equation*>

  so the second condition in<nbsp><eqref|eq:const-kappa-three> can be indeed
  satisfied. To meet condition<nbsp><math|<around*|[|\<bbb-C\>|]>>, we
  require

  <\equation>
    2a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\><frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|4><label|eq:const-kappa-four>,
  </equation>

  and <underline|choose <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>> large enough> so that

  <\equation*>
    \<alpha\>+<frac|1|16>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>\<leqslant\><frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|4><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>-<frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|8>\<leqslant\><around*|(|<frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|2>-2a
    \<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)> <wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>.
  </equation*>

  <with|color|black|Given <math|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>> as above, we
  <underline|fix <math|<wide|k|\<bar\>>> large enough> as discussed in
  Sec.<nbsp><reference|sec:random-flow>.> Then we <underline|fix <math|a>
  sufficiently large> so that

  <\equation*>
    a<with|color|black|\<geqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>><around*|(|2s-\<delta\>|)>/<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>\<geqslant\>2<wide|k|\<bar\>>\<beta\>/<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>2<wide|k|\<bar\>>\<gamma\>/<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>,
  </equation*>

  Consequently, relation<nbsp><eqref|eq:a-nu-gamma> compels us to
  <underline|set <math|<with|color|black|\<nu\>=\<gamma\>/a>>>. To ensure
  condition<nbsp><math|<around*|[|\<bbb-D\>|]>> we introduce
  a<nbsp>constraint

  <\equation>
    <around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>\<leqslant\><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>/2.<label|eq:const-kappa-one>
  </equation>

  Condition<nbsp><math|<around*|[|\<bbb-E\>|]>> is met if

  <\equation>
    \<kappa\>\<leqslant\><frac|8s+d|6>,<label|eq:const-kappa-five>
  </equation>

  since then

  <\equation*>
    <with|color|black|\<vartheta\>=2\<vartheta\>-\<vartheta\>=<frac|1|16>\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>-\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\><around*|(|<frac|s|2>-<frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|16>-<frac|\<kappa\>|4>|)>-\<vartheta\>=\<beta\>-\<vartheta\>=\<gamma\>>
  </equation*>

  and

  <\equation*>
    \<vartheta\>=\<beta\>-\<gamma\>=s-<frac|\<delta\><rsub|\<star\>>|4>-<frac|\<kappa\>|2>-\<gamma\>\<leqslant\>2s-\<gamma\>.
  </equation*>

  To conclude, we <underline|fix <math|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>> and
  <math|\<kappa\>> small enough> to satisfy the remaining constraints, namely
  <math|<around*|[|\<bbb-G\>|]>,> <math|<around*|[|\<bbb-H\>|]>> as well
  as<nbsp><eqref|eq:const-kappa-two>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:const-kappa-three>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:const-kappa-four>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:const-kappa-one>,<nbsp><eqref|eq:const-kappa-five>.

  Let us now detail the analysis. As a first step, we extract the coercive
  contribution from the effective force by defining

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|Q<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>>|<cell|<with|color|black|\<assign\>>>|<cell|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>-<around*|(|-\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>-J<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|-\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>-<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>+J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>-<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>,>>>>><label|eq:difference-decomposition>
  </equation>

  where <math|\<psi\>> is a generic field,

  <\equation*>
    \<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\>
  </equation*>

  and

  <\equation*>
    F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,0>=\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>>,<space|2em>F<rsub|><rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,1><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>=<wide|r|\<bar\>>*\<psi\>,<space|2em>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|>|)>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<barsuchthat\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>.
  </equation*>

  <with|color|black|Recall that the norms
  <math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>>=<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
  and \ <math|><math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>=<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
  depending on the terminal scale <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>
  were introduced in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:triple-norms>.>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:overall-difference-bound><with|color|black|Assume<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-zeta>,
    <eqref|eq:xi-on-zeta>, <eqref|eq:one-J-bound> and>

    <\equation>
      <wide|k|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>5,<space|2em><wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>\<nu\>+<around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><label|eq:cond-kappabar-one>.
    </equation>

    Then the bounds

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*Q<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around*|<left|[|3>|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>+<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|2>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>|<right|]|3>>>>>>><label|eq:bound-Q>
    </equation>

    and

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>,>>>>><label|eq:bound-JtildeF>
    </equation>

    hold uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,>
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>
    >and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    First, observe that by the triangular inequality applied to the
    decomposition<nbsp><eqref|eq:difference-decomposition>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*Q<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*J<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*J<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>+F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>+F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|5\<nu\>>*<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<lambda\>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    To obtain the second estimate, we used that
    <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>5\<nu\>>, which is a
    consequence of<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one>, together with the
    identity <math|J<rsub|\<sigma\>>=L<rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    and the bound <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\>1>,
    the latter being a consequence of Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>.
    The bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-Q> follows now from
    Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:control-of-forcing>,<nbsp><reference|lem:l-0-kernels>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:difference-bound>. Since
    <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>3\<nu\>> and
    <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\>1>
    by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>
      \<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3\<nu\>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3\<nu\>>**\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3\<nu\>>*\<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|3>.
    </equation*>

    The bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-JtildeF> follows now from the estimate

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>+F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>+<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>
      \<psi\><rsup|3><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>
    </equation*>

    and Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:control-of-forcing>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:l-0-kernels>.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:control-of-forcing><with|color|black|Assume<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one>.>
    Then for every <math|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\>> such that
    <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0>, the bound

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<alpha\>+<around*|(|\<beta\>-\<gamma\>|)>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<delta\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsup|><label|eq:est-F-a>
    </equation>

    holds uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,>
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>
    >and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
    Moreover, provided

    <\equation>
      \<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>3<around*|(|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>|)>+\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>-\<kappa\>,<label|eq:choice-zeta>
    </equation>

    the following bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>.
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,>
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)> >
    and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    We first observe that by <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>>
    > and <math|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>>=1>, it holds that

    <\equation*>
      \<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, it follows from <math|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=K<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>\<otimes\><around*|(|K<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>>
    and Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels> of the kernel norm that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>,
    </equation*>

    where

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|>|)>\<assign\><frac|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><around*|(|z|)>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>
      <wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|>|)>
      \<rho\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>
      \<ldots\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>>.>
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      \;
    </equation*>

    Using that the weight <math|\<frak-o\>> is at scale <math|1> (cf.
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>) and that the weight
    <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>> is at scale
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>> (cf.
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights>), we deduce

    <\equation>
      \<frak-o\><around*|(|z|)><rsup|-1>=<around*|\<langle\>|z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>\<leqslant\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><around*|\<langle\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a>.z|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>\<zeta\><rsup|<rsub|-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z|)>.<label|eq:bound-o-zeta-weights>
    </equation>

    Noting that the Steiner diameter of a collection of points is always at
    least as large as the distance between any two points, we exploit the
    weight <math|<around*|(|<wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|a>|)><rsup|-1>>
    to propagate the weights <math|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|-1>> to the
    output variable. Using furthermore that
    <math|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>=\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<nu\>>> and
    <math|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>=\<frak-o\><rsup|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>>
    as well as <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>>,
    <math| k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>>
    and<nbsp><math|<eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one>>, we obtain

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|(|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsup|>\<rho\><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>-\<nu\>
      k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>>>>>><label|eq:weight-bound-1>
    </equation>

    We also observe that, by Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:triple-phi>,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>
      ><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|>.
    </equation*>

    Moreover, by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels>,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Combining the above estimates and using<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>,
    we conclude that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<alpha\>+<around*|(|\<beta\>-\<gamma\>|)>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<delta\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsup|>,
    </equation*>

    which proves<nbsp><eqref|eq:est-F-a>.

    To prove the second part, we observe that

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|color|black>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|\<gtr\>0|]>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<barsuchthat\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<barsuchthat\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<alpha\>+<around*|(|\<beta\>-\<gamma\>|)>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<delta\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsup|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<alpha\>+\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    where we used that <math|\<beta\>\<geqslant\>\<gamma\>>,
    <math|1\<leqslant\>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>>
    and <math|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>>. Since,
    by <math|\<alpha\>=3\<beta\>+\<kappa\>> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-zeta>,
    we have

    <\equation*>
      3\<gamma\>-\<alpha\>+\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>=3<around*|(|\<gamma\>-\<beta\>|)>+\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>-\<kappa\>\<leqslant\>\<vartheta\>,
    </equation*>

    the proof is complete.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:l-0-kernels>Assume<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one> and

    <\equation>
      \<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>2\<gamma\>\<wedge\><around*|(|3\<gamma\>-<frac|d+2s|2>-2\<kappa\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>|)>.<label|eq:xi-on-zeta>
    </equation>

    Then the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)>,
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,><math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>
    > and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    <with|color|black|On account of<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-kernels>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:B-form>, <math|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=0>.
    Thus,>

    <\equation*>
      F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z|)>=F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|1><around*|(|z|)>=\<xi\><rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>,M|)>><around*|(|z|)>,<space|2em>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><rsub|1><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=<wide|r|\<bar\>>*\<delta\><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Recall the definition <eqref|eq:norm-family-F> of
    <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>>. By
    Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:triple-phi>, <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>\<nu\>>
    and <math|\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>2\<gamma\>>, we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<with|color|black|<around*|\||<wide|r|\<bar\>>|\|>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>*\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Moreover, by<nbsp><eqref|eq:xi-on-zeta>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>\<frak-o\><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|<around*|[|0|]>,<around*|(|0|)>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|d+2s|)>/2-2\<kappa\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    where the bound <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>\<frak-o\><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>>>
    <with|color|black|follows from<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-o-zeta-weights>>,
    since <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>\<geqslant\>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one>.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-DF>Assume<nbsp><eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one> and

    <\equation>
      \<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>.<label|eq:DF-bound>
    </equation>

    Then the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|*G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|^>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|J<rsup|>|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|\<psi\>|^>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,>
    <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>,
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>>
    and <math|\<psi\>,<wide|\<psi\>|^>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    We have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<mathD\>
      F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsub|><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|^>|)>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\>\<barsuchthat\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<gtr\>0><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>
      ><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1|)>>\<otimes\><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|^>|)>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Observe that since <math| ><math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<assign\>\<cal-L\><rsup|-1><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><wide|J|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>,
    <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>=<wide|J|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>>,
    <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>J<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>=J<rsub|\<sigma\>>>
    and <math|K<rsub|\<sigma\>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>>=1>,

    <\equation*>
      \<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>,<space|2em><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|^>=<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|^>=K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>,<space|2em><wide|\<psi\>|~>=<wide|J<rsup|>|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|\<psi\>|^>.
    </equation*>

    Using Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels> of the kernel norm, we
    obtain\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>
      ><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1|)>>\<otimes\><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>
      ><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>L<rsup|2><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    where

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|>|)>\<assign\><frac|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|><around*|(|z|)>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z|)>
      <wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|>|)>
      \<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|2>|)>
      \<ldots\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>>.>
    </equation*>

    Using furthermore that <math|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>=\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<nu\>>>
    and <math|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>=\<frak-o\><rsup|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>>
    as well as <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>>,
    <math| k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|k|\<bar\>>>
    and<nbsp><math|<eqref|eq:cond-kappabar-one>>, we obtain

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>
      \<zeta\><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1|)>>|)><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>-\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>-\<nu\><around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>>.>>>>><label|eq:weight-bound-2>
    </equation>

    We also observe that, by Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:triple-phi>,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>
      ><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>>L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>
      > <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Moreover, by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels>,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Combining the above estimates and using<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>,
    we conclude that

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>
      ><rsup|\<frak-a\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1|)>>\<otimes\><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-\<alpha\>+\<space\>\<beta\>+<around*|(|\<beta\>-\<gamma\>|)><around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-1|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>-1>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<delta\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>-1>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>>
      <around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|<wide|k|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|\<bar\>>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|\<psi\>|~>|\<\|\|\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where in the last step we used <math|2s-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>=\<delta\>> and
    that <math|\<beta\>\<geqslant\>\<gamma\>>. This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:packaging>Assume that

    <\equation>
      \<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>\<delta\> <wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>-\<alpha\>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>.<label|eq:choice-of-K-and-l>
    </equation>

    Then\ 

    <\equation*>
      H<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>+\<mathD\>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>*<around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>F<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>|)>,<space|2em>\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>,
    </equation*>

    satisfies the bound\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>H<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<vartheta\>-1>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|2<wide|k|\<bar\>>>.
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,>
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>>
    and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    We observe that on account of the perturbative flow equation, it holds

    <\equation*>
      H<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\><neg|\<in\>>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>>B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<psi\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<assign\><around*|{|\<frak-a\>\<in\>\<frak-A\><mid|\|>\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<leqslant\><wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|}>>.
    Then, <with|color|black|working as in the proof of
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:control-of-forcing>> and using
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimate-B-kernels> as well as
    <math|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>=k<around*|(|\<frak-b\>|)>+k<around*|(|\<frak-c\>|)>-1\<leqslant\>2<wide|k|\<bar\>>>,
    we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>H<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\><neg|\<in\>>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>>*K<rsub|\<sigma\>>B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<psi\><rsup|\<otimes\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\><neg|\<in\>>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|B<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\><neg|\<in\>>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-<around*|[|\<frak-b\>|]>-<around*|[|\<frak-c\>|]>-\<gamma\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<frak-a\><neg|\<in\>>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<frak-b\>,\<frak-c\>\<in\>\<frak-A\><around*|(|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<gamma\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>-1><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-A\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*<around*|(|1+<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>>|)><rsup|2<wide|k|\<bar\>>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    <with|color|black|The factor <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>>>
    appearing in the second line arises due to the
    estimate<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-o-zeta-weights> by a bound similar
    to<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-bound-1>.> Now since
    <math|\<beta\>\<geqslant\>\<gamma\>> and
    <math|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>,2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|]>>,
    we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|[|\<frak-a\>|]>-\<gamma\>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>=-\<alpha\>+<around*|(|\<beta\>-\<gamma\>|)>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>+\<delta\>
      \<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>\<geqslant\>-\<alpha\>+\<delta\>
      <wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>-a\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>><around*|(|1+2<wide|\<ell\>|\<bar\>>|)>\<gtr\>0,
    </equation*>

    where we exploited<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogeneity-of-kernels>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:choice-of-K-and-l>. This proves the claim.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:difference-bound>For all

    <\equation>
      \<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>2s-2\<gamma\><label|eq:one-J-bound>
    </equation>

    the following bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|5\<nu\>>
      <around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>|)>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>+\<vartheta\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|2>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<psi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>.
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,>
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)> >
    and <math|\<psi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    <with|color|black|Let <math|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<assign\>1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>>.
    Then>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>|)>=<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|<left|[|2>|<around*|(|J<rsub|\<eta\><rsub|>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>+<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>+3<around*|(|J<rsub|\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|2>*<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>+3<around*|(|J<rsub|\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>*<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\><rsub|>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|2>|<right|]|2>>.
    </equation*>

    Choosing <math|\<eta\><rsub|>=<frac|\<sigma\>|6-5\<sigma\>>>, which
    implies <math|6\<eta\><around*|(|1-\<eta\><rsub|>|)><rsup|-1>=\<sigma\><around*|(|1-\<sigma\>|)><rsup|-1>>,
    the first contribution <math|<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|J<rsub|\<eta\><rsub|>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>>
    vanishes by the Fourier space support property of the product. As for the
    other contributions, we have, for example,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|5\<nu\>>*<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|5>*<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|5>*<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>>*\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|\<sigma\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\>> and
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<approx\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>>,
    by Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:triple-phi>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:schauder-two>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|5\<nu\>><rsub|\<mu\>>*<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-5\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|2>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<psi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-5\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<psi\>|\<interleave\>><rsup|2>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<psi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>.
    </equation*>

    The contributions coming from the terms
    <math|<around*|(|J<rsub|\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|2>*<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
    and <math|<around*|(|J<rsub|\<eta\>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>*<around*|(|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\><rsub|>>\<psi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><rsup|2>>
    satisfy the same bound. Since <math|\<vartheta\>\<leqslant\>2s-2\<gamma\>>,
    this finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <appendix|Auxiliary estimates><label|app:technical>

  We collect in this appendix various technical estimates of general
  character.

  <subsection|Kernel estimates>

  <\definition>
    <label|def:derivatives>For <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>
    and <math|<around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>\<times\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>
    >, we define

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||<wide|A|\<bar\>>|\|>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|i=1><rsup|d><around*|(|<around*|\||A<rsup|i+>|\|>+<around*|\||A<rsup|i->|\|>|)>,<space|2em><around*|\||A|\|>\<assign\>2s*<around*|\||A<rsub|0>|\|>+<around*|\||<wide|A|\<bar\>>|\|>,<space|2em>\<partial\><rsup|A>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsup|A<rsub|0>><rsub|0><big|prod><rsub|i=1><rsup|d><around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|i+>|)><rsup|A<rsub|i+>><around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|i->|)><rsup|A<rsub|i->>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      d<rsup|i,\<pm\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>\<assign\>\<pm\><around*|(|e<rsup|\<pm\>
      i\<varepsilon\><wide|k|~> e<rsub|i>>-1|)>/\<varepsilon\>\<comma\><space|2em>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>\<assign\><around*|(|i
      k<rsub|0>|)><rsup|A<rsub|0>><big|prod><rsub|i=1><rsup|d><around*|(|d<rsup|i,+><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)><rsup|A<rsub|i,+>><around*|(|d<rsup|i,-><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)><rsup|A<rsub|i,->>.
    </equation*>
  </definition>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:J-decay>Let <math|<wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>>
    be the kernel of <math|<wide|J|~><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>>. For all
    <math|n,\<ell\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>and
    <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>
    it holds

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d-2s-<around*|\||A|\|>>*<around*|(|1+<rsup|><around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-n>,>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d-2s-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>*<around*|(|1+<rsup|><around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-n>,>|<cell|>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    uniformly in <math|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Recall that

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsup|A><wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|t,x|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)><rsup|>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>*e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>*t+<wide|k|~><rprime|'>*x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0><rprime|'>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~><rprime|'>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>.
    </equation*>

    We start with the proof of the bound for
    <math|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>>.
    Let <math|><math|h :\<bbb-R\>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>> be defined
    by <math|h<around*|(|\<omega\>|)>\<assign\>-\<omega\>\<partial\><rsub|\<omega\>>j<around*|(|\<omega\>|)>>
    for <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>. It holds

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|[|j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0><rprime|'>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*
      j<rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>|]>=<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<sigma\>|)><rsup|-1><around*|[|h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rsub|0><rprime|'>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*j<rsub|><around*|(|\<tau\>
      q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>+j<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rsub|0><rprime|'>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*h<rsub|><around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>|]><around*|\||<rsub|\<tau\>=2<rsup|-\<ell\>>\<sigma\><rsup|-1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>>|\<nobracket\>>.
    </equation*>

    By the change of variables <math|k<rsub|0>=\<tau\><rsup|2s>*k<rsub|0><rprime|'>>
    and <math|<wide|k|~>=\<tau\> <wide|k|~><rprime|'>> with
    <math|\<tau\>\<equiv\>2<rsup|-\<ell\>>\<sigma\><rsup|-1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>>,
    we get

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|A>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>>|)><around*|(|t,
      x|)>=>>|<row|<cell|=<frac|\<tau\><rsup|-d-2s-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>|2<rsup|\<ell\>>\<sigma\><rsup|2>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>><around*|(|h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*j<rsub|><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>+j<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*
      h<rsub|><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>|)>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rsub|0>*t/\<tau\><rsup|2s>+<wide|k|~>
      *x/\<tau\>|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Recall that <math|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k|)>\<assign\><around*|[|<big|sum><rsub|i=1><rsup|d><around*|(|sin<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>*
    k<rsub|i>|)>/\<varepsilon\>|)><rsup|2>|]><rsup|1/2>>. Using the bound\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|<left|\||1>|\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|<left|(|1>|<around*|[|h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*j<rsub|><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>+j<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>*h<rsub|><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>|]>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|<right|)|1>>|<right|\||1>>\<lesssim\>
      1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>
      1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<rsup|>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsub|>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>,
    </equation*>

    for all <math|<around*|(|a<rsub|0>,<wide|a|~>|)>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|1+d>>
    uniform in <math|<around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>>,
    we show that, for all <math|p,q\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>,

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s><around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|p><around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-1><around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|q><with|color||<around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|j|\<check\>><rsub|\<sigma\>,\<ell\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<frac|\<tau\><rsup|-d-2s-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>|2<rsup|\<ell\>>\<sigma\><rsup|2>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsub|>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-2
      s-<around*|\||A|\|> -1>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    This proves the second of the stated bounds. The first follows by an
    analogous argument.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:K-kernel>Let <math|k\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0>> and
    <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>
    be such that <math|A<rsub|0>\<in\><around*|{|0,1|}>> and
    <math|<around*|\||<wide|A|\<bar\>>|\|>\<leqslant\>2>. The following
    bounds

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsup|A>K<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|\||A|\|>>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<mu\>,\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)>K<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>\<vee\><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|<wide|L|~><rsup|1,k><rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)><wide|K|~><rsup|1,k><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<around*|(|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\><around*|(|1+k|)>>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>,
    </equation*>

    <math|>hold uniformly in <math|><math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|)>> and
    <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    The lemma follows from Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:K-kernel-aux>,
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weight-w>,<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels>
    and <reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels> and the bound

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|w<rsup|2><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t,x|)>\<lesssim\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsup|2>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|4s>|)>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>|)>,>
    </equation*>

    which is a consequence of<nbsp><eqref|eq:dist-parabolic>.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:K-kernel-aux>For <math|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|[|0,1|]>> and
    <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|[|\<tau\>,1|]>> define

    <\equation*>
      <wide|L|^><rsub|\<tau\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+\<tau\><rsup|2s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)>,<space|2em><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1-\<tau\><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)>,<space|2em><wide|K|^><rsub|\<tau\>>\<assign\><wide|L|^><rsub|\<tau\>><rsup|-1><rsup|\<nosymbol\>>,<space|2em><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>\<assign\><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>><rsup|-1>,<space|2em><wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>,\<tau\>>\<assign\><wide|L|^><rsub|\<tau\>><wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>>,<space|2em><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>,\<tau\>>\<assign\><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t|)>\<assign\>1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsup|2>/\<tau\><rsup|4s>>,<space|2em><wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|x|)>\<assign\>1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>/\<tau\><rsup|2>.
    </equation*>

    <math|>Recall that we identify operators with their integral kernels. The
    following statements are true.

    <\enumerate-alpha>
      <item>The bounds

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|^><rsub|\<tau\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<vee\>\<tau\><rsup|2s>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsub|t><wide|K|^><rsub|\<tau\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<vee\>\<tau\>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsup|i,\<pm\>><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<vee\>\<tau\><rsup|2>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<Delta\><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,
      </equation*>

      hold uniformly in <math|><math|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|]>>.

      <item>The bounds

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-<wide|L|^><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|2s>
        \<eta\><rsup|-2s>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>\<tau\>
        <rsup|2> \<eta\><rsup|-2>\<leqslant\>\<tau\><rsup|2s>
        \<eta\><rsup|-2s>,
      </equation*>

      hold uniformly in <math|><math|\<tau\>,\<eta\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|]>>.

      <item>The bounds

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>,\<tau\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>,\<tau\>><rsub|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,
      </equation*>

      hold uniformly in <math|><math|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|]>> and
      <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|[|\<tau\>,1|]>>.
    </enumerate-alpha>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    The first of the bounds stated in Item a) is a<math|>n immediate
    consequence of the fact that

    <\equation*>
      <wide|K|^><rsub|\<tau\>><rsub|><around*|(|t|)>=\<tau\><rsup|-2s>
      <with|color|black|\<bbb-1\><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
      exp<around*|(|-t/\<tau\><rsup|2s>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Let us proceed to the proof of the second of the bounds stated in Item
    a). First, recall that the heat kernel

    <\equation*>
      G<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><around*|(|t,\<bullet\>|)>=e<rsup|-<around*|(|m<rsup|2>-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>t>
    </equation*>

    satisfies the following standard estimate

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|A>G<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|\<bbb-1\><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
      t<rsup|-d/2-<around*|\||A|\|>/2> e<rsup|-m<rsup|2>t-c
      <around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>/t>,<space|2em>A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>.
    </equation*>

    Note that\ 

    <\equation*>
      <wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>=<big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>e<rsup|-<around*|(|1-\<tau\><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)>\<lambda\>><rsup|>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, we have

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||<around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><around*|(|x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>/2><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2-<around*|\||A|\|>/2> e<rsup|-\<lambda\>-c
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>/\<lambda\>>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>/2>e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\><rsup|>|)>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2-<around*|\||A|\|>/2> e<rsup|-\<lambda\>/2-c
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>/\<lambda\>/2>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>/2><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|2-d-<around*|\||A|\|>>e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\><rsup|>|)>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2-<around*|\||A|\|>/2>
      e<rsup|-\<lambda\><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>-c
      /\<lambda\>> \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>/2><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|2-d-<around*|\||A|\|>>e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\>|)>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2-<around*|\||A|\|>/2> e<rsup|-c /\<lambda\>>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\><rsub|>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>/2><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|2-d-<around*|\||A|\|>><around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>/\<tau\><rsup|2>|)><rsup|-2><rsup|>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    uniformly in <math|x\<in\>><math|R<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>\<setminus\><around*|{|0|}>>
    and <math|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|]>.> We also have
    <math|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|0|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|2-d-<around*|\||A|\|>>>.
    As a result, since <math|d=3>, for all
    <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>
    such that <math|<around*|\||A|\|>\<leqslant\>1>, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <big|sum><rsub|x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|d><around*|(|
      1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>/\<tau\><rsup|2>|)>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|2-<around*|\||A|\|>>+\<tau\><rsup|-<around*|\||A|\|>><big|sum><rsub|x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>\<setminus\><around*|{|0|}>><around*|(|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|d>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|2>+<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|4>|)><rsup|-1>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|-<around*|\||A|\|>>,
    </equation*>

    which implies <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<vee\>\<tau\>
    <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsup|i,\<pm\>><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1>.
    The bound <math|\<tau\><rsup|2> <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<Delta\><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1>
    follows now from the identity <math|\<tau\><rsup|2>\<Delta\><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>=<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>-1>.
    This finishes the proof of Item a).\ 

    To prove Item b) observe that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|1-<wide|L|^><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>>=<wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>>-<wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>,\<tau\>>=\<tau\><rsup|2s>
      \<eta\><rsup|-2s><around*|(|<wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>>-1|)>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|1-<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>=<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>-<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>,\<tau\>>=\<tau\><rsup|2>
      \<eta\><rsup|-2><around*|(|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>-1|)>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, by Item a) we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-<wide|L|^><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|2s>
      \<eta\><rsup|-2s><around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|1|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>+
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|^><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|^><rsub|\<eta\>>|)>>|)>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|2s>
      \<eta\><rsup|-2s>
    </equation*>

    and<math|>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|2>
      \<eta\><rsup|-2><around*|(|<around*|\<\|\|\>|1|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>+
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<wide|w|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)>>|)>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|2>
      \<eta\><rsup|-2> .
    </equation*>

    This proves Item b). Item c) follows from Items a) and b).\ 
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:check-K>Let <math|<wide|K|\<check\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>
    >. For <math|N\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>,
    <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<gtr\>3/<around*|(|4N|)>> the following bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|\<check\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2N/<around*|(|2N-1|)>><rsup|><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|d+2s|)>/2N>,
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    We have <math|<wide|K|\<check\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>\<otimes\><math|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>,
    where <math|<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> and
    <math|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> are the kernels of the operators
    <math|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>>>
    and <math|<around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>>,
    respectively. Note that <math|>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>=0><around*|(|t|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<omega\>><around*|\||t|\|><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1><around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|-\<omega\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\>> for all
    <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>. Hence,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|><rsub|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>><rsup|><rsup|><wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2N/<around*|(|2N-1|)>><rsup|>>\<leqslant\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s/2N><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|><rsub|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>><rsup|><rsup|><wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|0><around*|(|\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2N/<around*|(|2N-1|)>><rsup|>>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<omega\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s/2N>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> for all
    <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> provided <math|2N
    <wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<gtr\>1>. Observe that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>=C<rsub|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>e<rsup|-<around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)>\<lambda\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1>\<mathd\>\<lambda\>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|C<rsub|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>\<gtr\>0> is some constant.
    Consequently, by the standard estimate for the heat kernel
    <eqref|eq:est-kernel-G-s-1>, the kernel
    <math|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> satisfies the bound

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2> e<rsup|-\<lambda\>-c
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>/\<lambda\>>\<lambda\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d>e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2> e<rsup|-\<lambda\>/2-c
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>/\<lambda\>/2>\<lambda\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|2<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-d>e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2> e<rsup|-\<lambda\>/<around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>-c
      /\<lambda\>>\<lambda\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|2<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-d>e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2>
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|\<infty\>>
      \<lambda\><rsup|-d/2> e<rsup|-c /\<lambda\>>\<lambda\><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1>
      \<mathd\>\<lambda\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\><rsub|\<omega\>>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d><around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|2<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-d><around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-\<omega\>>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    where we used\ 

    <\equation*>
      e<rsup|-\<lambda\>-c <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>/\<lambda\>>\<leqslant\>e<rsup|-\<lambda\>/2-c
      <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)><rsup|2>/\<lambda\>/2>
      e<rsup|-c<rsup|1/2> <around*|(|<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    We also have <math|<around*|\||<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|0|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|2<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-d>>.
    Hence, for all <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|><rsub|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>><rsup|><rsup|><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|\<bullet\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2N/<around*|(|2N-1|)>><rsup|>>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<omega\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d/2N>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>, provided <math|4N
    <wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<gtr\>d=3>. Using the bounds for
    <math|<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>,
    <math|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> one easily deduces the desired bound
    for <math|<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:hat-K>Let <math|m\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>> and
    <math|<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-1><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-2>>
    and

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1,>\<ldots\>,z<rsub|m>|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z|)>*<wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>+z|)>
      \<cdots\><wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|m>+z|)><space|0.4spc>\<mathd\>z.<label|eq:cal-K>
    </equation*>

    For <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<in\><around*|[|0,1/<around*|(|m+1|)>|)>>,
    the function <math|\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>\<in\>C<around*|(|\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|m>|)>>
    is Hölder continuous and satisfies, for all
    <math|\<omega\>\<geqslant\>0>, the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<omega\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>m>\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
      m> <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
      m>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    <\with|color|black>
      We have

      <\equation*>
        <wide|K|^><rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<otimes\><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,<space|2em>\<cal-K\><rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<otimes\><wide|\<cal-K\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,
      </equation*>

      where <math|<wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>,
      <math|<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> are the kernels of the operators
      <math|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>><rsup|\<nosymbol\>>>
      and <math|<around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>>
      and

      <\eqnarray*>
        <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|<wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,t<rsub|m>|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\>><wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t|)><wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t<rsub|1><with|color|black|+>t|)>\<cdots\><wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t<rsub|m><with|color|black|+>t|)>
        \<mathd\> t,>|<cell|>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|<wide|\<cal-K\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|x<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,x<rsub|m>|)>\<assign\><big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|x|)><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|x<rsub|1><with|color|black|+>x|)>\<cdots\><wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|x<rsub|m><with|color|black|+>x|)>
        \<mathd\> x.>|<cell|>>>>
      </eqnarray*>

      Since <math|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>\<less\>1/2> and <math|d=3> the symbol of
      the operator <math|<around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|<with|color|black|<wide|\<kappa\>|^>-2>>>
      and its derivates are absolutely integrable. As a result, one easily
      shows that for all <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>,

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||<wide|K|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<omega\>><with|color|black|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d>>
        <around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-\<omega\>>,
      </equation*>

      uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>. This implies that
      for all <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>>,

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|<around*|(|1+<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>|)><rsub|><rsup|\<otimes\>m><wide|\<cal-K\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d
        m>> ,
      </equation*>

      uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>. Note that

      <\equation*>
        <wide|K|\<breve\>><rsub|0><around*|(|t|)>=<big|int><frac|exp<around*|(|\<mathi\>p
        t|)>|<around*|(|1+\<mathi\> p|)><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>><frac|d
        p|2\<pi\>>,
      </equation*>

      and

      <\equation*>
        <wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|0><around*|(|t<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,t<rsub|m>|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsup|m>><frac|exp<around*|(|\<mathi\>
        p<rsub|1>t<rsub|1>+\<cdots\>+\<mathi\>p<rsub|m>
        t<rsub|m>|)>|<around*|(|1<with|color|black|->\<mathi\><around*|(|p<rsub|1>+\<cdots\>+p<rsub|m>|)>|)><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>
        <around*|(|1+\<mathi\>p<rsub|1>|)><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>\<cdots\><around*|(|1+\<mathi\>p<rsub|m>|)><rsup|1-<wide|\<kappa\>|^>>><frac|\<mathd\>p<rsub|1>\<cdots\>\<mathd\>p<rsub|m>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|m>>.
      </equation*>

      Observe that for all <math|\<alpha\>,\<beta\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>
      such that <math|1\<less\>\<alpha\>+\<beta\>> there exists
      <math|C\<in\><around*|(|0,\<infty\>|)>> such that\ 

      <\equation*>
        <big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\>><frac|\<mathd\>p|<around*|(|1+<around*|(|p+q|)><rsup|2>|)><rsup|\<alpha\>/2><around*|(|1+p<rsup|2><rsub|>|)><rsup|\<beta\>/2>>\<leqslant\><frac|C|<around*|(|1+q<rsup|2>|)><rsup|\<alpha\>/2\<wedge\>\<beta\>/2>>,
      </equation*>

      for all <math|q\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>. Applying the above observation
      recursively, one shows that

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|<around*|(|1+<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>|)><rsub|><rsup|\<otimes\>m><wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
        m> <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|<around*|(|1+<around*|\||\<bullet\>|\|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>|)><rsub|><rsup|\<otimes\>m><wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|0>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
        m>,
      </equation*>

      <\with|color|black>
        where the factor <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
        m>> in the first step comes from the rescaling

        <\equation*>
          <wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,t<rsub|m>|)>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s
          m><wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|0><around*|(|t<rsub|1>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>,\<ldots\>,t<rsub|m>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>|)>.
        </equation*>
      </with>

      Using the bounds for <math|<wide|\<cal-K\>|\<breve\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>,
      <math|<wide|\<cal-K\>|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> one easily deduces the
      bound stated in the lemma.
    </with>
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:Gdot-decay>For every <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2s|)>>
    and <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>,
    it holds

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A>G<rsub|1/2><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|-d-\<alpha\>><label|eq:G-one-half>
    </equation>

    and

    <\equation>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsup|>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>|)>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-\<alpha\>>,<label|eq:Gdot-bound>
    </equation>

    uniformly in <math|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>.>
  </lemma>

  <\remark>
    The above lemma implies that for any <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2s|)>>,
    <math|\<beta\>\<in\><around*|[|0,d|]>> and
    <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsup|>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<beta\>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<beta\>-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)><rsup|-d-\<alpha\>+\<beta\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|<around*|(|t,x|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>.>
  </remark>

  <\proof>
    We only prove<nbsp><eqref|eq:Gdot-bound> since the proof
    of<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-one-half> follows the same lines. Observe that

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><frac|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'>|)>|)>|)>
      <rsup|>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|2s><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>**e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>*t+<wide|k|~><rprime|'>*x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0><rprime|'>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~><rprime|'>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>.
    </equation*>

    To prove a bound for the <math|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>-norm of

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>t<rsup|a<rsub|0>>x<rsup|<wide|a|~>>
      \<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>,
    </equation*>

    it suffices to control the <math|L<rsup|1>>-norm of

    <\equation>
      <around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,k<rprime|'>|)>\<mapsto\>\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|(|<frac|\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'>|)>|)>|)>
      <rsup|>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|2s><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>|)>.<label|eq:G-dot-proof-Furier-1>
    </equation>

    Since for noninteger parameters <math|s> the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>><rsup|<wide|a|~>>q<rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|2s><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\||<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|\|><rsup|2s-<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>>,
    </equation*>

    uniform in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>, is optimal, the
    <math|L<rsup|1>>-norm of the function<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-Furier-1>
    is bounded uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> only
    if <math|<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>\<less\>d+2s>. As a result, the above
    simple strategy can only be used to prove the lemma for
    <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,<around*|\<lfloor\>|2s|\<rfloor\>>|]>>.
    To establish the claim for every <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2s|)>>
    a more refined argument is needed. To this end, let <math|><math|h
    :\<bbb-R\>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>> be

    <\equation*>
      h<around*|(|\<omega\>|)>\<assign\>-\<omega\>\<partial\><rsub|\<omega\>>j<around*|(|\<omega\>|)>
    </equation*>

    for <math|\<omega\>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>. Moreover, let the families of
    kernels <math|<around*|(|<wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><rsub|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<infty\>|)>>>,
    <math|<around*|(|<wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>>|)><rsub|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<infty\>|)>>>,
    <math|<around*|(|<wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>>|)><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>\<in\><around*|(|0,\<infty\>|)>>>
    be defined by

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>\<assign\>\<tau\><rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
      <frac|j<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>+h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>*e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>*t+<wide|k|~><rprime|'>*x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0><rprime|'>\<mathd\><wide|k|~><rprime|'>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>,>>|<row|<cell|<wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|t,x|)>\<assign\>\<tau\><rsup|-1>\<eta\><rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
      <frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>
      h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>
      h<around*|(|\<tau\>\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>|<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i
      m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>*e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>*t+<wide|k|~><rprime|'>*x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0><rprime|'>\<mathd\><wide|k<rprime|'>|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>,>>|<row|<cell|<wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>\<assign\>\<tau\><rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>><around*|(|<frac|j<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>-<frac|<around*|(|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>|)> h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>
      |<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>|)>e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>t+<wide|k|~><rprime|'>x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0><rprime|'>\<mathd\><wide|k<rprime|'>|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    We claim that

    <\equation>
      <wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|t,x|)>=\<sigma\><rsup|-2><wide|G|~><rsub|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>*/\<sigma\><rsup|>><rsub|><around*|(|t,x|)>,<space|2em><wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>>=<wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>>+<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|\<infty\>><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>>*\<mathd\>\<eta\>.<label|eq:G-dot-proof-identities>
    </equation>

    The first identity follows from

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>>j<rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|\<omega\>|)>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>\<sigma\><rsup|-1>h<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>\<sigma\><rsup|-1>\<omega\>|)>.
    </equation*>

    To verify the second, we use the identities

    <\equation*>
      <frac|h<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>=<frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>
      h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>
      |<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>-<frac|<around*|(|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>|)> h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>
      |<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>
    </equation*>

    as well as

    <\equation*>
      <big|int><rsup|\<infty\>><rsub|1/2>\<eta\><rsup|-1>h<around*|(|\<tau\>\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>=-<big|int><rsup|\<infty\>><rsub|1/2>\<partial\><rsub|\<eta\>>
      j<around*|(|\<tau\>\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>
      \<mathd\>\<eta\>=j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>/2|)>
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>/2|)>=j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Let us motivate the usefulness of the representation of
    <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> given
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-identities>. First, note that if
    <math|<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>\<less\>d+4s>, then the
    <math|L<rsup|1>>-norm of the function

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>\<mapsto\>\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|(|<around*|(|<frac|j<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>-<frac|<around*|(|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+m<rsup|2s>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>
      |<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>|)>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>,
    </equation*>

    is bounded uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
    This stands in contrast to the function
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-Furier-1>, whose <math|L<rsup|1>>-norm
    remains uniformly bounded in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>
    only if <math|<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>\<less\>d+2s>. As a result, it is
    possible to control the <math|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>-norm of the function

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>t<rsup|a<rsub|0>>x<rsup|<wide|a|~>>\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>
    </equation*>

    for <math|<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>\<less\>d+4s>. Since
    <math|<around*|\<lfloor\>|4s|\<rfloor\>>\<geqslant\>3\<gtr\>2s\<gtr\>\<alpha\>>
    this indicates that <math|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>>>
    indeed exhibits the desired decay at infinity. On the other hand, the
    <math|L<rsup|1>>-norm of the function

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>\<mapsto\>\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|(|<frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|
      >q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|>\<eta\><rsup|>
      q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>|<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i
      m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>
    </equation*>

    is bounded uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> for
    all <math|a<rsub|0>,<wide|a|~>> and consequently
    <math|\<partial\><rsup|A>><math|<wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>>> has
    good decay properties. However, the bound for the
    <math|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>-norm of the function

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|t,x|)>\<mapsto\>t<rsup|a<rsub|0>>x<rsup|<wide|a|~>>
      \<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|t,x|)>
    </equation*>

    depends on <math|\<eta\>>. To complete the argument, we must therefore
    control the above norms uniformly in <math|\<varepsilon\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>,
    <math|\<tau\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>> and
    <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,\<infty\>|)>>.

    We claim that the following bounds imply<nbsp><eqref|eq:Gdot-bound>,

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,0|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-d><around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\><rsup|2s>|)><rsup|-d-4>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>><around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-d-3
      ><around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\><rsup|2s>|)><rsup|-d-4>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<eta\><rsup|-2s-1>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-d>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\><rsup|2s>|)><rsup|-d-4>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<eta\><rsup|1-2s>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-d-2>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\><rsup|2s>|)><rsup|-d-4>.>>>>><label|eq:G-dot-proof-bounds>
    </equation>

    <math|>To prove this claim, first use the last two bounds to conclude
    that for all <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2|]>> it holds

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<eta\><rsup|\<alpha\>-1-2s>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      \ <around*|(|1+<around*|\||x|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-d-\<alpha\>>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t|\|><rsub|>/\<tau\><rsup|2s>|)><rsup|-d-4><rsup|>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, the second identity in<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-identities>
    and the above bound yield

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<alpha\>>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      \ <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-d>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-\<alpha\>>
    </equation*>

    for <math|\<alpha\>\<in\><around*|[|0,2s|)>>. Combining the above
    estimate with the first estimate in<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-bounds> we
    obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><rsub|\<alpha\>>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      \ <around*|(|1+<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>|)>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-d>
      <around*|(|1+<around*|\||t,x|\|><rsub|s>/\<tau\>|)><rsup|-\<alpha\>>.
    </equation*>

    The bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:Gdot-bound> follows now from the first identity
    in<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-identities>.\ 

    It remains to prove<nbsp><eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-bounds>. Starting from the
    bound for <math|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>><around*|(|t,x|)>>,
    we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>=>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em>=\<tau\><rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
      <frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\><around*|\||k<rprime|'><rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|\<tau\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|\<tau\>\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>|)>|<around*|(|k<rsub|0><rprime|'>-i
      m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>,<wide|k|~><rprime|'>|)>**e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rprime|'><rsub|0>*t+<wide|k|~><rprime|'>*x|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0><rprime|'>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~><rprime|'>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em>=\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>\<eta\><rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>><frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>h<around*|(|\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i
      \<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>e<rsup|i<around*|(|k<rsub|0>t/\<tau\><rsup|2s>+<wide|k|~>x/\<tau\>|)>><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where we set <math|k<rsub|0>=\<tau\><rsup|2s>k<rprime|'><rsub|0><rsup|>>
    and <math|<wide|k|~>=\<tau\><wide|k|~><rprime|'>>. It follows that

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s*><around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|a<rsub|0>><around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-1><around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|\||<around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|1em>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>\<eta\><rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>><around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|[|<frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>h<around*|(|\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i
      \<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>|]>|\|><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>.>>>>><label|eq:integral-to-control>
    </equation>

    Observe the following:

    <\itemize>
      <item>In<nbsp><eqref|eq:integral-to-control>, the factor
      <math|h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>>
      restricts the integration domain to
      <math|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>\<in\><around*|[|1,2|]>>.
      In this region, the denominator is never vanishing. More precisely

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|\|><rsup|2>\<geqslant\>1.
      </equation*>

      <item>Similarly, the factor <math|h<around*|(|\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>>
      restricts the integration domain to those <math|<wide|k|~>> such that
      <math|><math|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>\<in\><around*|[|\<eta\><rsup|-1>,2\<eta\><rsup|-1>|]>>.
      Thus, on the integration domain <math|>

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>>q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|2s-<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>\<approx\>\<eta\><rsup|<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>-2s>.
      </equation*>
    </itemize>

    On account of these comments, we have the following bound for the
    integrand

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|(|<frac|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>h<around*|(|\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<eta\><rsup|<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>-2s>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>1<rsub|<around*|[|1,2|]>><around*|(|\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsub|>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>,
    </equation*>

    for all <math|<around*|(|a<rsub|0>,<wide|a|~>|)>\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|1+d>>.
    This implies that

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s*><around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|p><around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-1><around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|q><around*|\||<around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|^><rsub|\<tau\>,\<eta\>>|)><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>\<eta\><rsup|q-2s-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>1<rsub|<around*|[|1,2|]>><around*|(|\<eta\>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsub|>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>
      <frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>\<eta\><rsup|q-2s-d-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/<around*|(|\<tau\>\<eta\>|)>>>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>
      1<rsub|<around*|[|1,2|]>><around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/<around*|(|\<tau\>\<eta\>|)>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>
      <frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>\<eta\><rsup|q-2s-d-1>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    for any <math|p,q\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|+>.> The proof for
    <math|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>>
    is similar. Working as in the previous case, we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s*><around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|p><around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-1><around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|q><around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,
      x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|-d-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>
      \<times\><with|font-series|bold|>>>|<row|<cell|\<times\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>><around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|[|<around*|(|<frac|j<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>+<frac|<around*|(|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)>h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>
      |<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i \<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>|)>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|]>|\|><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    As above, also here the denominators are non-vanishing on the integration
    domain, more precisely,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||i k<rsub|0>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|\|>\<geqslant\>1<space|2em>and<space|2em><around*|\||<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i
      \<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|\|>\<geqslant\>1.
    </equation*>

    In the first term, this is due to the factor
    <math|h<around*|(|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>>,
    which restricts the integration domain to
    <math|q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>\<in\><around*|[|1,2|]>>,
    while in the second one this is due to the factor
    <math|h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>>, which
    restricts the integration domain to <math|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>\<in\><around*|[|1,2|]>>.
    Since <math|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>>q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>><math|q<rsup|4s-<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>,
    we get

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|a<rsub|0>>\<partial\><rsub|<wide|k|~>><rsup|<wide|a|~>><around*|[|<around*|(|<frac|j<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>
      h<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>+<frac|<around*|(|i
      k<rsub|0><rprime|'>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)>
      h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>
      j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>
      |<around*|(|k<rsub|0>-i \<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>|)><rsup|2>+q<rsup|4s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>|)>*d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|]>|\|>\<lesssim\>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em>
      <application-space|2em>\<lesssim\> 1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>
      1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<rsup|>q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsub|>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>
      <around*|(|1\<vee\>q<rsup|4s-<around*|\||<wide|a|~>|\|>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    This implies that, for <math|q\<less\>d+4s>,

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s*><around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|p><around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-1><around*|\||x|\|>|)><rsup|q><around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>-1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsub|>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)><around*|(|1\<vee\>q<rsup|4s-q><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>|)>\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>\<mathd\><wide|k|~>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<tau\><rsup|-d-<around*|\||A|\|>-1>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Since <math|d+4s\<gtr\>d+3> the bound for
    <math|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>>> follows.
    Finally, we discuss the first bound in <eqref|eq:G-dot-proof-bounds>. By
    changing the variables as above, we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s
      ><around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|p><around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,0|)>|\|>\<leqslant\>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em><application-space|2em><application-space|2em>\<leqslant\>\<tau\><rsup|-1-d-<around*|\||A|\|>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>><around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|p><around*|[|<frac|j<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)><rsup|>|)>+h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)><rsup|>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\><rsup|>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|]>|\|>\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>\<mathd\><wide|k|~>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    We use the same argument as for <math|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<check\>><rsub|\<tau\>>>:
    indeed both terms in the integrand have non-vanishing denominators due to
    the factors <math|h<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)><rsup|>|)>>
    and <math|h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>>,
    respectively. Analogously, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsub|k<rsub|0>><rsup|p>
      <around*|[|<frac|j<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>h<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)><rsup|>|)>+h<around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s><rsup|>|)>j<around*|(|q<rsup|><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)><rsup|>|)>|i
      k<rsub|0>+\<tau\><rsup|2s>m<rsup|2s>+q<rsup|2s><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|<wide|k|~>|)>>d<rsup|A><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>><around*|(|k<rsub|0>,<wide|k|~>|)>|]>|\|>\<lesssim\>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)>,
    </equation*>

    and thus

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|\<tau\><rsup|-2s > <around*|\||t|\|>|)><rsup|p><around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|~><rsub|\<tau\>><around*|(|t,x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|-1-d-<around*|\||A|\|>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\><rsup|\<ast\>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>/\<tau\>>>1<rsub|<around*|[|0,2|]>><around*|(|<around*|\||k<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|1/2s>|)><frac|\<mathd\>k<rsub|0>*\<mathd\><wide|k|~>|<around*|(|2\<pi\>|)><rsup|d+1>>\<lesssim\>\<tau\><rsup|-1-d-<around*|\||A|\|>><around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<tau\><rsup|-1>|)><rsup|-d>=\<tau\><rsup|-1-<around*|\||A|\|>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-d>.
    </equation*>

    This concludes the proof.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Properties of the weights><label|sec:weight-properties>

  We collect here some important properties of the various weights introduced
  throughout the paper.

  <\with|color|black>
    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:fractional-bound>For <math|\<alpha\>\<geqslant\>0>,we have

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>
        \<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<alpha\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
        a>
      </equation*>

      uniformly in <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
    </lemma>

    <\proof>
      Let <math|f\<in\>C<rsup|2><around*|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>|)>.> Recall
      that, by<nbsp><eqref|eq:integral-rep-frac-lap-discrete>, we have

      <\equation*>
        <around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>
        f<around*|(|x|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|y|)>*<around*|(|f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|x-y|)>|)>
        \<mathd\>y,<space|2em>x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>,
      </equation*>

      where the kernel <math|H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s>:\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>>
      is positive and such that <math|H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|0|)>=0>,
      <math|H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x|)>=H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|-x|)>>
      and

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|x|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>*<around*|\||x|\|><rsup|-d-2s>,<space|2em>x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>.
      </equation*>

      Let <math|B<around*|(|\<delta\>|)>> the ball in
      <math|\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>> of radius
      <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0> centred at the origin and
      <math|B<rsup|c><around*|(|\<delta\>|)>\<assign\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|d>\<setminus\>B<around*|(|\<delta\>|)>>.
      For any <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0>, we have

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>
        f<around*|(|x|)>|\|>\<leqslant\><frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|\<delta\>|)>>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|y|)>*<around*|(|2f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|x+y|)>-f<around*|(|x-y|)>|)>
        \<mathd\>y+<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|\<delta\>|)>>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|y|)>*<around*|(|f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|x-y|)>|)>
        \<mathd\>y.
      </equation*>

      To bound the first term observe that

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||2f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|x+y|)>-f<around*|(|x-y|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\>\<nabla\>f|\<\|\|\>>
        <around*|\||y|\|><rsup|2>,
      </equation*>

      by Taylor's theorem, where <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\>\<nabla\>f|\<\|\|\>>>
      denotes the supremum norm of the Hessian of <math|f> in the continuum.
      <math|>As a result, we obtain

      \;

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||<big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|\<delta\>|)>>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|y|)>*<around*|(|2f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|x+y|)>-f<around*|(|x-y|)>|)>
        \<mathd\>y|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\>\<nabla\>f|\<\|\|\>><big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|\<delta\>|)>><around*|\||y|\|><rsup|2-d-2s>
        \<mathd\>y\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\>\<nabla\>f|\<\|\|\>>
        \<delta\><rsup|2-2s>.
      </equation*>

      Moreover, we have

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\||<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|\<delta\>|)>>H<rsup|<around*|(|\<varepsilon\>|)>><rsub|s><around*|(|y|)>*<around*|(|f<around*|(|x|)>-f<around*|(|x-y|)>|)>
        \<mathd\>y|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>>
        <big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|\<delta\>|)>><around*|\||y|\|><rsup|-d-2s>
        \<mathd\>y\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>>
        \<delta\><rsup|-2s>.
      </equation*>

      To conclude, we apply the above estimates with
      <math|f<around*|(|x|)>=\<zeta\><rsup|\<alpha\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|t,x|)>>
      and choose <math|\<delta\>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a
      s>>.
    </proof>
  </with>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:D-zeta>We have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><with|color|black|\<frak-D\><rsub|s>><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      a>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Recall that <math|\<mu\><rsub|s>> denotes the kernel defined
    by<nbsp><eqref|eq:int-kernel>, which is local in time. Let
    <math|B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>> the ball of radius
    <math|\<delta\>\<gtr\>0> centred at <math|z\<in\>\<Lambda\>>.
    By<nbsp><eqref|eq:D>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|[|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><with|color|black|\<frak-D\><rsub|s>><around*|(|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>|)><around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)><big|int><around*|[|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)><big|int><rsub|<with|color|black|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>>><around*|[|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)><big|int><rsub|<with|color|black|B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>>><around*|[|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z|)>|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<bbb-I\>+\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    On <math|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>\<assign\>\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>\<setminus\>B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>>
    we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<bbb-I\>=<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>><around*|[|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|1/3><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>-1|]><rsup|2>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>><around*|[|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-2/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>+1|]>
      \<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-2/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>+\<delta\><rsup|-2s>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Recall that

    <\equation*>
      \<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-2/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>\<lesssim\><with|color|black|\<zeta\><rsup|-2/3><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>=<around*|\<langle\>|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a>.<around*|(|z-z<rprime|'>|)>|\<rangle\>><rsub|s><rsup|2/3>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a><around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>><rprime|'>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/3>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|z=<around*|(|z<rsup|0>,<wide|z|\<bar\>>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>>
    and <math|z<rprime|'>=<around*|(|z<rsup|0>,<wide|z|\<bar\>><rprime|'>|)>\<in\>\<Lambda\>>.
    Since <math|2s\<gtr\>2/3>,

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-2/3><around*|(|z<rprime|'>|)>
      \<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|B<rsup|c><around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a><around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>><rprime|'>|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|1/3>\<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<delta\><rsup|-2s>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a/3>\<delta\><rsup|-2s+2/3>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Let us bound the second term. Thanks to the smoothness of
    <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>> in space, by Taylor's theorem

    <\equation*>
      \<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>\<leqslant\>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3><around*|(|z|)><big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>
      <around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>><rprime|'>-z|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>
      \<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Since <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<nabla\><rsub|>\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|-1/3>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a>>
    and <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|2/3>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>1>,
    we conclude

    <\equation*>
      \<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a><big|int><rsub|B<around*|(|z,\<delta\>|)>><around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>><rprime|'>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>
      \<mu\><rsub|s><around*|(|z,\<mathd\>z<rprime|'>|)>\<lesssim\>\<delta\><rsup|2-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s*a>.
    </equation*>

    Choosing now <math|\<delta\>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>>,
    we get

    <\equation*>
      \<bbb-I\>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a*s>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a/3><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s
      a-2a/3>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a*s>,<space|2em>\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>\<lesssim\>\<delta\><rsup|2-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2a>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s*a>.
    </equation*>

    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:weight-interaction>The bound

    <\equation*>
      <frac|<around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    We have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<frac|<around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<frac|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>><frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<frac|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>><frac|<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2-\<flat\>>|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>><frac|<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2-\<flat\>>|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2-\<flat\>>|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2>|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    which proves the claim.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:weight-interaction-v>For all <math|\<omega\>\<gtr\>0>, the
    following bound

    <\equation*>
      <frac|<around*|(|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<omega\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<omega\>>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<mu\>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|(|0,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By Def.<nbsp><reference|def:weights-kernels>,
    <math|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>=0> if
    <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)>\<leqslant\>1>.
    As a consequence,\ 

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<frac|<around*|(|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)><rsub|><rsup|><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)><rsub|><rsup|><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>><around*|(|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<omega\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<omega\>><frac|<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>+St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)><rsub|><rsup|><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>|<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|>+St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)><rsub|><rsup|><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>><around*|(|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    is non-vanishing only if <math|St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)>\<gtr\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>>.
    Hence

    <\equation*>
      <frac|<around*|(|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|w<rsup|<around*|(|1+m|)>,\<omega\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>\<leqslant\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<omega\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<omega\>><frac|<around*|(|2
      St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)><rsub|><rsup|><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>|<around*|(|St<around*|(|z,y<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,y<rsub|m>|)><rsub|><rsup|><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<omega\>>><around*|(|1-v<rsup|<around*|(|m+1|)>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<omega\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<omega\>>,
    </equation*>

    which proves the claim.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Norm estimates>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-1-h>The cumulant norms introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-cumulants> satisfy the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly over <math|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
    <math|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-2>, Young's inequality and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:weight-interaction> we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<around*|(|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>2>|)>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      <around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>>|)><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    This proves the statement.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-1-v>The kernel norms introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels> satisfy the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly over <math|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
    <math|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-o-2>, Young's inequality,
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:weight-interaction-v> and
    <math|<wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>w<rsup|<around*|(|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>|)>,\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><rsub|\<mu\>>>
    we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<with|font|Euler|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>>>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><wide|w|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><wide|w|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>
      <around*|(|<wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>\<kappa\><rsub|\<frak-o\>>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<with|font|Euler|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>=w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|2><rsup|><around*|(|z|)>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><rsup|><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>\<cdots\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><rsup|><around*|(|z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>.>
    </equation*>

    This proves the statement.
  </proof>

  <\with|color|black>
    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:aux-weight>The kernel norms introduced in
      Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels> satisfy the bound

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>
        >\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><rsub|><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>
        >|]>\<cdot\><wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>
        >|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>,
      </equation*>

      uniformly over <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
      <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>>, where <math|<wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>
      is a smooth weight on <math|\<Lambda\><rsub|0><rsup|1+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>>
      such that <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>1>
      uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and

      <\equation*>
        supp <wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<subset\><around*|<left|{|3>|<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>
        <mid|\|> \<forall\>i <around*|\||z<rsub|0>-z<rsub|i,0>|\|>\<leqslant\>c
        <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>,\<forall\>i
        <around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>><rsub|i>|\|>\<leqslant\>c
        <around*|(|\<varepsilon\>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>|)>|<right|}|3>>
      </equation*>

      for some <math|c\<gtr\>0> independent of <math|\<mu\>> and
      <math|\<varepsilon\>>.
    </lemma>
  </with>

  <\remark>
    Note that for <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>>\<geqslant\>\<varepsilon\>>
    the weight <math|<wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>> has comparable
    support property to the weight <math|v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>.
  </remark>

  <\proof>
    Let <math|k=k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>. Since
    <math|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>
    >=<wide|L|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|<rsup|>
    >> by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels>
    and<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<around*|[|<wide|L|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>=<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<around*|[|<around*|(|L<rsub|\<mu\>>\<otimes\><around*|(|L<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|2>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>k>|)><around*|(|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>|]>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where <math|L<rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2>>.
    Integrating by parts each of the differential operators appearing in the
    tensor product <math|L<rsub|\<mu\>>\<otimes\><around*|(|L<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|2>|)><rsup|\<otimes\>k>>,
    we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>=<big|sum><rsub|A,B\<in\>I>c<rsub|A,B>
      <around*|(|D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|A><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><around*|(|
      <around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>
      D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|B>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    Here <math|I >is a finite index set, <math|<around*|(|c<rsub|A,B>|)><rsub|A,B\<in\>I>>
    is a family of real constants and <math|<around*|(|D<rsup|A>|)><rsub|A\<in\>I>>
    is a family of \ differential operators on <math|\<Lambda\><rsup|1+k>>.
    Each <math|D<rsup|A>> has the form

    \;

    <\equation*>
      D<rsup|A><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|(|D<rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|t,\<mu\>>\<otimes\>
      D<rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|x,\<mu\>>|)>\<otimes\>\<cdots\>\<otimes\><around*|(|D<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|t,\<mu\>>\<otimes\>
      D<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|x,\<mu\>>|)>,
    </equation*>

    with temporal operators

    <\equation*>
      D<rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|t,\<mu\>>,\<ldots\>,D<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|t,\<mu\>>\<in\><around*|{|1,<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)>|}>
    </equation*>

    and spatial operators

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|D<rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><rsub|x,\<mu\>>,\<ldots\>D<rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|x,\<mu\>>\<in\>\<b-D\><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>>\<cup\><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2>\<b-D\><rsup|<around*|(|1|)>>\<cup\><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2>\<b-D\><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>>,>
    </equation*>

    where

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|\<b-D\><rsup|<around*|(|l|)>>=<around*|{|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|<around*|\||A|\|>>
      T<rsub|x> \<partial\><rsup|A> <mid|\|>
      A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>,
      <around*|\||A|\|>\<leqslant\>l,x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|}>>.
    </equation*>

    <with|color|black|The symbol <math|\<partial\><rsup|A>> denotes the
    derivative operator on <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>
    introduced in Def.<nbsp><reference|def:derivatives>, and <math|T<rsub|x>>
    stands for the translation by <math|x\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|d><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>.
    The highest-order operator is either <math|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)>>
    or <math|<around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2>>;
    all lower-order operators are included as well. Since we are on a
    lattice, applying the Leibniz rule requires considering spatial operators
    that shift the spatial variable by multiples of lattice spacings in
    certain directions.>

    With this decomposition, it is straightforward to see that

    <\equation*>
      D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|A><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<big|otimes><rsub|i=0><rsup|k><around*|<left|(|2>|D<rsup|<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|t,\<mu\>><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|-1>\<otimes\>D<rsup|<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|x,\<mu\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-2>|<right|)|2>>.
    </equation*>

    By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:K-kernel-aux>, we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|A><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,
    </equation*>

    where

    <\equation*>
      <with|font|Euler|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k>|)>=w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|2><rsup|><around*|(|z|)>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><rsup|><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>\<cdots\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><rsup|><around*|(|z<rsub|k>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Therefore, by<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-o-2> and Young's inequality, we
    conclude

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|A,B><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<around*|(|D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|A><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><around*|(|
      <around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\>
      D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|B>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      |]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|A,B><around*|\<\|\|\>|D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|A><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|B>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\><rsub|>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>F<rsup|\<frak-a\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>,>>>>><label|eq:decomp-Kolmogorov>
    </equation>

    where in the last step we introduced the weight

    <\equation*>
      <wide|v|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\>sup<rsub|B\<in\>I><around*|\||D<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|B>v<rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\|>.
    </equation*>

    This proves the first of the stated bounds, while the second one is
    trivial.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-1-K-coeff>The kernel norms introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-kernels> satisfy the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<around*|(|1-<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly over <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>,
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>> and
    <math|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:aux-weight> we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|[|<around*|(|1-<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-v<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<around*|(|<wide|L|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<mu\>>.
    </equation*>

    By<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w-o>, Young's inequality,
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:K-kernel> and
    <math|<wide|w|~><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<leqslant\><wide|w|~><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>>
    we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <rsub|><tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<around*|(|<wide|L|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|<wide|L|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)><wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|<with|font|Euler|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>>>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<frak-o\><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<cdot\><around*|[|<wide|K|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\><wide|w|~><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|F|\<dot\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where <math|<with|color|black|\<frak-w\><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>=w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|2><rsup|><around*|(|z|)>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><rsup|><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>\<cdots\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><rsup|><around*|(|z<rsub|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\>|)>>|)>>>.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-1-K>The cumulant norms introduced in
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-cumulants> satisfy the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|(|1-K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>*<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly over <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By Young's inequality, Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:K-kernel> and
    <math|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>\<leqslant\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\>>>
    we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|(|1-K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|<left|[|1>|<around*|(|1\<otimes\><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)>K<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|<right|]|1>>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>-1|)>K<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|)>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    as claimed.
  </proof>

  <subsection|Schauder estimates>

  In this section, we establish estimates that characterise the spacetime
  regularity of distributions <math|\<phi\>> in terms of the size of
  <math|\<cal-L\>\<phi\>>.

  <\with|color|black>
    <\lemma>
      <label|lem:LP-block>For all <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>
      the following bounds

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|\||A|\|>>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|-1><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>,<space|2em><space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>
      </equation*>

      hold uniformly in <math|i\<geqslant\>-1>.
    </lemma>

    <\proof>
      The estimates follows from the identity
      <math|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>>=2<rsup|-i-2>>
      and Def.<nbsp><reference|def:space-LP> of the spatial Littlewood-Paley
      blocks.
    </proof>
  </with>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-for-G>For all <math|A\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsub|0><rsup|<around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>>>
    the following bounds

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>G|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsub|<rsup|>><rsup|2s>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<partial\><rsup|A><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1-<around*|\||A|\|><rsub|s>>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>,
    </equation*>

    hold uniformly in <math|i\<geqslant\>-1> and
    <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|(|1/2,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Recall that <math|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>> is the spatial
    Littlewood-Paley block, <math|\<zeta\><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\><around*|(|1+<around*|\||z|\|><rsup|2><rsub|s>|)><rsup|-1/2>>
    and note that

    <\equation*>
      G=<big|int><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>><rsup|1><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<mu\>+<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|\<mu\><rsub|i>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<mu\>>
      \<mathd\>\<mu\>+G<rsub|1/2>.
    </equation*>

    Taking into account Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:weight-properties><nbsp>a),
    we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>G|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>><big|int><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      \<mathd\>\<mu\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|-1><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|\<mu\><rsub|i>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      \<mathd\>\<mu\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|-1><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)>G<rsub|1/2>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      .>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Consequently, using Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:Gdot-decay> we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>G|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1>
      \<mathd\>\<mu\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|\<mu\><rsub|i>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|><rsup|2s-3>
      \<mathd\>\<mu\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<times\>1>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsub|<rsup|>><rsup|2s>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsub|<rsup|>><rsup|2>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsub|><rsup|2s-2>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsub|<rsup|>><rsup|2s>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    This proves the first bound. The second bound follows directly from
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:Gdot-decay>. To show the third bound notice
    that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|1><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      \<mathd\>\<sigma\>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|1><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>.
    </equation*>

    This completes the proof.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:schauder-full>It holds

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-2\<gamma\>><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>>,<label|eq:schauder>
    </equation>

    uniformly in <math|\<phi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>,
    <math|i\<geqslant\>-1> and <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>>,
    where the norms <math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>>=><math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
    and <math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>=><math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
    are defined by<nbsp><eqref|eq:sol-norm> and<nbsp><eqref|eq:sharp-norm>.
    In particular, for <math|<wide|\<gamma\>|^>\<gtr\>\<gamma\>>, it holds

    <\equation*>
      <big|sum><rsub|i>2<rsup|-<wide|\<gamma\>|^> i>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|<left|[|3>|<around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-2\<gamma\>><around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>|<right|]|3>>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<in\>*<around*|[|1/2,1|)>>,
    <math|\<eta\>\<in\><around*|[|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>> and
    <math|\<phi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    First observe that

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|j><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*\<chi\><rsub|j>*<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|j><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*\<chi\><rsub|j>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>*<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>sup<rsub|j><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>*<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>,<label|eq:schauder-change-weights>
    </equation>

    uniformly in <math|i\<geqslant\>-1> and
    <math|\<eta\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>. To obtain the last
    estimate we used the fact that

    <\equation>
      sup<rsub|j><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*\<chi\><rsub|j>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|j><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*\<chi\><rsub|j>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>.<label|eq:bound-weight-sch>
    </equation>

    Indeed note that if <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<leqslant\>\<eta\>\<leqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|j>>,
    we have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*\<chi\><rsub|j>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|a><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|j>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-a>|)><rsup|-\<nu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|j>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>.
    </equation*>

    On the other hand, if <math|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>,
    then <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>*\<chi\><rsub|j>*\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|j>><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>1>
    and <math|1\<leqslant\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|j>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>>.
    Hence, the bound <eqref|eq:bound-weight-sch> follows. By the estimate
    <eqref|eq:schauder-change-weights> it suffices to establish the bound
    <eqref|eq:schauder> with the weight <math|\<rho\><rsub|\<eta\>>> replaced
    by <math|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>>. To prove the latter bound note that

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|sup<rsub|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>\<leqslant\>\<eta\>\<leqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<vee\>sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<vee\><around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<gamma\>>
      sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    In order to bound the supremum in the last line above we shall use the
    following decomposition

    <\equation*>
      \<phi\>=\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>+<around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>,<space|2em>\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>.
    </equation*>

    Note that

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>>+sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <with|color|black|<with|color|black|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>,
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsup|1/3><rsub|\<eta\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\><around|\<interleave\>|\<phi\>|\<interleave\>>.
    </equation*>

    To complete the proof it is now enough to show that

    <\equation>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-3\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>,<label|eq:schauder-proof-bound>
    </equation>

    uniformly in <math|\<eta\>\<geqslant\>\<mu\><rsub|i>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>.
    To this end, recall that <math|L<rsub|\<mu\>>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2*s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><rsup|><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>,
    where <math|<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<assign\><rsup|><rsup|\<nosymbol\>><around*|(|1-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2>\<Delta\>|)><rsup|2>>.
    Now

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<phi\>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>L<rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)><around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>\<partial\><rsub|t>|)><around*|(|K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<partial\><rsub|t>G
      <around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<bbb-I\>+\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    We have the following bound for the first term

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>
      \<bbb-I\>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    The above estimates follow from<with|font-shape|italic|>
    Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:weight-properties><nbsp>a),
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-for-G> and the bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\>1,
    </equation*>

    which is a consequence of Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:LP-block>. In order
    to bound <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>
    \<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>> we first note that

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|t>G=1-<around*|(|m<rsup|2>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>|)>G
    </equation*>

    and write

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>\<partial\><rsub|t>G
      <around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>-<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><around*|(|m<rsup|2>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>|)><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>G
      <around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>+\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|2>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    We have the following bound for <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>
    \<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>>:

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>
      \<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|1>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|><around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>*<rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<with|color|magenta|>\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    For <math|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>\<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|2>|\<\|\|\>>>
    we have, exploiting Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-for-G>,

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>
      \<bbb-I\>\<bbb-I\><rsub|2>|\<\|\|\>>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|><around*|(|m<rsup|2>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>|)><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><around*|(|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i-1>+<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>+<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i+1>|)>\<Delta\><rsub|i>G
      <around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|m<rsup|2>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>|)><rsup|><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><around*|(|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i-1><rsup|>+<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>+<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i+1>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>G|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|(|1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>|\<\|\|\>>*<rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|>K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where we used that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|\<zeta\><rsub|><rsup|>|\<bar\>><rsup|-1><around*|(|m<rsup|2>+<around*|(|-\<Delta\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>|)><rsup|s>|)><rsup|><wide|L|\<bar\>><rsub|\<eta\>><around*|(|<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i-1><rsup|>+<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i><rsup|>+<wide|\<Delta\>|\<bar\>><rsub|i+1>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>\<lesssim\>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\><rsub|i>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>,
    </equation*>

    which follows from Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:LP-block>. Summing up, we
    have\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|><rsub|><around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|><rsub|>
      K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-3\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|3\<gamma\>>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|\<eta\>><rsup|><rsub|>
      K<rsub|\<eta\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-3\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<bullet\>>\<cal-L\>\<phi\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>.
    </equation*>

    This proves the bound<nbsp><eqref|eq:schauder-proof-bound> and completes
    the proof of the lemma.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:schauder-two>Let <math|J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<assign\>1-J<rsub|\<eta\>>>.
    We have

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>,
    </equation*>

    uniformly in <math|<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,\<mu\>,\<eta\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>,
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>\<vee\><wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>,1|)>>
    and <math|\<phi\>\<in\>\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>,
    where the norm <math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>>=><math|<around|\<interleave\>|\<bullet\>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sharp\>,<wide|\<mu\>|\<bar\>>>>
    is defined by<nbsp><eqref|eq:sharp-norm>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Using Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:weight-properties><nbsp>a) and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-for-G>, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*<around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|\<zeta\><rsup|-1>|)>>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>.
    </equation*>

    Next, we note that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*J<rsub|\<gtr\>\<eta\>>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>=<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*<around*|(|G-G<rsub|\<eta\>>|)>\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>*<around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|3>*\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s><around*|\<\|\|\>|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|3>*\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>>\<lesssim\>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<eta\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s>*<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-3\<gamma\>>*<around|\<interleave\>|\<cal-L\>\<phi\><rsub|\<bullet\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|#>,
    </equation*>

    on account of Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:triple-phi> and the identity
    <math|\<rho\><rsub|\<sigma\>>=\<zeta\><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<nu\>>>.
    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <appendix|Flow equation estimates><label|app:flow-eq>

  <subsection|Estimates for <math|\<cal-A\>> and
  <math|\<cal-B\>>><label|sec:A-B-cumulants>

  Goal of this section is to prove the bounds for the operators
  <samp|<math|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>>>> and
  <math|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>> appearing in the flow
  equation for cumulants<nbsp><eqref|eq:cumulant-flow>, thereby proving
  Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:flow-cumulants>. We begin with the definition of
  the first operator:

  <\equation*>
    <big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|i=1><rsup|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>,
  </equation*>

  where

  \;

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|\<ell\><rprime|'>=0><rsup|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1><big|sum><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>><rsub|k<rprime|'>=0><around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em>\<times\><with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|i><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
    \<frak-K\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+1><around*|<left|(|1>|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|i-1>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|i+1>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>>|<right|)|1>>.>>>>><label|eq:specific-operator-A>
  </equation>

  The summation index <math|\<b-b\>> is constrained by the allowed values of
  <math|<around*|(|\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<rprime|'>|)>> appearing on the
  right-hand side. The operator <math|<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|i><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
  acts by applying <math|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> to the output
  variable of the <math|<around*|(|i+1|)>>-th kernel, and by inserting the
  resulting function into the last input variable of the <math|i>-th kernel.
  <with|color|black|This operator generalises
  <math|<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
  defined in<nbsp><eqref|eq:frak-B-operator>, which appears in the flow
  equation for the effective force kernels<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-kernels>.>

  We now proceed with the definition of the second operator:

  <\equation*>
    <big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|i=1<rsup|>><rsup|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>><big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>,
  </equation*>

  where

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<big|sum><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<assign\><big|sum><rsub|I<rsub|1>,I<rsub|2>><big|sum><rsub|\<ell\><rprime|'>=0><rsup|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1><big|sum><rsup|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>><rsub|k<rprime|'>=0><around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>\<times\>>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em>\<space\><application-space|2em>\<times\><with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
    <around*|<left|(|2>|\<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|1>>,F<rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<rprime|'>+1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
    \<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|2>|\|>+1><around*|<left|(|1>|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|2>>|<right|)|1>>|<right|)|2>>.>>>>><label|eq:specific-operator-B>
  </equation>

  Here, for a fixed <math|i\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>|}>>,
  the sum <math|<big|sum><rsub|I<rsub|1>,I<rsub|2>>> runs over all the
  partitions of the set

  <\equation*>
    I<rsub|1>\<sqcup\>I<rsub|2>=<around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,i-1,i+1,\<ldots\>,n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>|}>.
  </equation*>

  The summation index <math|\<b-b\>> is now constrained by the allowed values
  of <math|<around*|(|I<rsub|1>,I<rsub|2>,\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<rprime|'>|)>>
  on the right-hand side of <eqref|eq:specific-operator-B>. For precise
  definitions of the operators <samp|<math|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>>>>
  and <math|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>>>,
  see<nbsp><cite|duchFlowEquationApproach2021>.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-A>For all <math|<with|font-series|bold|a>\<in\><with|font-series|bold|\<b-A\>>>
    and <math|i\<leqslant\>n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>>, the
    following bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-1><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    Recalling<nbsp><eqref|eq:specific-operator-A>, our task is to analyse the
    expression

    <\equation*>
      \ <with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|i><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      \<frak-K\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Using <math|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>=1> and
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>, we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|
      K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>,K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>><around*|<left|(|2>|<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|i><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      \<frak-K\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>>|)>|<right|)|2>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|=<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|i><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+1,K<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>+1>\<frak-K\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>+1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|1>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<rprime|'>+1|)>>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\><rprime|'>|]>,<around*|(|k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,\<ldots\>,F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|n<around*|(|\<b-a\>|)>>>|)>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    As a consequence,

    <\equation*>
      K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>.
    </equation*>

    <\with|color|black>
      Hence, by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-cumulants> of the cumulant
      norm,

      <\equation*>
        <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<space\>\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>,<around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>,<around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>|)>|\<interleave\>>,>>>>>
      </equation*>

      where the last estimate follows from<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w> and
      <math|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>>
      denotes the function

      <\equation>
        z\<mapsto\><around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|z|)>|\|>
        w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z|)>.<label|eq:A-proof-dot-G-w>
      </equation>

      As a result, using Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-cumulants> one proves
      along the lines of Lemma<nbsp>5.29 in<nbsp><cite|duchFlowEquationApproach2021>
      that

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G<rsup|>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|\|><rsup|><rsub|M><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>
        <around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>|\<interleave\>>=
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G<rsup|>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|\|><rsup|><rsub|M><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>
        <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,
      </equation*>

      where <math|<around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G<rsup|>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|\|><rsup|><rsub|M>>
      denotes the periodisation in space of the
      function<nbsp><eqref|eq:A-proof-dot-G-w> with period <math|M>. Thus,
      since by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:Gdot-decay>

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G<rsup|>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|\|><rsup|><rsub|M><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1-d>,
      </equation*>

      we obtain

      <\equation*>
        <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\>
        \ <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1-d>
        <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
        .
      </equation*>
    </with>

    It follows that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1-d>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-1>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.
    </equation*>

    In the last step, we used<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogenity-cum>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:compatibility>, which imply

    <\equation*>
      -<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>-1-d=-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-1+\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>-d<rsub|>\<geqslant\>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-1.
    </equation*>

    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-B>For all <math|<with|font-series|bold|a>\<in\><with|font-series|bold|\<b-A\>>>
    and <math|i\<leqslant\>n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>> the
    following bound

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,<with|font-series|bold|c>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|c>|]>-1>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>,
    <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>.>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    The proof proceeds along the same lines as the previous one.
    Recalling<nbsp><eqref|eq:specific-operator-B>, we now need to analyse the
    expression

    <\equation*>
      <with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      <around*|<left|(|2>|\<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|1>>,F<rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<rprime|'>+1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      \<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|2>|\|>+1><around*|<left|(|1>|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|2>>|<right|)|1>>|<right|)|2>>.
    </equation*>

    Using <math|L<rsub|\<sigma\>>K<rsub|\<sigma\>>=1> and
    Def.<nbsp><reference|def:regularizing-kernels-for-kernels>, we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>><around*|<left|(|3>|<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      <around*|<left|(|2>|\<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|1>>,F<rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<rprime|'>+1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>
      \<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|2>|\|>+1><around*|<left|(|1>|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|2>>|<right|)|1>>|<right|)|2>>|<right|)|3>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|=<with|font|cal|<with|font|Euler|C>><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|<left|(|3>||<right|\<nobracket\>|3>><around*|[|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1,k<rsub|1>>\<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|1>>,F<rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-1-\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<rprime|'>+1|)>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|4em><around*|<left|\<nobracket\>|2>|<around*|[|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|\||I<rsub|2>|\|>+1,k<rsub|2>>\<frak-K\><rsub|<around*|\||I<rsub|1>|\|>+1><around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|(|\<ell\><rprime|'>,k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>|)>>,<around*|(|F<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>>|)><rsub|j\<in\>I<rsub|2>>|)>|]>|<right|)|2>>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    where <math|k<rsub|1>=<big|sum><rsub|j=1><rsup|i-1>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>|)>+k<rprime|'>+1>
    and <math|k<rsub|2>=<big|sum><rsub|j=i+1><rsup|n<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|a>|)>>k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|j>|)>+k<around*|(|\<frak-a\><rsub|i>|)>-k<rprime|'>>.
    As a consequence,

    <\equation*>
      K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>=\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Hence, by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-cumulants> of the cumulant norm,

    <\equation*>
      <with|color|black|<tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<around*|[|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|]>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<space\>\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>,<around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>,<around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>|)>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|a>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>>,<around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>,<around*|\||K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\|>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>|)>|\<interleave\>>,>>>>>>
    </equation*>

    where the last estimate follows from<nbsp><eqref|eq:weight-w>. As a
    result, by Def.<nbsp><reference|def:norm-cumulants> and
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>, we have

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|b>>|\<interleave\>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|K<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cdot\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<with|font-series|bold|c>>|\<interleave\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1><around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Consequently, we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,\<b-c\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-1>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|c>|]>-1>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    In the last step we used<nbsp><eqref|eq:homogenity-cum>
    and<nbsp><eqref|eq:compatibility>, which imply

    <\equation*>
      -<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|a>|]>+2s-1=-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|c>|]>-\<varrho\>+\<theta\>+\<beta\>-\<delta\>+2s-1\<geqslant\>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|b>|]>-<around*|[|<with|font-series|bold|c>|]>-1.
    </equation*>

    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

  <\remark>
    <label|rem:A-B-epsilon-bounds>Note that
    Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:Gdot-decay> implies that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<\|\|\>|<around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G<rsup|>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|)>|\|><rsup|><rsub|M><rsup|>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-1-d>,<space|2em><around*|\<\|\|\>|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>+2s-1>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|<around*|\||L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G<rsup|>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|>|\|><rsup|><rsub|M>>
    denotes the periodisation in space of the function
    <math|z\<mapsto\><around*|\||<around*|(|L<rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><around*|(|z|)>|\|>
    > with period <math|M>. Using the above bounds one shows, along the lines
    of the proofs of Lemmas<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-A>
    and<nbsp><reference|lem:estimates-B>, that\ 

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-A\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>+2s-1>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|K<rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<cal-B\><rsup|\<b-a\>,<around*|(|i|)>><rsub|\<b-b\>,<with|font-series|bold|c>><around*|(|<wide|G|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>,\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<varepsilon\><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>+2s-1>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-b\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|\<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-c\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    These bounds are used to prove the estimate<nbsp><eqref|eq:expected-epsilon>.
    Note that the norms appearing on the left-hand sides of the above bounds,
    as well as the norm in<nbsp><eqref|eq:expected-epsilon>, do not involve
    weights.
  </remark>

  <subsection|Localisation><label|app:localization>

  In this section, we introduce the Taylor expansion on the (semi)-discrete
  lattice <math|\<Lambda\>=\<Lambda\><rsub|\<varepsilon\>>>. At first order,
  we have

  <\equation*>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>+<big|sum><rsub|i\<in\><around*|{|0,1\<pm\>,2\<pm\>,\<ldots\>,d\<pm\>|}>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i>
    <around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|i>\<psi\>|)><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>,>>>>>
  </equation*>

  where <math|\<partial\><rsup|0>> denotes the time derivative,

  <\equation*>
    \<partial\><rsup|k\<pm\>>\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>\<assign\>\<pm\>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-1><around*|[|\<psi\><around*|(|z\<pm\>e<rsub|k>|)>-\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>|]>,
  </equation*>

  denote the discrete forward (<math|k+>) and backward (<math|k->)
  derivatives in the <math|k>-th spatial direction and for
  <math|h\<in\>\<Lambda\>> the function <math|\<rho\><rsub|h>:<around*|[|0,1|]>\<rightarrow\>\<Lambda\>>
  is a bounded variation path such that <math|\<rho\><rsub|h><around*|(|0|)>=0>
  and <math|\<rho\><rsub|h><around*|(|1|)>=h>. We use the notation
  <math|<around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|0>\<assign\>\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)>>
  and <math|<around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|k\<pm\>>\<assign\><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|k><around*|(|t|)>|)><rsub|\<pm\>>>,
  where <math|<around*|(|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|k><around*|(|t|)>|)><rsub|\<pm\>>>
  denote the positive and negative parts of the signed measure
  <math|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|k><around*|(|t|)>>. Note that
  the path <math|\<rho\><rsub|h>> is piecewise constant in space, so that the
  signed measure <math|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|h><rsup|i>> is well defined and
  given by a sum of delta functions multiplied by the corresponding
  increments. We choose it so that its total mass is bounded by
  <math|<around*|\||h|\|><rsub|>> and

  <\equation*>
    <big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|h><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|k\<pm\>>=<around*|[|h|]><rsup|k\<pm\>>\<assign\>h<rsup|k>
    \<bbb-1\><rsub|\<pm\>h<rsup|k>\<geqslant\>0>.
  </equation*>

  <\remark>
    Note that in the continuum we could choose

    <\equation*>
      \<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>= <around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)> t.
    </equation*>

    Moreover, since in the continuum both the right and left derivatives
    <math|\<partial\><rsup|k\<pm\>>> coincide with
    <math|\<partial\><rsup|k>>, we have

    <\equation*>
      \<psi\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>=\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>+<big|sum><rsub|k\<in\><around*|{|0,\<ldots\>,d|}>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1><around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|k>\<psi\>|)><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>
      <around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><rsup|k> \<mathd\>t.
    </equation*>
  </remark>

  \;

  Since we intend to use the second-order Taylor expansion, it is convenient
  to choose the path such that <math|\<rho\><rsup|0><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>=0>
  for <math|u\<in\><around*|[|0,1/2|]>> and

  <\equation*>
    \<rho\><rsup|i><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>=<with|color|black|\<rho\><rsup|i><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|1/2|)>+>1<rsub|i=0>
    <around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><rsup|0><rsub|> <around*|(|2u-1|)>
  </equation*>

  for <math|u\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|]>>. This allows to avoid second order
  terms with one derivative in time and one in space. Note also that\ 

  <\equation*>
    <big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1/2><around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|\|>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1/2><around*|\||<around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|]><rsup|j>|\|>\<leqslant\><around*|\||<wide|z|\<bar\>><rsub|1>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsub|>,<space|2em><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)><rsup|>|\|>\<leqslant\>
    <big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|\||<around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|]><rsup|0>|\|>\<leqslant\><around*|\||<around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)><rsub|0>-z<rsub|0>|\|><rsup|>.
  </equation*>

  We have

  <\eqnarray*>
    <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>+<big|sum><rsub|i><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i>
    \<partial\><rsup|i>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>+<big|sum><rsub|i\<neq\>0><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1/2><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i>
    \<partial\><rsup|i>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>+<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1>
    \<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)>
    \<partial\><rsup|0>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>.>>>>
  </eqnarray*>

  Expanding once more the spatial derivatives, we have

  <\eqnarray*>
    <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>+<big|sum><rsub|i\<neq\>0>\<partial\><rsup|i>\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>
    <around*|[|z<rsub|1>-z|]><rsup|i>+<big|sum><rsub|i,j\<neq\>0,><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1/2><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|]><rsup|j>
    \<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|)>+>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|
    +<big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1>\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)>
    \<partial\><rsup|0>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>.>>>>
  </eqnarray*>

  As a consequence, for a generic kernel <math|V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>,
  and symmetrising the factor <math|\<partial\><rsup|i>\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>>
  using the relation <math|\<partial\><rsup|i->\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>-\<partial\><rsup|i+>\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>=\<varepsilon\><around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|i+>\<partial\><rsup|i->\<psi\>|)><around*|(|z|)>>
  we obtain

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|V<around*|(|\<psi\>|)><around*|(|z|)>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>\<psi\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|\<psi\><around*|(|z|)><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>+<big|sum><rsub|k\<neq\>0><frac|\<partial\><rsup|k+><rsub|>\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>+\<partial\><rsup|k->\<psi\><around*|(|z|)>|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\>z<rsub|1><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><rsup|k>V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|\<space\>+<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\>z<rsub|1><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1>\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)>V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>\<partial\><rsup|0>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|-<big|sum><rsub|k><frac|\<varepsilon\><around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|k+>\<partial\><rsup|k->\<psi\>|)><around*|(|z|)>|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||z<rsub|1>-z|\|><rsup|k>
    V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>\<mathd\>z<rsub|1>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|sum><rsub|i,j\<neq\>0><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\>z<rsub|1><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1/2><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>
    <around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|]><rsup|j><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i>V<around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>\<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>\<psi\><around*|(|z+\<rho\><rsub|z<rsub|1>-z><around*|(|u|)>|)>.<htab|5mm>>>>>><label|eq:Taylor-tested>
  </equation>

  By duality, we can write this Taylor expansion as an operation over the
  kernel <math|V> via the operators <math|<with|font-series|bold|L>> and

  <\equation>
    <with|font-series|bold|R>\<assign\><with|font-series|bold|R><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>>+<big|sum><rsub|i,j\<neq\>0><with|font-series|bold|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>>+<big|sum><rsub|k><with|font-series|bold|R><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|<around*|(|k|)>>,<label|eq:decomposition-of-R>
  </equation>

  of the form

  <\equation>
    <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|L>V|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\><wide|z|~>*V<around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
    \<mathd\><wide|z|~> \<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)>+<big|sum><rsub|i\<neq\>0><frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~>*-z|)><rsup|i>V<around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>*|)>
    \ <around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|i+><rsub|>+\<partial\><rsup|i->|)>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|R><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>>V|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1>\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)>V<around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>\<partial\><rsup|0>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z-\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>
    \<mathd\><wide|z|~>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>>V|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|\<space\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|1/2><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>
    <around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|]><rsup|j><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i>V<around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>\<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z-\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|)>
    \<mathd\><wide|z|~>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|<around*|(|k|)>>V|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>>|<cell|\<assign\>>|<cell|-<frac|\<varepsilon\>|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>
    <around*|\||<wide|z|~>-z|\|><rsup|k> V<around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
    \<mathd\><wide|z|~> <around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|k+><rsub|>\<partial\><rsup|k->|)>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)>.>>>>><label|eq:L-R-operators>
  </equation>

  When tested with a smooth function this gives the identity\ 

  <\equation*>
    V<around*|(|\<psi\>|)>=<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|L>V|)><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>+<around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|R>V|)><around*|(|\<psi\>|)>,
  </equation*>

  as seen in<nbsp><eqref|eq:Taylor-tested>. We use this expansion for the
  analysis of relevant cumulants, namely

  <\equation*>
    \<cal-F\><rsup|\<b-a\>><rsub|\<mu\>>=<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>=\<bbb-E\>F<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>,<space|2em>\<ell\>\<in\><around*|{|1,\<ldots\>,<wide|\<ell\>|^>|}>.
  </equation*>

  Recall that we have the following decomposition<nbsp><eqref|eq:flow-decomposition>,

  <\eqnarray*>
    <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|<around*|(|1-K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>>|)><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>-<big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|-<with|font-series|bold|L><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>-<with|font-series|bold|L><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<mathd\>\<sigma\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|-<math-bf|R><big|int><rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|1><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>
    \<mathd\>\<sigma\>,>>>>
  </eqnarray*>

  where <math|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>\<assign\>\<partial\><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|F|\<bar\>><rsub|1><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>>.

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-local>The following bounds hold uniformly in
    <math|\<sigma\>,\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>>.

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<cwith|2|2|1|1|cell-halign|r>|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><with|font-series|bold|><rsub|\<sigma\>>,>>|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><with|font-series|bold|><rsub|\<sigma\>>.>>>>>
    </equation*>
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    As we arged in Remark<nbsp><reference|rem:symmetries> the cumulants are
    invariant under spatial reflections. As a result, we conclude that

    \;

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|i+><rsub|>+\<partial\><rsup|i->|)>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>\<mathd\><wide|z|~>*<around*|(|<wide|z|~>*-z|)><rsup|i><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)><with|color|black|=0>.
    </equation*>

    Hence, the following identity

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>
    </equation*>

    holds true. Similarly,

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      <around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.
    </equation*>

    In order to prove the first of the bounds stated in the lemma, we observe
    that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.
    </equation*>

    Thus, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<mu\>><with|font-series|bold|L><around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>
      K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.
    </equation*>

    and

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)>|\|>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>
      \<mathd\>z<rsub|1><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>\<mathd\><wide|z|~>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<\|\|\>|K<rsub|\<mu\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|TV<around*|(|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>>|)>>
      \ sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>,>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:bounds-K-J>. Since

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>\<lesssim\>sup<rsub|z><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>=<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><with|font-series|bold|><rsub|\<sigma\>>,
    </equation*>

    this proves the first of the bounds stated in the lemma. By a similar
    argument, we get

    \;

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>
      <around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.
    </equation*>

    Consequently, by Lemma<nbsp><reference|lem:weight-interaction>, we obtain

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|L><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<\|\|\>|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|1-h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>
      <around*|(|w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>>|)><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|\<infty\>>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><with|font-series|bold|><rsub|\<sigma\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.
    </equation*>

    This proves the second of the bounds stated in the lemma.
  </proof>

  <\lemma>
    <label|lem:estimates-remainder>The following bound\ 

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
    </equation*>

    holds uniformly in <math|\<mu\>\<in\><around*|[|1/2,1|)>,\<sigma\>\<in\><around*|[|\<mu\>,1|)>>.
  </lemma>

  <\proof>
    By applying the triangular inequality
    to<nbsp><eqref|eq:decomposition-of-R>, we arrive at

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<with|font-series|bold|R><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|sum><rsub|i,j\<neq\>0><around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|+<big|sum><rsub|k><around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    We have

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=>>|<row|<cell|<application-space|2em>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|<frac|1|2>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|]><rsup|j><around*|[|\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|]><rsup|i>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)><around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z-\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Thus,\ 

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<math|<around*|\||w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>>>>|<row|<cell|\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|<frac|1|2>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|\|>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|\|>
      w<rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      <around*|\||K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>*<around*|\||
      \<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z-\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Recall that

    <\equation*>
      w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|<around*|(|2|)>,\<flat\>><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>=<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-z<rsub|1>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>.
    </equation*>

    Introduce the point <math|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>\<assign\>z+\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>>
    and note that

    <\equation*>
      w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>\<lesssim\>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>|)>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>-z<rsub|1>|)>\<leqslant\>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>-z<rsub|1>|)>.
    </equation*>

    The second inequality above follows from

    <\equation*>
      w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>|)>\<lesssim\>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>,
    </equation*>

    which holds because, by construction, <math|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>>
    lies on the path connecting <math|z> and <math|<wide|z|~>>. Overall, this
    yields

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<around*|\||w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>|\|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|1em>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|<frac|1|2>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|\|><around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|\|>
      w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      <around*|(|<with|color|black|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>>|)><rsup|-1>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|<space|2em>\<times\>w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>
      <around*|\||<around*|(|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|\|>*w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>-z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|\|| \<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    As a consequence, we obtain

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|z,<wide|z|~>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|<frac|1|2>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|\|>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|\|>
      w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)><around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>|)><rsup|-1>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|\<times\><around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      sup<rsub|z,<wide|z|~>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>
      w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>-z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|\|| \<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\>z<rsub|1>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Using

    <\equation>
      <big|int><rsub|0><rsup|<frac|1|2>><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|u|)>|\|>
      <around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsup|><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|\|>\<lesssim\><around*|\||<wide|<wide|z|~>|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsup|2>,<label|eq:bounded-total-mass>
    </equation>

    and

    <\equation>
      <big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><rsub|>w<rsup|\<flat\>><rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|>|)><around*|\||
      \<partial\><rsup|i>\<partial\><rsup|j>K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\>z\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2>,<label|eq:bound-for-deriv-of-K>
    </equation>

    as well as

    \;

    <\equation>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<frac|<around*|\||<wide|<wide|z|~>|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|><rsup|2>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>><frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|2-\<flat\>|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2>|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2-\<flat\>>|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>>,>>>>><label|eq:absorbing-monomials>
    </equation>

    we conclude that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|i,j|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.
    </equation*>

    Next, note that

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=<big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1>\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)><around*|(|h<rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<partial\><rsup|0>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z-\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><around*|(|t|)>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~>.
    </equation*>

    Proceeding as above we get

    \;

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|sup<rsub|z,<wide|z|~>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1><around*|\||\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><rsup|><around*|(|t|)>|\|>
      \ w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)><around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>|)><rsup|-1>\<times\>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|\<times\><around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      sup<rsub|z,<wide|z|~>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>-z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|\|| \<partial\><rsup|0>K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-<wide|z|~><around*|(|z,u|)>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\>z<rsub|1>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Using

    <\equation*>
      <big|int><rsub|1/2><rsup|1>\<mathd\>\<rho\><rsub|<wide|z|~>-z><rsup|0><around*|(|t|)>\<leqslant\><around*|\||<wide|z|~><rsub|0>-z<rsub|0>|\|>,
    </equation*>

    and

    <\equation*>
      <big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><rsub|>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z<rsub|>-z<rprime|'>|)>
      <around*|\||\<partial\><rsup|0>K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z-z<rprime|'><rsub|>|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\>z\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2s>,
    </equation*>

    as well as

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\||<wide|z|~><rsub|0>-z<rsub|0>|\|><frac|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>|w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>>h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>><frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-<around*|(|2s-\<flat\>|)>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|2s>|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s><rsup|><rsup|>|)><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|>|)><rsub|s><rsup|2s-\<flat\>>|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><frac|1|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2-2s><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2s-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    we arrive at

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsup|<around*|(|0|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>>
      \ <around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>
      .
    </equation*>

    Finally, we discuss the term

    <\equation*>
      <around*|(|<math-bf|R><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|)><around*|(|z,z<rsub|1>|)>=<frac|\<varepsilon\>|2><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|\||<wide|z|~>-z|\|><rsup|k><around*|(|h<rsub|\<mu\>>K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|)><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      \<mathd\><wide|z|~> <around*|(|\<partial\><rsup|k+><rsub|>\<partial\><rsup|k->|)>\<delta\><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)>
      .
    </equation*>

    Also in this case the proof follows the same lines. We obtain

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|\<varepsilon\>
      *sup<rsub|z,<wide|z|~>\<in\>\<Lambda\>><around*|\||<wide|<wide|z|~>|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|2><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>
      h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>
      <around*|(|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>|)><rsup|-1>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|>|<cell|\<times\><around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-z<rsub|1>|)>
      <around*|\|| \<partial\><rsup|k+><rsub|>\<partial\><rsup|k->K<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z<rsub|1>-z|)>|\|>
      \<mathd\>z<rsub|1>.>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Note that

    <\equation*>
      <tabular|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<frac|<around*|\||<wide|<wide|z|~>|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>
      h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>>>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><frac|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>>><frac|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||<wide|z|~>-z|\|><rsub|s>|<around*|(|1+<around*|(|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2>|)><rsup|><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><frac|1|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||<wide|z|~>-z|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<flat\>-1>><frac|1|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1><around*|\||z-<wide|z|~>|\|><rsub|s>|)><rsup|2-\<flat\>><rsup|>>,>>>>>
    </equation*>

    Since <math|<around*|\||<wide|<wide|z|~>|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|>>\<neq\>0
    implies <math|<around*|\||<wide|z|~>-z|\|><rsub|s>\<geqslant\>\<varepsilon\>>
    we have

    <\eqnarray*>
      <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|<frac|<around*|\||<wide|<wide|z|~>|\<bar\>>-<wide|z|\<bar\>>|\|>w<rsub|\<mu\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>
      h<rsub|\<mu\>><around*|(|z,<wide|z|~>|)>|w<rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|(|z-<wide|z|~>|)>>>|<cell|\<lesssim\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><frac|1|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>/\<varepsilon\>|)><rsup|\<flat\>-1>><frac|1|<around*|(|1+<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-1>/\<varepsilon\>|)><rsup|2-\<flat\>><rsup|>>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|\<leqslant\>>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>>
      <around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>-1>\<varepsilon\><rsup|1-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2-\<flat\>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|\<flat\>-2><rsup|>>>|<row|<cell|>|<cell|=>|<cell|<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2-\<flat\>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-1>.>>>>
    </eqnarray*>

    Hence, using again<nbsp><eqref|eq:bound-for-deriv-of-K> with <math|i=k+>
    and <math|j=k-> we get

    <\equation*>
      <around*|\<interleave\>|<math-bf|R><rsub|\<varepsilon\>><rsup|<around*|(|k|)>><around*|(|<around*|[|K<rsup|1,1><rsub|\<sigma\>><wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|]>\<cdot\>h<rsub|\<mu\>>|)>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<mu\>>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-2><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|2-\<flat\>>\<varepsilon\><rsup|-1>*<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>=<around*|\<llbracket\>|\<mu\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|-\<flat\>><around*|\<llbracket\>|\<sigma\>|\<rrbracket\>><rsup|\<flat\>>*<around*|\<interleave\>|<wide|<wide|F|\<bar\>>|\<dot\>><rsub|\<sigma\>><rsup|<around*|[|\<ell\>|]>,<around*|(|1|)>>|\<interleave\>><rsub|\<sigma\>>.
    </equation*>

    This finishes the proof.
  </proof>

