      <\db-entry|+8S8UKPGNtN|article|duchStochasticQuantizationTwoDimensional2024>
        <db-field|contributor|mgubi>

        <db-field|modus|manual>

        <db-field|newer|+8S8UKPGNtM>

        <db-field|date|1760088049>
      <|db-entry>
        <db-field|author|Paweª <name|Duch><name-sep>Wojciech
        <name|Dybalski><name-sep>Azam <name|Jahandideh>>

        <db-field|title|Stochastic quantization of two-dimensional <math|P<around*|(|\<Phi\>|)>> quantum field theory>

        <db-field|journal|Annales Henri Poincaré>

        <db-field|year|2025>

        <db-field|issn|1424-0637, 1424-0661>

        <db-field|doi|10.1007/s00023-024-01447-w>

        <db-field|urldate|2025-10-10>

        <db-field|abstract|Abstract We give a simple and self-contained
        construction of the <math|P<around*|(|\<Phi\>|)>> Euclidean quantum
        field theory in the plane and verify the Osterwalder\USchrader
        axioms: translational and rotational invariance, reflection
        positivity and regularity. In the intermediate steps of the
        construction, we study measures on spheres. In order to control the
        infinite volume limit, we use the parabolic stochastic quantization
        equation and the energy method. To prove the translational and
        rotational invariance of the limit measure, we take advantage of the
        fact that the symmetry groups of the plane and the sphere have the
        same dimension.>

        <db-field|langid|english>

        <db-field|volume|26>

        <db-field|pages|1055\U1086>
      </db-entry>

      <\db-entry|+8S8UKPGNtP|article|duchErgodicityInfiniteVolume2025>
        <db-field|contributor|mgubi>

        <db-field|modus|manual>

        <db-field|newer|+8S8UKPGNtO>

        <db-field|date|1760088259>
      <|db-entry>
        <db-field|author|Paweª <name|Duch><name-sep>Martin
        <name|Hairer><name-sep>Jaeyun <name|Yi><name-sep>Wenhao <name|Zhao>>

        <db-field|title|Ergodicity of infinite volume
        <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> at high temperature>

        <db-field|year|2025>

        <db-field|number|arXiv:2508.07776>

        <db-field|eprint|2508.07776>

        <db-field|primaryclass|math>

        <db-field|publisher|arXiv>

        <db-field|doi|10.48550/arXiv.2508.07776>

        <db-field|urldate|2025-10-10>

        <db-field|abstract|We consider the infinite volume
        <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> dynamic and show that it is globally
        well-posed in a suitable weighted Besov space of distributions. At
        high temperatures / small coupling, we furthermore show that the
        difference between any two solutions driven by the same realisation
        of the noise converges to zero exponentially fast. This allows us to
        characterise the infinite-volume <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>
        measure at high temperature as the unique invariant measure of the
        dynamic, and to prove that it satisfies all Osterwalder\USchrader
        axioms, including invariance under translations, rotations, and
        reflections, as well as exponential decay of correlations.>

        <db-field|archiveprefix|arXiv>

        <db-field|keywords|Mathematical Physics,Mathematics - Analysis of
        PDEs,Mathematics - Mathematical Physics,Mathematics - Probability>

        <db-field|journal|arXiv preprint arXiv:2508.07776>
      </db-entry>

